According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, during the 222 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to December 8, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and A total of 231,192 vehicles were fined, including 170,329 motorcycles and 60,863 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorcycles are mostly helmet overcrowding, no license plate, cell phone use and drunkenness. The offenses for cars are mostly speeding, drunken driving, drunk driving licenses, no belts and cell phone use.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 222 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for December 8, 2020, traffic accidents across Cambodia also occurred 3 times, in which 3 people died and 0 people were injured (0 seriously injured).
