Pursat Provincial Department of Environment Rejects Post That Parks Officers Involved in Buffalo Theft and Thigh Breaking in Phnom Kravanh District
(Pursat): The Pursat Provincial Department of Environment on December 8, 2020, denied that the Ministry of Environment's rangers at the Phnom Oral Wildlife Sanctuary in Pursat Province were involved in the theft of buffaloes, people and twins. Take the thigh in Sanle commune, Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province recently.
The Pursat Provincial Department of Environment emphasized that "the above publication has no clear basis and is slanderous, provocative and affects the honor of the park rangers and the Pursat Provincial Department of Environment."
The next day, October 2, 2020, he went to the Cardamom Market to buy a new phone and reported to Mr. Kim Sok Pich, Deputy Director of Phnom Oral Wildlife Sanctuary, about the lost phone at Phnom Kay on the 4th of May. October 2020 at 9:20 am by telegram and asked Mr. Kim Sok Pich to add a new phone number to the Telegram Working Group of Phnom Oral Wildlife Sanctuary.
On December 4, 2020, at 10:30 AM, Mr. Phuong Sinoeun asked Mr. Kim Sok Pich for permission through the telegram system to attend the inauguration party of Mr. Chinnith's Organic Fertilizer Company in Koul Toteung Village, Santrey Commune. Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province, and sang in the program with many witnesses. The Krakor District Police Inspectorate is also investigating the allegations.
In relation to the above case, the Pursat Provincial Department of Environment would like to completely reject the publication of the above two accounts and ask the public to be informed.
