In connection with this case, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, issued an order temporarily suspending the entry of civil servants working in the premises of the Ministry of Interior until further notice. This is according to the order received by Fresh News on December 7.
This regulation is made to follow the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, and in consultation with the Ministry of Health to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 to the leadership of civil servants, national police officers and prison officials who Serves on the premises of the Ministry of Interior as well as community outreach.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng decided to issue the following regulations:
1: Suspension of entry and exit to work temporarily in the premises of the Ministry of Interior for civil servants, national police officers and prison officials in the General Departments and units located within the premises of the Ministry of Interior from the 7th This December 2020 until further notice.
2. The leaders of civil servants, national police officers and prison officials working in general-departments or units located in the premises of the Ministry of Interior who have not been sampled to diagnose Kovid 19 virus must hurry. Get a sample on December 7, 2020 at the Ministry of Interior.
4. In order to ensure the sustainability of the work of the Ministry of Interior, the leaders of civil servants, national police officers and prison officials working in the premises of the Ministry of Interior must work remotely online.
5: The General Secretariat of the Ministry of Interior shall collect the entry-exit card issued by the Ministry of Interior in accordance with Instruction No. 053 dated December 3, 2020 and prepare a new entry-exit card to be provided to However, the leaders and officials assigned to the Ministry of Interior as defined in point 4 above. The United States has set itself up as a "beacon of human rights", ready to accept Hong Kong residents as temporary residents.
