Spokesman for the General Commission: On December 7, another 332 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, during the 221 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to December 7, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and A total of 230,761 vehicles were fined, including 170,048 motorcycles and 60,713 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorcycles are mostly helmetless, unlicensed and drunk. The offenses for cars are mostly speeding, drunken driving, drunk driving licenses, no seat belts and cell phone use.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 221 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
