(Phnom Penh): Non-profit international NGOs have signed a memorandum of understanding with the Cambodian private sector to improve local agricultural products and food security in Pursat province. The signing ceremony took place on December 7, 2020.
Adra Cambodia is an international non-profit organization and part of a network of international aid and development agencies in 120 countries around the world. Davan, on the other hand, is a private company that specializes in the agricultural production chain and the food safety market.
"For the common purpose of promoting domestic agricultural products and food safety, Davan and Adra Cambodia have agreed on cooperation through the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding," the statement said. Which lasts for 3 years. "This Memorandum of Understanding is effective from the date of this signing until December 31, 2020."
Through grassroots programs, Adra Community seeks to establish full support for the well-being of its people, all of which requires the organization and implementation of sustainable, community-led projects that support the Sustainable Development Goals. In that, Adra included a number of goals, such as zero hunger, strong health and well-being, and the goal of quality education.
Currently, Adra Cambodia, with technical support from the International Entrepreneurship Development Program (IDD), is supporting farmers in five districts in the entire Pursat province under the project "Promoting Market Production Chain through Sustainable Production" called Promark Market. 5 years until December 2023. This project aims to improve the value chain of fruit and vegetable products by working with smallholder farmers in Pursat province.
Mr. Chheng Makara added: "We hope to have more partners like Tuesday Adra Cambodia to promote local products and strive to produce food safety."
