The object of the complaint is to request the prosecutor to make three charges, including:
* Public defamation * Public insult * Incitement to commit a crime, for example.
The offense took place during November 2020 on telecommunication and audio-visual systems, along with misleading messages leading to a loss of confidence in the NEC as well as the election.
Mr. Som Soreida, Deputy Secretary General of the NEC and Representative of the NEC in this case, stated that the Criminal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia also defines the boundaries of this right not to exercise its rights. Affects other individuals and society, including:
* Affects individuals, including infringement of image rights, housing rights, and other defamatory acts that infringe on the dignity of individuals, including individuals and legal entities.
* Harm to society, such as the exercise of rights, leads to serious damage to public order or incitement that leads to loss of national security.
