The Ministry of Education has introduced four guidelines for educational institutions to participate in the prevention and control of the spread of Kovid 19 disease at the community event on November 28 (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on December 7, 2020. Introduced four guidelines to be sent to educational institutions to participate in the prevention and control of the spread of Kovid 19 at the November 28 community event.
According to a letter from the Ministry of Education, received by Fresh News on December 7, in order to prevent and curb the spread of Kovid 19 at the Nov. 28 community event, the ministry would like to introduce administrative measures and health safety measures in Performing the following tasks:
1: All units must instruct subordinate educators to perform remote or online work when it is not necessary to come to the unit. Educators must be on the lookout for updates on the status of community events November 28 and must not travel to high-risk areas.
2. In case of need to come to the unit, the education staff must ensure that they are in good health and must strictly implement health safety measures by wearing protective masks regularly, washing their hands and maintaining the safety gap between individuals and society.
3. Each unit must take measures to improve health safety in the unit, such as measuring the temperature of staff, taking measures to maintain hygiene in the unit and must consider delaying or postponing the implementation of programs or meetings.
If it is not possible to postpone or postpone, apply in small format or online.
4: All requests for advice, transmission of documents and decisions from the management must be done online (telegram group).
