Understand the law: the power of the boss
Therefore, the legal awareness program of FRESH NEWS, in collaboration with the Cambodian Bar Association for International Cooperation, would like to raise the topic of "parental power" to the following students:
According to Article 1034 of the Civil Code, "parental authority refers to the person who has the rights and obligations to take care of the minor's body and control the child's property." Out of the relationship between parents and children, parents have the duty to raise, care for and control their children. Not only that, the law also divides the limits of parental authority, which are as follows:
1 * Determining parental authority in the case of married parents: In the case of married parents, the parents must exercise parental authority in collaboration with the minor child. In cases where one parent is unable to exercise parental authority because the parent is unconscious or unable to communicate, the other parent can exercise parental authority.
3 * Determining parental authority in the case of a divorced parent: When the parents are divorced, the parents usually live separately, so the child must live with one of the parents. Post-divorce parental authority can be divided into two: single parental authority, which gives one or both parents, and joint parental authority, in which the father and mother continue to have joint parental authority.
4 * Determining parental authority in the case of unmarried parents: In the case of unmarried parents, only the mother has parental authority, according to the Civil Code. However, if the father recognizes the child and wants to have parental authority over the minor child, the father must have a discussion with the mother, and if there is no parental consent in the discussion, the father can Requires the court to determine who has the authority.
In short, parental authority is the legal bond between parents and minors, which binds the rights and obligations of parents to minors in the education, upbringing, care and supervision of children. However, in some cases, the parents have abused their parental authority or in the case of protecting the interests of their children, the parental authority may be suspended or revoked.
