The glorious past of the Khmer of the Angkorian period is buried in the magazine "Preah Nokor"
(Siem Reap): After years of research in the Angkor Park area and recording, the APSARA Authority has published a new magazine called "Preah Nokor" as most of the articles From the former capital of Yasodharapura, eels bring readers' attention to the famous Khmer Angkorian era.
All articles in this Kingdom Magazine are written by national and international researchers. There are also a variety of topics, such as general considerations on the development of Angkor, technical articles such as detailed maps of archeological sites, based on the latest data from Lydar Technology (LiDAR), a study of the composition of ancient Khmer rocks. Build a temple and a bronze workshop at Angkor Thom.
There are also technical articles related to maintenance as well as repairs, such as the maintenance of sandstone and mortar sculptures, not to be degraded through many years of experience in Angkor, repair of brick structures. Some articles also inform the reader about the various artifacts that the APSARA Authority has found in various places and prepare and record the inventory.
Anthropological texts also mention rice-related festivals celebrated by locals in their archeological sites. In the field of irrigation, there are studies on the Angkor area and related to the temple of Preah Vihear.
APSARA Authority hopes that this magazine will be a source of new knowledge for all Cambodian children who want to learn about Angkor. Therefore, you can come to this Kingdom Magazine at the APSARA Authority Library to get information about the past and the current situation of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
