According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, during the 217 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to December 3, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and A total of 229,173 vehicles were fined, including 169,152 motorcycles and 60,021 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorbikes are mostly without helmets, offenses, without license plates, overtaking, getting drunk and using mobile phones. The offenses for cars are mostly speeding, drunken driving, drunk driving licenses, no belts and cell phone use.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 217 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for December 3, 2020, traffic accidents across Cambodia also occurred 18 times, in which 9 people died and 18 people were injured (11 seriously injured).
