Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has always taken care of the strong will and high commitment to promote the rights of people with disabilities. At the same time, Samdech Techo encouraged the people together to continue to improve the welfare of people with disabilities for the benefit of the disability sector in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also requested all relevant local authorities to strengthen coordination mechanisms to prevent discrimination and insults on people with disabilities. "I want to think about the type of business and business that is suitable for people with disabilities, meet the needs of the market to ensure the sustainability of business and business and increase awareness of opportunities for entrepreneurship to start a business and start your own business."
On the occasion of the celebration of the Day of Persons with Disabilities, Samdech Techo Hun Sen made eight recommendations for the relevant authorities to implement to ensure the protection and promotion of the rights of persons with disabilities. The eight recommendations include:
First, all ministries, institutions and competent authorities at all levels must implement the National Strategic Plan on Disability 2019-2023 effectively and efficiently by preparing annual action plans and budgets by sector of each ministry, institution and unit.
Second, all ministries, institutions and competent authorities at all levels must continue to disseminate measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 in accordance with the guidelines of the Ministry of Health and provide all possible opportunities for people with disabilities to receive information on prevention. And prevent Kovid-19 disease.
Thirdly, all people with disabilities should follow the health rules by keeping a safe distance, wearing a mask, washing their hands with alcohol, soap, or sticking to public places and in the community.
Fourth, all ministries and state institutions must encourage people with disabilities who have the qualifications and ability to fulfill their responsibilities in their positions to have the right to work without discrimination, including working as civil servants, workers, employees and children. Carpenter or trainee.
Fifth, the participation of the private sector, civil society, factories, enterprises and institutions must be carried out responsibly and by raising the obligation to recruit people with disabilities to continue working as others. It is stated in the Law on the Protection and Promotion of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities.
Sixth, the Council for Disability Action must promote the implementation of the National Strategic Plan on Disability 2019-2023, the Law on the Protection and Promotion of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities, the implementation of the Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities and other national policies for the welfare of persons with disabilities. All kinds and all levels.
Seventh: Continue to facilitate access to public places for people with disabilities of all kinds, such as parking for people with disabilities, ramps, equipment, door handles, bathrooms for people with disabilities, Put up signs in ministries, institutions, departments, roads, recreation centers, cultural centers, sports venues, entertainment venues, educational institutions, hotels, hospitals, health centers and transportation facilities, etc.
Eighth, the Ministry of Information shall introduce to all public and private radio and television stations, as well as all media outlets, increase the broadcast time, including sign language translation, especially information on epidemics and how to prevent Kovid-19 for humans. The deaf can receive information in a timely manner. RFI suspends broadcasting on Canadia building, temporarily closed by the Ministry of Health after the discovery of Kovid
