Cambodia, Russia examine possibility of free trade agreement
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia and Russia are studying and examining the possibility of establishing a free trade agreement together to further expand their trade volume.
Discussions on the possibility of free trade between Cambodia and Russia were held during a meeting between Mr. Sok Sopheak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce and Mr. Anatoly Borovik, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Russian Federation to Cambodia. Video system on December 1, 2020.
According to the Ministry of Commerce's Facebook page, the talks focused on strengthening bilateral trade and investment cooperation and examining the feasibility study of a future Cambodia-Russia free trade agreement.
According to the Ministry of Commerce, the Russian Ambassador expressed his appreciation to the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia for the effective implementation of anti-Kovid-19 measures, so far no victims in Cambodia have been lost. Life by this virus.
However, the Secretary of State and the Ambassador stressed that the virus has been hindering the use of orders and shipments worldwide and has contributed greatly to trade volume. Bilateral trade between Cambodia and Russia will fall by about 18% in the first 10 months of 2020.
The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce also took this opportunity to highlight the signing of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement (CCFTA) on October 12, 2020 and the negotiation process for trade agreements. Free Cambodia-Republic of Korea (CKFTA), which completed the fourth round in November 2020.
Mr. Sok Sopheak emphasized that in this spirit, Cambodia expressed its intention to study the possibility of establishing a bilateral free trade agreement between Cambodia and Russia as soon as possible.
The Secretary of State requested the Russian side to invite Cambodian businessmen and investors to participate in the upcoming programs of the Russian Chamber of Commerce and Industry to get trade and investment opportunities provided by the Russian Federation and to request the Russian side to provide Kovid-19 vaccine. Cambodia, if the Russian side succeeds in producing this vaccine in the future.
The Ambassador accepted these requests to inform the Russian government and promised to provide information to the Cambodian side soon. The meeting ended in a cordial and fruitful manner, and both sides expressed high optimism on the bilateral cooperation.
