Spokesman for the General Commission: On December 2, another 369 vehicles were inspected and fined
(Phnom Penh): On December 2, 2020, the traffic police throughout Cambodia inspected and fined a total of 369 vehicles, including 217 motorcycles and 152 cars. This was confirmed by Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and spokesman for the National Police.
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, during the 216 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to December 2, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and A total of 228,729 vehicles were fined, including 168,890 motorcycles and 59,839 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorbikes are mostly without helmets, offenses, without license plates, drunkenness and using mobile phones. The offenses for cars are mostly speeding, drunken driving, drunk driving licenses, no seat belts and cell phone use.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kimkhoeun continued that for the past 216 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
