(Phnom Penh): The Asian Vision Institute (AVI) has studied the projects of major Chinese companies in Cambodia and found that these projects are conducive to the sustainable development of the national economy and society in Cambodia. This is according to Dr. Keo Piseth, President of the Center for Sustainable Development Studies of the Asian Vision Institute in a recent video interview with reporters.
Dr. Keo Piseth said that the Asian Vision Institute has studied Chinese companies and six major joint ventures between China and Cambodia in Cambodia: road construction companies, bridges, banks, duty-free goods companies and hydropower companies. Leading company in the field of investment in Cambodia.
The research report, entitled "Sustainable Development of Chinese Enterprises in Cambodia", assumes that Chinese companies' investment contributes to the development of Cambodia by improving livelihoods, improving the economy, protecting the environment, social work and humanitarian work. That has helped Cambodia in the past.
According to Dr., China is one of the largest investors in Cambodia, from 1994 to 2019, the number of Chinese companies invested about one-fifth of the total investment in Cambodia. . After China, investment companies from the Republic of Korea, the United Kingdom, Malaysia, Japan and Vietnam.
Dr. also told the media that during the research, the research team visited the location of the Lower Sesan 2 hydropower company and asked the relevant sources, including the people, the relevant authorities, whether the company has resolved the issues peacefully. And how are the effects?
Dr. Keo Piseth pointed out that after conducting research, the Lower Sesan 2 hydropower company has a clear mechanism for resolving disputes with the people, most of which authorize the study to assess the environmental impact according to the Ministry of Environment. Many have settled negotiations from one stage to another. The people agree with the compensation and are satisfied with the solution provided by the company.
He also stressed that if you look at the big benefits, the construction of dams has really contributed to the benefit of society as a whole, that is, those companies have contributed to economic and social development according to different possibilities and areas. .
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide campaign against illegal drugs for December 2, 2020 showed that law enforcement forces cracked down on 22 cases, including 12 cases of use and 10 cases of trafficking, arresting 53 suspects.
Research Report: Lower Sesan 2 Hydropower Contributes to Maintaining Energy Stability and Boosting Cambodia's Economic Growth
(Phnom Penh): A new report researched by the Asian Vision Institute (AVI) praised the investment of Chinese investors in the construction of Lower Sesan 2 hydropower plant in Stung Treng province, which has created energy stability and contributed to Cambodia's economic growth. Well.
The study was conducted in Beijing, China on November 23, 2020. The report, conducted by the Asian Vision Institute, is divided into four sections: Introduction to Research Methods, Results, and Chinese and Cambodian-Cambodian Joint Venture Enterprises in Cambodia.
Among them, they conducted an important study on the implementation of the Lower Sesan 2 dam project by visiting resettlement sites around the reservoir area of the second Sesan 2 hydropower station. Conversations to compare the income levels of the residents in the resettlement area before and after the relocation related to health infrastructure, education to make inferences.
Mr. Chheang Vannarith, President of the Asian Vision Institute, said that the research report found that Chinese enterprises, especially Chinese state-owned enterprises that have invested in Cambodia, are law-abiding, have good operations and integrate into the country's society. Cambodia is good and active in social responsibility.
Separately, Dr. Keo Piseth pointed out that the research found that the Lower Sesan 2 hydropower company has a clear mechanism to resolve disputes with the people, most of them authorized to study the environmental impact assessment according to the Ministry of Environment. That is, most disputes have been resolved through negotiations from one stage to another. The people agree with the compensation and are satisfied with the solution provided by the company.
Mr. Keo Piseth also stressed that if you look at the big benefits, the construction of dams really contributes to the benefit of society as a whole by maintaining energy stability and meeting the need for electricity to meet. Other requirements as well as industrial processes.
According to the study, the Lower Sesan 2 dam project, while striving to provide clean, safe and reliable energy, also improves climate change, promotes local development and upliftment. People's livelihood, etc. And actively fulfilled social responsibilities.
The report shows that Lower Sesan 2 hydropower companies have complied with laws and regulations in Cambodia, working closely with the government and local people to address the displacement and doing everything possible to protect them. Environment and culture, contributing greatly to the sustainable development of Cambodia.
