Mr. Khuong Sreng thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for the second donation of 1 million masks for distribution to people living in Phnom Penh to prevent Kovid-19
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, this morning, November 2, 2020, thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, for donating the second mass of 1 million masks for distribution. In Phnom Penh to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 after the outbreak of the "Community 28 November".
Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced on Fresh News on the night of December 1, 2020 to the public that Samdech decided to release 2 million more masks, including one million for Phnom Penh and one million for the province. Siem Reap to participate in the immediate use of help to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
Speaking on Fresh News, Mr. Khuong Sreng, on behalf of the Armed Forces, civil servants and all the people of Phnom Penh, expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, for donating 1 million masks. Mass to Phnom Penh Capital Administration for distribution to the people.
Mr. Khuong Sreng considered that this gesture showed the highest level of concern from the top leaders of the nation to the people as Cambodia and the world as a whole are facing the disease of Kovid-19, especially after Cambodia. The outbreak first entered the community, known as the "Community November 28" event.
Please be reminded that the release of 2 million mass (second time) for Phnom Penh 1 million mass and Siem Reap 1 million mass now is an addition to the previous release of 2 million mass once for Phnom Penh.
At the same time, Samdech Krala Hom also advised to pay attention to solving traffic congestion more effectively.
According to Samdech Sar Kheng, the enforcement of the law on land traffic has achieved remarkably good results, with 778 traffic accidents reduced in the first 10 months of 2020, equal to 23%, the number of fatalities has decreased. 288 people, equal to 17% and the number of injured decreased 1207 people, equal to 23% compared to the same period in 2019.
Samdech Sar Kheng praised and appreciated the spirit of caring, fulfilling the noble duties and responsibilities of road traffic police officers, public works and transport officials and relevant authorities in monitoring and enforcing the law on road traffic. Land and legal education have led to positive results.
Samdech Krala Hom said that although the traffic situation seems to be better than before, it is found that road traffic accidents still pose a high risk compared to other social accidents that cause loss of life, injuries, property damage and affect The livelihoods of many victims' families as well.
Therefore, in order to reduce this risk and to promote better road traffic safety, Samdech Sar Kheng has introduced the following measures to prevent and curb the growth of road traffic accidents:
1. The Capital and Provincial Road Safety Sub-Committee shall urge the following measures:
* Improve traffic order by enforcing the law on parking violations, disrespecting traffic lights, signs and unauthorized use of sidewalks. At the same time, care must be taken to solve traffic congestion more effectively.
* Increase the dissemination of education on the law on road traffic.
* Further strengthen the emergency system for road traffic victims in terms of mechanisms, means and communication of information for professional and timely rescue.
* Care must be taken to implement the "Special Area of Road Safety" competition movement as stated in the instruction dated February 15, 2019. In order to promote this movement, the General Secretariat of the National Road Safety Committee shall assign a working group to inspect and initiate a commendation evaluation to the units and individuals who have performed their duties in 2020.
* Must strive to strengthen discipline, morality, virtue and professional conscience, as well as continue to encourage the competent forces to implement the law on road traffic on a regular basis.
