Ministry of Foreign Affairs announces the results of the 23rd ASEAN-EU Foreign Ministers' Meeting
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, on December 1, 2020, attended the 23rd ASEAN-EU Foreign Ministers' Meeting via video.
A press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs stated that the main results of the meeting were as follows:
The meeting noted the progress of cooperation through the implementation of the ASEAN-EU Action Plan (2018-2022).
The meeting also exchanged views on ways and means to enable the two regions to enhance cooperation in tackling common emergencies such as the Kovid-19 outbreak and public health emergencies. Economic recovery after a global pandemic, as well as further strengthening existing partnerships.
The meeting agreed to establish a concrete framework for the ASEAN-EU Free Trade Agreement and look forward to the speedy conclusion of this agreement.
The meeting adopted the ASEAN-EU Foreign Ministers' Joint Declaration on Connectivity and commended the efforts to explore the possibility of synthesizing the "ASEAN Connectivity Master Plan 2025" and the European Strategy on "European Connectivity". And Asia. ” The meeting also agreed to work towards the speedy conclusion of the ASEAN-EU Comprehensive Air Transport Agreement (CATA).
For the economic sector, the Deputy Prime Minister praised the efforts to achieve the ASEAN-EU Free Trade Agreement, which he believes is the key to achieving business and investment potential, which is an important foundation for building ASEAN relations. - The European Union to be even stronger.
He welcomed the upgrading of the ASEAN-EU Dialogue Partnership to the strategic partnership achieved at the meeting, believing that the new achievement would further strengthen friendly relations and mutually beneficial cooperation. Go back and forth in the past.
