AHF, along with governments and civil society organizations from around the world, will hold a series of commemorative events, including live events and social events, to maintain a safe distance to commemorate those who have died of HIV / AIDS and to raise awareness. Publicize the importance of blood tests, prevention and treatment of HIV and to seek support in continuing this important fight.
Efforts to raise enough funds around the world to respond to the global AIDS epidemic still lack up to $ 6 billion of demand each year. 19. Donor governments must be appropriately involved in strengthening HIV prevention efforts and ensuring that everyone has access to life-saving access to essential care and treatment.
According to the latest UNAIDS statistics, 38 million people are living with HIV / AIDS worldwide, and in 2019, 1.7 million people were newly infected with HIV and 690,000 died of HIV / AIDS. . While millions have been treated with life-saving antiretroviral drugs, there will still be millions more who need life-saving treatment.
"AIDS is a global epidemic that we have been fighting for 30 years," he added. This World AIDS Day would like to remind everyone that AIDS is still a crisis across the region and we must all work together to fight it by investing our efforts and resources focused on HIV testing. AIDS Prevention and Treatment.
