Finally! Kavan, the world's loneliest elephant, has been flown from Pakistan to Cambodia via a special flight.
The reception of cavalry to live in the natural forest of Cambodia was presided over by Mr. Neth Pheaktra at the Siem Reap Airport, with the participation of representatives of the Siem Reap and Oddar Meanchey provincial administrations and other professional officials and representatives of wildlife conservation organizations. Cambodia, the recipient of the caravan to take care of and protect.
After receiving a blessing from the monks at Siem Reap International Airport, the caravan was taken to a new 4,350-hectare sanctuary in the Kulen Promtep Wildlife Sanctuary in Oddar Meanchey province, which is protected by the Wildlife Conservation Organization. Cambodia has received permission from the Ministry of Environment to protect and conserve. In that area, there are three elephants from Nhi district brought from Mondulkiri province.
Cavan, a 35-year-old male elephant, was rescued from a Pakistani zoo by a wildlife conservation group through legal action, and Pakistan's Supreme Court has finally decided to release him and release him. Natural forests of Cambodia's wildlife sanctuaries.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Mr. Neth Pheaktra stated that Cambodia is pleased to welcome the Cavalry Elephant. From now on, Cavan elephants will no longer live in isolation. The caravan will live in the wild in the Kulen Promtep Wildlife Sanctuary in Oddar Meanchey province under the auspices of the Ministry of Environment and the Cambodian Wildlife Conservation Organization (CWS).
At the same time, the senior ministry official said that the Kavan elephant is an endangered Asian elephant and that Cambodia has between 400 and 600 Asian elephants living in the protected forest. Nature of Cambodia in Ratanakkiri and Mondulkiri provinces and in the Cardamom Mountains. Cambodia also has more than 70 domestic elephants.
The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment emphasized that with the strict law enforcement measures of the authorities and the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia to protect and conserve in the last 10 years, the level of crime of hunting and killing wild elephants to get ivory and tail to Consumption according to ancient beliefs in Cambodia has dropped dramatically, almost none.
The Secretary of State said that according to estimates, the 10-year action plan for the conservation of Asian wild elephants requires $ 40.5 million, which is expected to come from a combination of sources, including the government's budget. Yes, governments and development partners. Tuol Roka 1 villagers in Meanchey district will no longer face flooding of houses and houses after the drainage system
(Phnom Penh): At the groundbreaking ceremony for the two-lane sewer project on the morning of November 30, 2020, Mr. Pich Keo Mony, Meanchey District Governor, told the people that from the next day, the road flooded and the house flooded will no longer exist. And because two drainage systems are being built on Street 9 in Tuol Roka 1 village, Chak Angre Krom commune, which always floods the road every year by rain, because before the drainage system was small and there is no drainage system.
The district governor confirmed that seeing this consequence to release water in this area, the capital governor dropped the budget to Meanchey district administration to install machinery to build a sewer system immediately to release water to the people on Street 9, Tuol Roka village. .
Mr. Lay Ch, the director of the specialized office, confirmed that the two-lane sewer system, more than 466 meters long, with a diameter of 6 meters, will be built now, connecting from Street 9 to the main sewer system of the commune hall and connecting to the sewer system of Borey Peng Huoth pours into the Boeung Tompun development canal.
At the same time, the district governor instructed the commune chief and the company that before starting the project, you must inform and ask for forgiveness from the people along the construction site, the installation of sewer system, sewer repair, road repair and road construction should not do anything. To affect the people absolutely, if affected anywhere, go down to salute the people for understanding.
The district governor said that the people along the site under construction to check together with professional officials to monitor all activities of the company that has the right to build sewers and roads because of all these achievements. It belongs to all of us, a common thing for long-term use.
While inspecting the sewerage system, Mr. Pich Keo Mony addressed the villagers' suspicions that no money was being taken from the villagers as they had been concerned as the villagers connected the system from their respective homes. Each body.
He said that unless the people rely on contractors to help make or buy materials, the people will have to pay for the labor or sewage according to negotiations.
At the same time, while seeing the authorities installing machinery to build the sewer system, the people living on both sides of Street 9 came out to cheer, each of them expressing their happiness mixed with the sound that our house will not be flooded from now on. It's raining again. Citizens thanked Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh and Khan Administration for taking care of them.
The district governor instructed the commune chief to cooperate with the relevant units such as the Water Supply Authority, the electricity unit and other relevant officials to make sure that the construction site of the sewerage system runs smoothly and is completed as planned for the people. It will be used in the coming rainy season.
