Tbong Khmum Provincial Administrative Unity Force cracks down on illegal fishing and removes more than 300 meters of barricades in Krouch Chhmar district
(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Mao Dung, Director of Provincial Administration, represented Mr. Cheam Chansophoan, Provincial Governor and Chairman of Tbong Khmum Provincial Administrative Unity Command, on November 29, 2020, led a joint force to crack down on illegal fishing in the district. Wedge by dismantling more than 300 meters of barricades, destroying illegal fishing gear and detaining the perpetrators on the spot.
The operation was attended by the Director of the Department of Agriculture, the Governor of Tbong Khmum District, the Deputy Governor of Krouch Chhmar District, 40 provincial commissioners, Tbong Khmum District Inspector and Krouch Chhmar, 20 Provincial Gendarmerie, as well as the Mekong Fisheries Administration Inspectorate and the Fisheries Administration District, a total of 80 people. People.
According to the crackdown report, the results of this operation include:
First, the 50-meter-long canal barrier was removed at Prek Changvar point in Svay Khleang commune, Krouch Chhmar district.
Second: Dismantled the 100-meter-long barrier at Preah Khla Bay in Tuol Snoul commune, Krouch Chhmar district.
Third: Dismantled the barrier at Prey Khmar Bay, Tuol Snoul Commune, 1.20 meters long
Fourth: Dismantled a 35-meter-long canal (Bang Phit) at Prek Srah Angkam in Krouch Chhmar commune, Krouch Chhmar district.
