The five guidelines of the Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces instruct the commanders of all types of specialized troops and directors of institutions under the General Command to strictly implement, including:
* First: Soldiers of all units and institutions under the General Command are not required to be allowed to work at home.
* Second, the army and school bases must manage the force well and consistently implement measures to prevent Kovid-19 disease, such as temperature measurement at all entrances and exits of the unit, disinfection in the meeting room forts. Or the office wears a mask, washes hands with alcohol or soap regularly, maintains social safety gaps and suspends unnecessary gatherings.
* Third: Soldiers involved in the "Community of 28 November" must take samples to check and conduct the most rigorous, in case the soldiers do not perform the proper compulsion will apply the general rules of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
* Fourth: All units and institutions under the General Command must be ready, both professional and intervention forces, to be ready in the event of an order.
Fifth, the Royal Government's working group to help local people to educate and disseminate to the people, migrants, to strictly implement the provocation and to jointly strengthen measures to prevent Kovid-19 under the guidance of the Royal Government and the appeal of the Ministry of Health .
