Kampot provincial governor seeks solution to congestion on rice exports to Vietnam through Ton Horn
(Kampot): Mr. Chiao Tai, Governor of Kampot Province, on November 30, 2020, led officials and relevant authorities to inspect the border area, especially the congestion of rice exports to Vietnam through the Ton Horn bilateral gate in Prek Kris commune. Kampong Trach recently, dealing with traders with confidence and smooth.
The move comes as more than two weeks of rice exports to Vietnam through the upper border have been delayed and traders from far-flung provinces have had to wait for days, affecting business. They.
After inspecting and meeting with the relevant authorities and officials at the Tonle Sap border gate, traders and residents said that there are two main reasons for the congestion and delays in rice exports, including:
* First, due to the spread of Kovid 19 disease in Vietnam, the Vietnamese side enforces preventive measures * and secondly, tightens Vietnam's road traffic law (requires relevant documents and legal weighting of trucks).
The provincial governor also proposed that the provincial administration set up a working group to resolve rice exports and hold a meeting with the Vietnamese side through a video conference to discuss solutions to rice export barriers and mechanisms. There is no cell interface, meaning smooth rice exports.
