Spokesman for the General Commission: On November 30, another 459 vehicles were inspected and fined
(Phnom Penh): On November 30, 2020, traffic police throughout Cambodia inspected and fined a total of 459 vehicles, including 320 motorcycles and 139 cars. This was confirmed by Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and spokesman for the National Police.
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, during the 214 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to November 30, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and A total of 227,720 vehicles were fined, including 168,214 motorcycles and 59,506 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorbikes are mostly without helmets, offenses, without license plates, drunkenness and using mobile phones. The offenses for cars are mostly speeding, drunken driving, drunk driving licenses, no belts and cell phone use.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kimkhoeun continued that for the past 214 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for November 30, 2020, traffic accidents across Cambodia also occurred 10 times, in which 4 people died, 14 people were injured (10 people were seriously injured).
