Residents of Kampong Ror district, Svay Rieng province, complain about the high price of rice harvesters this year and it is difficult to call them to harvest rice again
(Svay Rieng): Residents of Kampong Ror district, Svay Rieng province, are busy harvesting rain-fed rice, and most residents have complained about the high price of this year's rice harvesters and the difficulty of calling for a harvest.
According to the people in Kampong Ror district, their rain-fed rice harvest this year was good, but some of the paddy fields were affected by the floods, causing the ripe rice to fall all over the fields, making it difficult to harvest. It is very difficult to find a harvester because there are not many harvesters now and the owner of the harvester has to pay more.
Citizens have appealed to the local authorities and relevant departments to facilitate the traders who have rice harvesters, please reduce the price appropriately so that people can afford to harvest their rice.
According to Mr. Un Moniroth, Director of the Agriculture Office of Kampong Ror District, the people have harvested 13,610 hectares of light and medium rice this year. For this year, 1 kg of fragrant rice sells for 1,000 riel to 1,050 riel and regular rice for 950 riel per kilogram.
