Ministry of Rural Development Issues Guidance on Participation in Preventing and Preventing the Outbreak of Kovid 19 to Its Leaders and Civil Servants
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Rural Development on November 30, 2020, issued instructions to leaders and civil servants at all levels under the Ministry to participate in the prevention and control of the spread of Kovid 19 disease.
In the context of the outbreak of Kovid-19, there is a "first community outbreak in Cambodia" and in line with the guidelines of the Royal Government and the Ministry of Health, continue to call on people to be extra vigilant to prevent Kovid-19 infection. Rural Development would like to advise the leaders and civil servants at all levels under the Ministry to participate in the implementation of the following guidelines:
1: Take care to protect your personal and family health by wearing a mask and washing your hands often with soap and water or alcohol or do not touch your face with unwashed hands. .
2. It is necessary to maintain the social safety gap and the personal safety gap of more than one and a half meters.
3. All workshops, training courses, outreach sessions and other meetings must strictly abide by the guidelines of the Ministry of Health and must first seek permission from the Minister of Foreign Affairs.
4. The Department of Rural Health Care shall continue to cooperate with relevant institutions, partner organizations and local authorities to disseminate information on the prevention and control of the outbreak of Kovid-19 as directed by the Ministry of Health.
5: Ministry leaders and civil servants who notice that they are involved somewhere in the community event on 28 November, please check the possibility of doing self-examination in accordance with the principles issued by the Ministry of Health and Report immediately to the Ministry.
