(Phnom Penh): On November 29, 2020, the traffic police throughout Cambodia inspected and fined a total of 481 vehicles, including 343 motorcycles and 138 cars. This was confirmed by Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and spokesman for the National Police.
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, during the 213 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to November 29, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and A total of 227,261 vehicles were fined, including 167,894 motorcycles and 59,367 vehicles of all types.
The most notable offenses for motorcycles are not wearing a helmet, overtaking, not having a license plate, being drunk and using a cell phone. The offenses for cars are mostly speeding, drunken driving, drunk driving licenses, no belts and cell phone use.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kimkhoeun continued that for the past 213 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
