Kampot pepper received orders from the Czech Republic and a European company as the cultivated area increased to nearly 300 hectares
On that occasion, the Minister requested and encouraged the relevant ministries, institutions, relevant national and international organizations, as well as development partners and producers of "Kampot pepper" to continue to cooperate and participate more actively in activities to promote "Mech Kampot".
According to Mr. Pan Sosak, the selection and registration of "Kampot pepper" as the first geographical mark in Cambodia took place in 2010. He said that initially there were 118 producers, 12 companies and only 10 hectares of cultivated land, which can only harvest 10 tons.
By 2020, Kampot pepper will have a total of 455 families, 38 companies, and the cultivated area will increase to 290 hectares, with a yield of up to 82.78 tons and export markets to Asian countries. And Europe.
