China's first self-developed nuclear reactor goes live
China's nuclear reactor is a major first step in reducing China's reliance on the West for energy security and other complex technologies.
The Hualong One nuclear reactor has been in operation since Friday, with a capacity of 10,000 kilowatt-hours a year, according to the China National Nuclear Cooperation (CNNC). It is also in line with China's commitment to reduce CO2 emissions to 8.16 billion tons.
Foreign nuclear power plants supplied less than 5 percent of China's total energy consumption in 2019. Hualong One is a new step that will allow China to break the exclusive control of foreign nuclear companies and aim to reduce its carbon emissions to zero by 2060. The Minister of Health sent a team to urgently inspect the case of alcohol poisoning at the funeral of drug addicts in Kampong Chhnang province
(Phnom Penh): Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, on November 28, 2020, sent a working group to cooperate with local authorities to inspect and solve the case of alcohol poisoning in the funeral of drug addicts. In Kampong Chhnang province, 4 people were poisoned and 1 died.
Ms. O Vandin, Secretary of State and spokesperson of the Ministry of Health, confirmed to Fresh News that the Ministry of Health team that visited the case was led by Professor Xia Huang, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, accompanied by Dr. Hok Kim Cheng, Director General. Health Technician and Dr. Ngov Kang, Deputy Inspector General of the Ministry of Health.
She stated that the team required to repeat the night and discussed with the Governor of Kampong Chhnang to stop the sale and distribution of wine immediately.
According to a spokesman for the Ministry of Health, four suspected alcohol poisoning (two females and two males) are currently being treated at Kampong Chhnang Provincial Hospital. She also called on all people not to drink wine produced without proper technology, which causes accidents.
