Spokesman for the General Commission: On November 28, another 872 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, during the 212 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to November 28, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and A total of 226,780 vehicles were fined, including 167,551 motorcycles and 59,229 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorcycles are mostly helmets, overtaking offenses, no license plates, drunkenness and cell phone use. The offenses for cars are mostly speeding, drunken driving, drunk driving licenses, no seat belts and cell phone use.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun continued that for the past 212 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for November 28, 2020, traffic accidents throughout Cambodia also occurred 7 times, in which 4 people died, 10 people were injured (05 people were seriously injured).
