The Senior Minister thanked all the benefactors as well as the Royal Government, the Provincial Working Group for Sangkum Thmey District and the Wat Mon Scholars Association for their financial support in this event. Education Officer: 37 out of 100 target schools successfully implement the standard "School Board and Teacher Qualification Promotion Program"
The School Board and Teachers' Qualification Enhancement Program will be more actively involved in strengthening the education sector in Cambodia and will help teachers, students with in-depth knowledge, clearer professional skills and a stronger life goal.
The School Management Board Qualification Program was established to strengthen self-efficacy and to strengthen leadership and teaching in schools. The Teacher Qualification Program is trained by the Faculty of Education, the Faculty of Science and the Faculty of Sociology and Humanities of the Royal University of Phnom Penh. As for the program to improve the qualifications of the school management, it is trained by the Faculty of Education of the Royal University of Phnom Penh.
According to Dr., the first generation of students consisted of 160 students from the management of 100 secondary and high schools who worked hard to complete all the subjects in the detailed curriculum and had to defend their graduation report. Before getting a Bachelor of Education Management from Royal University of Phnom Penh.
Academic Outcomes After completing the training in this educational program, students will be qualified
Bachelor's degree with the following qualifications:
* Demonstrates a systematic knowledge of leadership and management in the field of education in general and in schools, such as: curriculum, teaching and learning, assessment, learning, school planning, school management, financial management. Objects Community Inspection Inspections.
* Demonstrate knowledge of ethical scientific research, researchers for finding new knowledge and helping to solve problems in school education.
* Prepare, manage and evaluate schools with good governance so that schools can develop sustainably.
* Evaluate new information, ideas and evidence from various sources and use knowledge and experience to make proposals for solving problems in the process of leading and managing the school with confidence, such as student learning, assessment, teaching, teacher communication With the community, administration, finance, staff resources, and the school environment.
* Use information and communication technology to collect, interpret and disseminate information and ideas and new knowledge responsibly towards improving student learning, teacher teaching and brotherly communication with community parents. And stakeholders.
Apply knowledge and skills about leadership and education management in the development and improvement of schools to achieve the goals of responsible education, cooperation in a team spirit, respect and value to stakeholders.
* Develop a positive attitude and confidence, a sense of responsibility and accountability, and professional and life skills for professional work and living with others with dignity in society. Ms. Koy Pisey and General Kwan Sam continue. Visit border and ring road in Tbong Khmum and Prey Veng provinces
