(Phnom Penh): Sixty Cambodian military students from three institutions: Army, Navy and Air Force, who are studying in the Socialist Republic of Vietnam, visited and paid tribute to the martyrs of Cambodia. The historical heritage is located in Kam Mi district, Dong Nai province, Vietnam.
The event took place on the morning of November 28, 2020, led by a squadron of international trainees of the Second Border Protection Secondary School in Baria, Vietnam.
This is a visit to a historical site so that the military students can learn a lot about Cambodian history about the process of establishing 125 units, the first unit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and accompanied by four other comrades. Life was made to lead the formation of a resistance movement (Unit 125), the first unit of the Cambodian National Salvation Unity Force, established on May 12, 1978.
This movement was the first starting point of the movement of the Cambodian resistance movement before the establishment of the United Front for National Salvation of Cambodia on December 2, 1978, a national movement for the liberation of the country and People get rid of the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
All participants in the Socialist Republic of Vietnam thanked the school's management for organizing the visit.
They also expressed their deepest gratitude to the brave hero who dared to change his life and take life as the capital of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who worked hard physically and mentally away from his family and country to find peace for the people. To get rid of the Pol Pot regime.
