Ministry Tells Information and Audiovisual Professionals to Register (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Ministry of Information spokesman Meas Sophorn urges IT and audiovisual professionals to register At the Ministry of Commerce in accordance with the law, at the same time as the inter-ministerial announcement, the Ministry of Information and the Ministry of Commerce have officially announced that.
He was speaking at a press conference on "Business Registration and Protection of Trademarks and Trademarks for Information and Audiovisual Licensing" held on November 27, 2020.
In addition, a spokesman for the Ministry of Information also urged professionals in the field of information and audio-visual to adopt a profession to maintain the value of information as well as its institutions.
He added that "the Ministry of Information and the Ministry of Commerce have reached an agreement in the provision of a joint proclamation to provide more value for the organization or those who practice journalism and information in Cambodia. "There are values of quality professionalism, professional ethics and professionalism by following the procedures and laws as well as the legal documents in force."
On November 5, 2020, Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, stated that the request to open an information and audio-visual unit required to register with the Ministry of Information and the Ministry of Commerce could only proceed. He said that in the past, the request to open an information and audio-visual unit required only the Ministry of Information to be able to open, but now, in principle, must be registered with another Ministry of Commerce.
The Minister also urged the Ministry of Information Legal Unit to review some media units for the implementation of the above procedures as well as professional practices to ensure the rights of employees and staff working under the auspices of the media.
