Beaten 82-Year-Old Nun to Death at a Pagoda in Mongkul Borei District, Banteay Meanchey Province
(Banteay Meanchey): An 82-year-old nun was abducted and killed at a pagoda and was found by monks at 6:30 pm on November 26, 2020 at Wat Borom Niwet, Sala Deng Village, Russey Krok Commune, Mongkul Borei District. Banteay Meanchey Province.
Police said that the body of the victim, Sao Set, a 82-year-old woman, was a grandmother at a Buddhist monastery. Police said that before receiving information from a 28-year-old monk named Kim Sokmak, when he was urinating in the toilet near the victim's house, he heard the radio on but could not see her.
At that time, the monk also called two other monks to call her, but when he arrived, he found out that he had been beaten to death and did not know when, and then informed the authorities.
After receiving the information, the Mongkol Borei Provincial and District Criminal Police, led by Brigadier General Sithi Loh, Provincial Police Commissioner, arrived at the scene and concluded that her body was a murder because she claimed to have been beaten. On a crushed surface.
After making a report, the police force is searching for the killer, burning his hands and feet to find the killer and bring him to justice.
