(Phnom Penh): Cambodians of Chinese descent living overseas have raised more than 210,000 US dollars for Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, to help solve the difficulties of the Royal Government and the people affected by the floods in the past.
Duke Pung Kheav Se, President of the Cambodian-Chinese Coalition Association in Cambodia, highlighted that after receiving information about the victims of the Cambodian people due to the floods, Cambodians of Chinese descent living in the United States, Canada, France and other countries There is great sorrow and grief over this flood.
According to Duke Pung Kheavse, although these Cambodians of Chinese descent now live overseas, they still miss Cambodia, their homeland, and always care for their fellow countrymen. And the development of the motherland of Cambodia.
