The general stressed that because the Royal Government has taken good measures to prevent Kovid-19 disease by cleaning, keeping the social gap, washing hands, we can take good care of our health, there is no such vicious infection.
General Moeng Samphan added that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the head of the Royal Government, has taken care to protect the well-being of the people at all times, as well as to help restore the lives of the people and the national economy from the effects of Kovid-19, such as : Provides cash subsidies to disadvantaged people affected by the Kovid-19 outbreak in the past.
During the meeting with the people at that time, General Moeng Samphan brought some materials such as masks, gels, alcohol to the health center to continue to prevent and prevent Kovid-19 disease.
Blessing Ceremony for Fresh News on Fresh Building of Fresh News Unit was held this Friday morning, November 27, 2020. The blessing ceremony was held according to the Khmer Buddhist tradition, with the blessing of Samdech Preah Vanroth Noy Chrek, the third Deputy Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia and four other monks.
The Blessing Headquarters, which is inaugurated today, is a brand new achievement and a personal asset of Fresh News under the thoughtful management efforts and overcoming many obstacles of the co-founders. Mr. Lim Chea Vutha and Mr. Kim Meng and the staff as some leaders, as well as the active participation and high work spirit of all staff.
Mr. Lim Chea Vutha told the staff that the presence of the building of Fresh News is a great new achievement for the unit born from the hard work and energetic efforts of the management and staff for almost 6 years. With overcoming countless difficulties and obstacles.
"From today we have a warm support, which is our asset," the young CEO said. This building is the result of our hard work. We will continue to walk together, move forward together and succeed together. "I could not have had this day without the participation of all of you."
CEO Lim Chea Vutha also took this opportunity to thank all business owners for co-sponsoring Fresh News' media coverage. Mr. Lim Chea Vutha said that the support and cooperation of the owners of these companies and businesses are a strong support for the operation and progress of Fresh News. Announcing the transfer of duties, appointments and ranks to 150 National Police officers in Ratanakkiri Province
(Ratanakkiri): General Pen Vibol, Deputy Commissioner General and Director of the Personnel Department, Representative of General Santin Bandith Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General, this morning, November 27, 2020, announced the transfer of duties, appointments and ranks to officials. 150 members of the Ratanakkiri National Police.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Muong Pang, Deputy Governor of Ratanakkiri Province and was attended by the Commander of the three Armed Forces, Judges, Deputy Prosecutor of the Provincial Court, Deputy Commissioner, Deputy Chief of Planning. , Chief-Deputy Chief of Office, District Inspector, City under the Ratanakkiri Provincial Police Commissioner.
In addition, I would like to ask all officers, deputy chiefs and police officers to have good internal unity, to have good relations with other departments, units and institutions to implement the 9 points of safe village-commune policy of the Royal Government and thank you for the peace. Which makes the country progress as today and participate in the implementation of the Ministry of Health to prevent the spread of Kovid-19.
In the next 3 weeks, Cambodian travelers from abroad will be coming to work at Chatsalisak Center, Phnom Penh, in Prek Pnov District
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Youk Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, said that in about three weeks, we will be able to send Cambodian passengers from abroad to do the Leysak at the "Leysak Center in Phnom Penh" at all costs during the Leysak. The Royal Government is the insurer as before.
This statement was made by the Secretary of State during a visit to Phnom Penh's Leysak Center, located in Phsar Lech Village, Sangkat Prek Pnov, Khan Prek Pnov, on the afternoon of November 27, 2020.
She said, "When the center is completed by the end of 2020, all travelers from abroad as Cambodian citizens, we will bring all the location at this location. In the past, we have taken some school sites and other places to do licenses for them. ”
Please be informed that the Ministry of Health, in cooperation with Phnom Penh Capital Hall, has built 4 buildings that can accommodate 460 people and expanded 2 more buildings that can accommodate 800 people in a land area of about 1 hectare at a total cost of 790,000 USD. Funded by the Royal Government of Cambodia.
She stated that when the new location is ready for Cambodian travelers from abroad to come to the new location, except foreigners who have to stay at the hotel. This practice is made to be easy to manage because in this center, there are doctors on duty and equipment already.
Tbong Khmum Provincial Governor Provides 5 Million Riels to Joint Police Forces to Crack Down on Illegal Fishing in Peam Chiliang Commune, Tbong Khmum District
(Tbong Khmum): On the morning of November 26, 2020, the forces of Tbong Khmum Provincial Administrative Unity Command and Tbong Khmum District joint forces conducted a joint operation to crack down on fishery crimes at Peam village, Peam Chiliang commune, Tbong Khmum district. Fishing in prohibited areas and using illegal fishing gear and transporting it to brokers in Peam Chiliang commune for distribution to the market.
Authorities say that recently, a number of illegal fishing gangs broke into the fish conservation area bordering Tbong Khmum-Kroch Chhmar district using illegal fishing gear. Also, take care to protect all fish, do not use illegal fishing gear and do not fish in the restricted area.
Preliminary results from the half-dose group of volunteers showed that the vaccine protected them from COVID-19 better than the two-dose group. This means that the vaccine is 90% effective when given to low-dose volunteers and only 62% effective when 2 doses are given to volunteers, and the combined results are vaccines. 70% effective.
The Swedish Embassy in Cambodia announced on its Facebook page on November 27 that its government on November 26 decided to close its embassy in Phnom Penh by the end of 2021. The embassy claimed that Sweden has always had good relations with Cambodia and will continue to do so through other means after the embassy closes.
(Kampong Chhnang): Two women died after being sent to the Provincial Referral Center and 13 others were in critical condition after all the victims ate well water in the field. Lunch break at 12 noon on November 25, 2020 in Chip Rang village, Chiep commune, Teuk Phos district, Kampong Chhnang province.
The victims who died in the water poisoning case were Nol Varom, 45 years old, and Mao Chenda, 47 years old, both living in Chi Prang village, Chiep commune, Teuk Phos district, Kampong Chhnang province.
On the morning of November 25, 2020, a total of 14 people, including a girl, were taken to the hospital, said Risaran, a young victim. Going to harvest rice at O Rong in Chi Prang village, they stopped to eat at 12:00 noon, while he went to fetch water from a well in the field to eat together.
After eating and resting for a while, they started harvesting again until 4 pm, some people started to have nausea, headache, dizziness and sent to Teuk Phos District Health Center, but due to severe symptoms. Transferred to the Provincial Referral Hospital at 9 p.m.
Due to the severe condition that could not be saved until more than 12 midnight, a woman who owned a field died and on November 26 at 5:45 pm, another woman also died at the Provincial Referral Hospital. .
According to the woman, there was a watermelon field near the rice field, which was suspected to have been sprayed with pesticides in the watermelon field. Poisoned to death and the victim was being treated at the hospital, so this is just his suspicion, however, waiting for the results of the investigation by the authorities.
Regarding the above case, Mr. Khem Vibol, Police Inspector of Teuk Phos District, said that in the case where two people died and 13 others were hospitalized, there was a suspicion of drinking the well water. In fact, professional officials are also doing research.
Apsara Authority experts excavate pottery kiln north of Angkor Thom
(Siem Reap): Researchers from the International Center for Research and Documentation of Angkor of APSARA Authority in November 2020 excavated at Tuol Trapeang Bos in Kor Krao village, Kork Chak commune, Siem Reap city, located north of the land gate. The pot of Angkor Thom found an ancient pottery kiln, which was presumed to have been in the Angkorian or post-Angkorian period.
The project will be completed on December 10, 2020, and through excavations, the team also found that most of the furnace walls and utensils were everyday items, with clay pots, tiled stoves, but no smooth layers. After the excavation, the team will ask for research principles in this area further by listing all the hills, mapping this place as a protected area for tourists to visit and study by researchers.
Mr. Chhay Rachana, Director of the Angkor Pottery Office of the Angkor Center for International Research and Documentation, also confirmed that at this time the team did not know the full shape of the kiln, only saw the walls of a small round kiln with a fire place with a diameter of three. Only square meters, and the features of this pottery structure are amazing like never before.
Spokesman for the General Commission: On November 27, another 790 vehicles were inspected and fined
(Phnom Penh): On November 27, 2020, the traffic police throughout Cambodia inspected and fined a total of 790 vehicles, including 715 motorcycles and 175 cars. This was confirmed by Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and spokesman for the National Police.
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, during the 211 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to November 27, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and A total of 225,908 vehicles were fined, including 166,877 motorcycles and 59,031 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 211 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
It should be noted that for November 27, 2020, there were 3 traffic accidents throughout Cambodia, in which 1 person was killed and 6 people were injured (05 people were seriously injured).
Good young people unite to support drug eradication! Nationwide drug crackdown for November 27: 31 cases cracked, 73 arrested
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide campaign against illegal drugs for November 27, 2020 showed that law enforcement forces cracked down on 31 cases, including 8 cases of use, 23 cases of trafficking and arrested 73 suspects.
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of November 27, 2020, General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, paid a courtesy call on Brigadier General Win Koko, Myanmar's newly-appointed Deputy Chief of Mission in Cambodia. .
During a meeting at the headquarters, Brigadier General Win Koko emphasized that during his three years in the military, he had studied a lot of Cambodian culture and heritage.
At the same time, the Myanmar Military Attaché also observed and highly appreciated the momentum of progress in all areas that Cambodia has achieved under the leadership of the Royal Government headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Cambodia is stable and peaceful throughout the country.
The Myanmar Military Attaché expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Cambodian people for donating more than 2 million masses and medical equipment to Myanmar to prevent the 19 Kovid epidemic. The Brigadier General considers Samdech Techo's donation at this time to be very valuable and reflects the true friendship that the Kingdom of Cambodia has with Myanmar in this difficult circumstance.
In response, General Vong Pisen praised the Myanmar Joint Chiefs of Staff's diplomatic mission, which further strengthened and expanded cooperation between the two armies.
The Commander-in-Chief reminded that the two countries (Cambodia-Myanmar) have a tradition and cooperation since 1955 and in 2020 is the 65th anniversary of the establishment of relations between the two countries.
The General congratulated Myanmar on the smooth conduct of the general election for paving the way for peace, national unity and stability in the country.
General Vong Pisen also expressed his condolences over the spread of Kovid 19 virus in Myanmar, which has claimed the lives of more than 1,800 people.
(Siem Reap): The leadership of APSARA Authority has instructed all its subordinates to pay more attention to make the results better.
