He instructed all departments to pay more attention to make the results better.
(Mondulkiri): After inspecting the border in Stung Treng and Ratanakkiri provinces, on November 26, 2020, Ms. Koy Pisey, Deputy Director of the Permanent Secretariat of the National Authority for Border Affairs and Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism and General Kwan Sam The Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander-in-Chief of the Engineering Command continued to visit Mondulkiri and Kratie provinces to further inspect the border and the ring road.
Inspections of the border and the ring road in the two provinces were also attended by some relevant local authorities.
Ms. Koy Pisey stated that Mondulkiri is a potential natural tourism area in the northeast of Cambodia, which has an eastern border with Vietnam. Those who want to travel along the border more easily, in addition to the roads to travel all the way and appreciate the natural beauty of the mountains, we have the opportunity to see the border posts running along the border ring road.
She added that the Royal Government is preparing to develop all border areas into border areas of peace, friendship, cooperation, tourism and trade in order to ensure that the people living along the border have the same opportunities as the people in the city and become The border area becomes a development area in all fields.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kun Kim, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission and First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, this morning, November 27, 2020, attended the 8th ASEAN Ministerial Meeting on Disaster Management System. Bluejeans Video Conference on "Promoting Transition to ASEAN in a Safe, Adaptive, Integrative and Resilient"
During the meeting, on behalf of the National Committee for Disaster Management of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Senior Minister Kun Kim thanked the Ministry of Defense of the Republic of the Philippines for hosting this year's meeting in the context of ASEAN member countries. All 10, as well as the entire world, are facing the crisis of Kovid-19.
On behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, Senior Minister Kun Kim expressed his deepest condolences and condolences for the loss of life and suffering of the victims. From Kovid-19 and recent natural disasters in ASEAN member states as well as in other countries around the world.
Senior Minister Kun Kim added that in tackling Kovid-19, the Royal Government of Cambodia has set out a number of strategies and measures to combat the Kovid-19 pandemic. In addition to Kovid-19, Cambodia also suffered severe flooding from September to October 2020, affecting 20 capitals and provinces.
Responding to the recent disasters in Cambodia, Kun Kim told the ASEAN Minister in charge of Disaster Management that Cambodia has always adhered to a culture of sharing in the spirit of mutual assistance for emergency relief using total force. And the overall means by which the armed forces have played an important role in disaster relief.
Therefore, Cambodia is committed to working closely with all stakeholders to reduce disaster risk in the country as well as in the ASEAN region, taking into account and referring to the "Sendai Framework for Risk Reduction". Disaster 2015-2030.
The meeting agreed to support the adoption of the ADDMER 2021-2025, which was unanimously approved by the 37th ASEAN Disaster Management Committee Meeting on 25 November 2020. The Amyra work program is intended to facilitate greater coordination among ASEAN member countries and contribute to the implementation of the ASEAN Declaration on "One ASEAN, One Response".
Hairdresser killed by truck in Meanchey district
(Phnom Penh): A horrific traffic accident occurred when a truck overturned, killing a man at the scene.
The incident happened at 2:40 pm on November 26, 2020 at the Boeung Trabek Pumping Station along Street 271 in Chak Angre Leu Sangkat, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh.
According to the police, the victim was But Sopheak, a 30-year-old male hairdresser living in Prek Thom Village, Sangkat Kbal Koh, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh. The perpetrator is Hoeung Rath, male, 29 years old, driver, living in Phum Teuk Thla, Khum Pheary Meanchey, Bor Seth District, Kampong Speu Province.
After the incident, the truck drove away from the scene, but was chased by the authorities until the road 60 meters was stopped.
After the incident, the competent authorities contacted the Land Traffic Police Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police to come down and measure at the scene and bring the perpetrator to the office for legal action.
Meanwhile, the body of the man was handed over to his family for a traditional ceremony in his hometown.
Mr. Khuong Sreng: Authorities will start developing Boeung Tumpun pumping station at the beginning of the dry season in 2021 to prevent future floods
(Phnom Penh): In order to speed up the pumping of water to avoid flooding in the coming years, Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, said that the Phnom Penh Capital Administration plans to install a new 1.5-meter water pump. And 2 1m2 water units, including the rehabilitation of the canal to be larger and the excavation on both sides of the canal at the Boeung Tumpun pumping station.
The decision to install a new pumping station, including canal rehabilitation at Boeung Tumpun Pumping Station, was made at a meeting on the development of Boeung Tumpun Pumping Station in Sangkat Boeung Tumpun I, Khan Meanchey this morning, November 27, 2020, chaired by Mr. Khuong Sreng.
The governor said that after this year, heavy rainfall conditions, including limited pumping capacity, caused some areas to be flooded due to the rains, which disrupted people's livelihoods.
The Governor of Phnom Penh said, "The Boeung Tumpun Pumping Station receives water from a lot of rainwater, such as flowing from Boeung Salang, Mondial area, Street 261, Sangkat Toek Laak 3, Khan Toul Kork, Lu Pram area, Stung Meanchey and another part of Khan Por Sen Chey. "There is redevelopment to be able to release water quickly."
The Capital Governor confirmed that today, the Capital Administration held a meeting to do more work, including:
Mr. Sam Piseth, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, said that the current condition of Boeung Tumpun water pump is 6 units, 4 old machines can pump 10 cubic meters per second and 2 new machines can pump 5 cubic meters per second, a total of 15 cubic meters per second, thus not meeting the demand.
He said that according to the study, the area of rainfall that flows to Boeung Tumpun station is 3,032 hectares, if the rainfall is 30 mm per hour, the amount of rainfall will increase by more than 9,900,000 cubic meters, 40 mm of rain. More than 1.2 million cubic meters of water per hour, and if it rains 60 millimeters per hour, more than 1.8 million cubic meters of water, so this volume does not meet the pump.
He said that in order to solve the problem of flooding in the area of Boeung Tumpun pumping station, six measures need to be taken.
The director of the department stated that the Capital Administration has six measures to solve this water problem, including:
Please note that according to the development plan of the Boeung Tumpun pumping station, it is planned to use for 9 months, starting from December 2020 onwards.
More than $ 30 million small and medium enterprise gathering area in Kandal province has opened a construction site, Senior Minister Cham Prasidh considers this a peaceful achievement
The groundbreaking ceremony was also attended by national and international guests, such as ambassadors and ambassadors, leaders of relevant ministries and institutions, and company staff. This area is located in Koh Kor Village, Sangkat Roka Khpos, Takhmao City, Kandal Province.
Senior Minister Cham Prasidh said that this area is the first SME Cluster in Cambodia, worth about 30 million US dollars on 6 hectares. The regional alliances also bring together small and medium-sized enterprises: electricity, water, telecommunications, roads, commercial buildings, enterprises, production bases, production processes, businesses and services.
He said that Cambodia is in the context of complete peace, political stability and social stability throughout the country, which is the sacred fruit of the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia has made the country develop in all areas. Therefore, as the leader of the Ministry of Industry and on behalf of the Royal Government, he announced his sincere support and appreciation to Mr. Sear Rithy and his colleagues who have invested in this area.
Mr. Sear Rithy said that the construction project will last for eight months and is scheduled to be completed by the end of 2021. He said that by formally investing in standardized services and reliable infrastructure for small and medium enterprises, the production line can really enhance value, create resources, save time, be creative, production and management. Quality and cost efficiency.
Not only that, these projects can provide mutual benefits, provide mutual support and improve community relations, and can also encourage more people to participate in the use of renewable energy through Providing appropriate financing that does not cause a social deficit, on the contrary, it can provide opportunities for people to continue to grow their family economy and society in a more sustainable way.
150 young teachers learn about heritage management in Angkor
(Siem Reap): Mr. Nget Sok Chan, Director of the Youth Office of the Department of Education and Youth of Phnom Penh, this afternoon, November 27, 2020, led the Council of Cambodian Children - Youth of Cambodia, 150 teachers of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. Listen to the presentation on conservation and sustainable development at Angkor resort from the leadership of APSARA Authority.
