In particular, from October 1 to November 27, 2020, provided humanitarian donations to flood victims and the most vulnerable people, a total of 34,002 families living in 1,002 villages. 436 districts, 171 districts and 25 capitals and provinces (including 14,976 families by the central office and 19,026 families by branch).
