According to Venezuelan Foreign Minister Ariasza, he plans to visit all 10 ASEAN member states once travel restrictions on the COVID-19 pandemic are lifted. ADB approves $ 70 million loan to strengthen Cambodia's agricultural value chain and food safety
According to the press release, the project to strengthen the competition of value chain and capacity in the agricultural sector aims to benefit 230 agricultural cooperatives and 50 agricultural enterprises in Kampong Cham, Kampong Thom, Oddar Meanchey, Preah Vihear, Siem Reap and Tbong Khmum.
The project will facilitate access to credit for agriculture and agribusiness, which is receiving only about 10% of the total official financing. The project will implement mutually supportive financing types, including lending and guaranteeing.
The project will support initiatives to strengthen food safety and quality in the value chain for cassava, cashews, mangoes, vegetables and farm chicken. It will enable agricultural cooperatives to carry out agricultural activities well and upgrade food safety laboratories to gain international recognition.
The project will also support the research and development of seeds and breeding birds by helping agricultural cooperatives obtain high-yielding, drought-resistant, disease-resistant seeds, as well as supporting other planting materials. In addition, the project will improve 110 km of rural roads and connect agricultural products to markets in the project area.
The Asian Development Bank (ADB) is committed to achieving environmental prosperity, resilience and sustainability in the Asia-Pacific region in line with its efforts to eradicate extreme poverty. Founded in 1966, the bank is governed by 68 member countries, of which 49 are from the region.
Indonesia visits "Samdech Mey Library"
(Phnom Penh): The vision of the Documentation Center of Cambodia is to focus on justice and the memory that is the foundation for healing for the survivors of the Khmer Rouge regime on the destructive legacy of the regime.
DC-Cam has used a number of means to preserve the arts, culture and national heritage as a basis for reconciliation. In 2015, the Documentation Center of Cambodia team participated in a workshop organized by the National Museum of Indonesia on the topic of protection and conservation.
There, the team interacted with an Indonesian artist, Nyoman Nuata, who specializes in sculpture. The team mentioned working with the artist to create a sculpture representing Cambodian women, a vision that has been in the public eye since 2008.
Mr. Nyumen and his wife visited Phnom Penh and Siem Reap to gather ideas about sculpture and to interview some of the women who survived the Khmer Rouge era. As a result of the visit, Nyomyen created a sculpture representing a woman to the Documentation Center of Cambodia to honor and respect Cambodian women, entitled "The Cambodian Heroine of Hope" ("PILLAROFHOPE").
