(Phnom Penh): Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the morning of November 27, 2020, delivered a keynote address via video at the opening ceremony of the 17th China-ASEAN Expo in Nanning, Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region. China.
The 17th China-ASEAN Expo 2020 will be held under the theme "Building the Belt and Road and Strengthening Digital Economic Cooperation", focusing on promoting regional economic recovery after the Kovid-19 crisis. And maintaining the momentum of deeper and deeper cooperation between China and ASEAN.
In this keynote address, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stressed the need to strengthen the commitment to uphold the principles of multilateralism and international cooperation in addressing the serious socio-economic impact of the Kovid-19 pandemic.
He stressed the importance of developing a digital economy and a digital society to adapt to new circumstances, promote resilience and sustainable development, and achieve further progress.
Samdech Techo also spoke about Cambodia's efforts to promote digitalization of production, industry, services and public administration, as well as the implementation of drastic reform measures to improve the business and investment environment.
The China-ASEAN Expo is an important forum for promoting trade, investment, economy, politics, tourism, culture and diplomatic relations. In particular, comprehensive cooperation between China and the 10 ASEAN member countries. The China-ASEAN Expo has been held annually since 2004 in Nanning, Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region, China.
Cambodia fully supports the organization of the China-ASEAN Expo. Samdech Techo Hun Sen has personally participated in the exhibition event 11 times in the past, which is more than the leaders of other ASEAN countries.
But for the year 2020, due to the problem of Kovid 19, Samdech Techo could not be invited to participate directly, only to give a speech via video system.
