Ministry of Commerce ready to host 1st Asia-Europe Economic and Business Forum
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, said that the working group is ready to host the first "Asia-Europe Economic and Business Forum".
During the meeting to review the work progress of the Secretariat Committee and the working group for the preparation of the first "Asia-Europe Economic and Business Forum" on November 26, 2020, Mr. Pan Sosak emphasized that the first Asia-Europe Economic and Business Forum A forum for business leaders from Asia and Europe.
He said the forum aims to strengthen trade and investment ties between the two countries, Asia and Europe.
According to Mr. Pan Sosak, in order for the meeting to be successful as expected, the Ministry has set up three working groups, including: 1: Documentation and Dissemination Working Group, 2: Venue Protocol Working Group Transport, Arts and Security Meeting and 3: Supply and Finance Working Group.
At the same time, the protocol team for organizing the venue, transportation, arts and security is divided into 8 groups, including: 1: Coordinating team, 2: Document and information dissemination team, 3: Product presentation and decoration team, 4th: Communication Officer, 5th: Art Group, 6th: Security Team, 7th: Transport Team, 8th: Protocol Team.
