Ministry of Tourism: Six major tourist destinations have been identified in the tourism development master plan of Mondulkiri province
(Phnom Penh): Six major tourism development plans have been selected by the Inter-Ministerial Commission to be identified and included in the Mondulkiri Tourism Development Master Plan 2020-2035, as these tourist destinations have other important geographical locations and potentials. Each, according to Mr. Chuk Chumnor, Director of the Department of Tourism Product Development, Ministry of Tourism.
The statement of the Ministry of Tourism was made after the meeting of the Inter-Ministerial Commission to consult on the third draft of the Mondulkiri Tourism Development Master Plan chaired by Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism on November 26, 2020 at the Ministry of Tourism.
Minister Thong Khon said that the completion of these inputs is to contribute to the development of tourism in Mondulkiri to be more attractive to attract international tourists will increase to 900,000 and more than 2 domestic tourists. Millions in 2035 with the development of new tourism products in line with the spirit of the master plan.
The Minister added that in the tourism development master plan of Mondulkiri province, six major tourist destinations are divided according to different geographical locations and potentials, including:
Ecotourism areas in the wildlife sanctuary: Because in Mondulkiri province, there are 5 wildlife sanctuaries under the control of the Ministry of Environment and full of potential in the field of ecotourism.
* Ecotourism and Indigenous Tourism Corridor: This second tourist destination will be connected from Busra to Dak Dam.
* Sen Monorom area: will develop this city into a multi-purpose development area with a variety of recreational activities.
* Mondulkiri Airport area in Oreang district: which will be developed as a satellite city of Sen Monorom city.
* Border Gate Integration Zone: In Mondulkiri province, there are four bilateral border gates with Vietnam, which can promote development activities and tourism along this border.
Mr. Thong Khon continued that after receiving the above suggestions, the expert team will write some more important inputs from the inter-ministerial-institution to prepare the final draft and will continue to submit to the Tourism Development Committee. National at the end of December 2020. After the approval of this commission and will continue to submit to the Royal Government in early 2021.
Ministry of Social Affairs Holds Consultative Workshop on Strategic Plan for Service Force Training Focusing on Child Protection 2021-2025
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation has organized a consultative workshop on a strategic plan to train service forces focusing on child protection 2021-2025, with technical and financial support from UNICEF and an invitation. Attended by 50 workshop members.
This consultation workshop is an important forum to participate in discussions, exchange ideas and share with each other the wisdom to be clearer and more comprehensive on the joint strategic activities of the Ministry to train forces. Social services.
This strategic plan, which is drafted, is the first five-year plan, focusing on vocational training in social work in order to strengthen the capacity of the social services force to have the right level of knowledge and professional skills with professional ethics. To provide services to customers who are victims and vulnerable to ensure high efficiency.
At the same time, the draft strategic plan sets out three major strategic points to be discussed in the collection of additional inputs: first, to develop programs and training packages for social services, and second, to improve the effectiveness of Education and training of social service forces; and third, strengthening the capacity of social service education and training institutions.
Mr. Khom Phal Loeun, Director of the National Institute of Social Affairs, representing the Ministry of Social Affairs, said that the workshop highlighted that this strategic plan is the first plan to focus on vocational training in social skills in order to strengthen the capacity of social services to the level of knowledge. And a real level of professional ethics to provide services to customers who are victims and vulnerable to ensure high efficiency.
He added that, of course, the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation has always been focused on improving the quality and modernizing human resource training in its field.
