(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Vandeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, presided over the handover ceremony of the President of the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia, with the participation of the leadership of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications and the management and staff of the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia. Many in the afternoon of November 26, 2020 at the Office of the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia.
Mr. Mov Chakrya, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, made a brief report on the major achievements of the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia in the past in relation to the modernization of equipment, expansion of the efficiency of telecommunication and ICT infrastructure, crime prevention and resource capacity building. People support the lives of civil servants to ensure the strength of the spirit of solidarity.
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Thong Chenda, the newly appointed President of the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia, said that he would like to express his deep gratitude to the Head of the Royal Government and the Minister for giving him the confidence to appoint him to lead the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia.
Taking the opportunity, he also praised the efforts of Mr. Mov Chakrya in leading the institution in the past, which has made a significant change in the sector.
The President is highly committed to the successful implementation of the policy of unwavering and unwavering reform, adhering to the art of soft but firm leadership, the energetic vibrancy of the Minister, as well as the political program of the Royal Government related to development and modernization. Telecommunications sector with quality, efficiency and honest competition.
On this occasion, Minister Chea Vandeth praised Mr. Mov Chakrya for many important achievements for the sector and the organization in the past.
The Minister highlighted some important priorities for Mr. Thong Chenda to focus on improving the efficiency of regulation, management, licensing, revenue collection from the telecommunications sector, and promoting the preparation of relevant legal documents. Ensure honest competition, protect consumers, and strengthen the quality of telecommunications services and telecommunication equipment standards.
Minister Chea Vandeth also instructed the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia to continue to strengthen the management of the administration to be more effective in performing its functions, promote the strengthening of human resources and professional capacity through additional training.
Minister Chea Van Det emphasized the strong belief that under the active and energetic leadership of Mr. Thong Chenda and especially the joint support and efforts of the leadership and civil servants at all levels, the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia will Continue to achieve many more achievements for the motherland.
