Director General of the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture urges farmers to strengthen the ability to grow safe vegetables with high yields instead of imports
(Kandal): Mr. Kao Thach, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Rural Development Bank and Agriculture, this morning, November 26, 2020, presided over the study visit program of vegetable farmers to Koh Thom Safe Vegetable Farm. Located in Kbal Damrey Leu village, Kampong Kong commune, Koh Thom district, Kandal province.
The invited participants are: Mr. Phan Phalla, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Member of the Board of Directors of the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture, Representatives of the Department of Agriculture of Kandal Province, Representatives of District / Commune Authorities and 62 model farmers in Kandal Province.
Mr. Kao Thach highlighted the model farmers who were present about some of the main reasons that led the Rural Development Bank and Agriculture to support the Koh Thom Safe Vegetable Farm project.
First, the supply of vegetables by Cambodian farmers to the market is still limited and can not respond enough for domestic consumption, so we need to import more vegetables from abroad. He said that in our case, we have already acknowledged that some of the imported vegetables contain chemicals that affect the health of consumers.
He added that this is why the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture, and on his own behalf, wants to see more Cambodian farmers grow vegetables without chemicals and high safety in order to supply enough local vegetables sustainably and accessible. To be able to export abroad.
Therefore, through the visit of the model farmers today, Mr. Kao Thach asked the farmers to strengthen and expand the capacity to grow safe vegetables with high yields to supply the market instead of importing vegetables from abroad.
Second, about your vegetable growing techniques are still limited and have a non-entrepreneurial mindset. In this regard, through the study tour program, Mr. Kao Thach would like to draw the attention of the model farmers to have a keen will to change the vegetable growing habits by acting on behalf of entrepreneurs, that is, growing vegetables to be a local supply business. Sufficient and capable of exporting abroad.
Mr. Kao Thach believes that when you change your farming habits, your life will be better and you will be able to reduce the poverty of your people.
