Spokesman for the General Commission: On November 26, another 800 vehicles were inspected and fined
(Phnom Penh): On November 26, 2020, the traffic police throughout Cambodia inspected and fined a total of 800 vehicles, including 610 motorcycles and 190 cars. This was confirmed by Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and spokesman for the National Police.
According to the spokesman of the General Commissioner, for 210 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to November 26, 2020, the traffic police across the country inspected and A total of 225,118 vehicles were fined, including 166,262 motorcycles and 58,856 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun continued that for the past 210 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
