Chip Mong focuses on the preservation of heritage by preserving and renovating a two-story French-style building in the center of the Hyatt Regency Hotel Phnom Penh to highlight the balance of Cambodia's ancient and modern times. The Hyatt Regency Hotel is the first hotel and hospitality project by Chip Mong, a local giant that has always focused on giving back to society.
Not yet operational, the Hyatt Regency Phnom Penh Hotel has brought local infrastructure improvements around the project for the common good of the community. In fact, the repair and construction of widening of Street 178 and the installation of side drains from Norodom Blvd. to Sisowath Quay cost more than $ 600,000 to facilitate the traffic of the public passing through the hotel.
The presence of Chip Mong Hyatt Regency Phnom Penh Hotel in Phnom Penh will enhance the beauty of Phnom Penh in this rich historical, cultural and commercial area.
Hyatt Regency is a brand of Hayat Hotel Corporation, a US hotel company that has been present in the international market for more than six decades, and to date, there are a total of 950 Hyatt hotels in 67 countries on six continents. The world.
