Minister Ith Sam Heng spoke about the progress in the field of employment and vocational training in Cambodia, which stems from the good cooperation between Cambodia and South Korea since the establishment of diplomatic ties in 1997.
He further emphasized the past cooperation between Cambodia and the Republic of Korea, including boosting Cambodia-Korea trade volume in 2019 to reach more than 1.5 billion US dollars. Investment from Korea in Cambodia is worth more than 5 billion US dollars to date and has made Korea the second largest country to invest in Cambodia.
He said that Cambodia and Korea are negotiating a free trade agreement to sign into force soon. The agreement will boost trade and investment, and more Korean investors will come to Cambodia to seek investment opportunities in other areas.
The Minister confirmed to the Ambassador that the Ministry of Labor will work to better support trade agreements related to Korean investors wishing to invest in Cambodia.
Regarding the transfer of Cambodian workers to Korea, HE Minister said that after the situation of Kovid-19 in Korea has eased to accept foreign labor, Cambodia is expected to become a priority country in Among the other 15 countries, due to Cambodia's favorable Kovid status, there are more flights.
The Ambassador of the Republic of Korea stated that in 2019, Cambodian workers have the largest number of workers working in Korea, and during the Kovid-19 phase of 2020, the Government of the Republic of Korea will still allow Cambodian workers.
"The reason why Korea allows such Cambodian workers is because the employers are satisfied with the high capacity of Cambodian workers, are honest with their work and strictly follow the instructions of the Korean government's health department," he said.
Please be informed that since 2007, Cambodia has sent a total of 68,294 workers (14,255 women) to work in Korea, including industry, agriculture and construction, with a term of 4 years 10 months while Currently, there are nearly 50,000 Cambodian workers working in Korea.
