Rice mill in Rolous commune, Dangkor district caught fire, police use 4 water trucks to put out the fire
(Phnom Penh): A fire broke out at a rice mill along National Road 2 in Kandal Village, Rolous Sangkat, Dangkor District, Phnom Penh at 9:10 am on November 26, 2020, and the fire was extinguished on time. Without causing it to spread to other places.
Colonel Prohm Yorn, director of the fire prevention office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, told Fresh News that after receiving a call from residents that there was a fire in a rice mill, he immediately issued an order. Eight fire trucks of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police to immediately intervene.
Colonel Prohm Yorn continued that in this case, the fire destroyed a rice dryer (size 3 meters x 20 meters) and did not cause the fire to spread to neighboring houses. The colonel added that the owner of the above location is Bung Sothy, a 43-year-old male rice miller.
During the operation, the police used 12 fire trucks using 4 water trucks, including:
* 8 fire trucks of Phnom Penh Municipal Police (using 2 units of water) * 3 fire trucks of Kandal Provincial Police (using 1 unit of water) * 1 fire truck of Cambodia Beer Company Use 1 unit of water.
