Minister Prum Sokha officially announces the inauguration of 30 officials of the Ministry of Public Works
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Public Service, Mr. Prum Sokha, on the afternoon of November 25, 2020, officially announced the inauguration of 30 officials of the Ministry of Public Service.
The ceremony was held at the Royal School of Administration with the participation of the Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, Deputy Director General, Deputy Director General, Deputy Director of the Royal School of Administration and many other government officials.
Pursuant to the Royal Decree, Sub-Decree and Prakas, the Ministry has decided to appoint 30 officials, including 8 ministry advisors, 2 undersecretaries of state, 2 deputy secretaries-general, 4 deputy directors general, 1 director of the department, 4 deputy directors of the department. 1 Secretariat, 3 Heads of Offices and 7 Deputy Heads of Offices.
On that occasion, the Minister of Public Service recommended to the newly appointed civil servants and civil servants under the supervision of public functions, including:
* Must strive to fulfill their duties and responsibilities with a high sense of responsibility, respond appropriately to the trust of our nation and people.
* Increase internal solidarity among all civil servants in increasing work efficiency to contribute to the successful implementation of the Royal Government's political program and rectangular strategy under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister
* Must continue to pay high attention to prevent and participate in the fight against the spread of Kovid 19 in accordance with the health prevention measures of the Ministry of Health to set a good example to continue to strengthen public health safety and contribute more actively to the cause of health. Peace, well-being and social development are endless.
