APSARA Authority completes the renovation of a Buddha statue at Ruot Bakan, the top of Angkor Wat temple
(Siem Reap): A Buddha statue in the south of Ruot Bakan, the top of Angkor Wat temple, which has a problem with the quality of construction, was completed by the sculptor conservation experts of the APSARA Authority in November 2020.
Soy Sophearin, a sculptural conservation officer with the Department of Temple Preservation in Angkor Parks and Preventive Archeology, said the statue had some problems with his head, face, lower legs and legs. Due to the poor quality of the footrest, the weight of the body emphasizes the sole of the lower foot, which leads to the lower leg cracking because the weight is too heavy.
Mr. Sophearin said that in order to save the statue to be better, the conservation team must regularly monitor the damaged condition and study, compile and repair in time to prevent serious problems to the whole statue. Now the first thing to do is strengthen the lower leg, change the support brace to reduce the pressure on the support.
For the body of the statue, the team used a dry cleaning method with a soft brush to wipe the dust, spider mites, dog nests, and then wet clean by cleaning the black spots caused by smoke, incense, candles wrapped in salt on the body. Face and scalp using materials to analyze what salts can cleanse the salt, strengthen the decay area, what substance can retain its original color.
The Buddha was originally attached to a closed wall in the room of Ruot Bakan, but was carved out of the wall in the French period around 1943 to dig down the central well of Tu Bakan for archeological purposes.
Chamkarmon District Governor Inspects Sewerage Project in Sangkat Toul Tum Poung I
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Theng Sothol, Governor of Chamkar Mon District, this morning, November 25, 2020, led a professional officer and Deputy District Governor in charge of inspecting the new sewer system repair project on Street 460 from Street 105 to Street. No. 135 in Sangkat Toul Tum Poung I, Khan Chamkar Mon, Phnom Penh, which is a project to develop the Sangkat Toul Tum Poung I in 2020.
While inspecting the sewerage installation activities, the Governor of Chamkar Mon District instructed the contractor to install the sewerage system to speed up and complete it according to the plan and technically correct to ensure long-term quality.
The district governor said that in the area where the sewer system is being installed, after the drainage system is installed, there will be no more worries about flooding due to flooding or rainwater flooding on the road or the houses of people living on both sides of the road. Inspecting the construction site of the drainage project is a consideration by the local authority of Chamkar Mon district to solve the flood problem during the rainy season.
While inspecting the sewer construction site, Mr. Theng Sothol also met with the people in the backyard of the house to find out about the sewer project to understand their living conditions and needs. More importantly, it is the connection between the district leadership and the people, that is, always being together and always thinking about the hardships of the people. Rainy season.
