On that occasion, the General Commissioner also brought a donation of 2,700,000 Riels from the Office of the Anti-Economic Crimes Bureau of the National Police and the Friends of the National Police Commissioner General and General Neth Savoeun. To burden the cost of treatment for this disease as well.
According to the NEC, the initial voter list and the list of those to be removed from the 2020 voter list will be posted simultaneously in communes across the country on November 27, 2020. There were 8,831,988 registered voters and a total of 23,425 polling stations. Separately, 154,768 voters will be removed from the voter list.
In a meeting with stakeholders on the morning of November 25, 2020 at the NEC, Mr. Hang Puthea, Member and Spokesperson of the NEC and Chairman of the meeting, added that the posting The initial voter list and the list of those to be removed from the voter list are intended for people who have already registered to vote to participate in verifying their data to ensure that their names are accurate and clear.
Stakeholders who attended today's meeting were very interested in the names of more than 150,000 voters who will be removed from the 2020 voter list.
Deletion of a citizen's name from the voter list must be based on accurate, clear documents and go through several procedures to ensure that every Cambodian citizen who meets the legal requirements must be on the voter list. There are also procedures for filing, receiving and resolving complaints. The complaint is called a protest and / or objection.
Complaints may be made about the loss of a voter's name or a name on the voter list, but inaccurate records of relevant data or information he or she provided or the NEC has deleted the name incorrectly. Made for a person named on the initial voter list but who does not qualify to be named on the voter list and for a person named on more than one place on the voter list.
Mr. Hang Puthea emphasized that in order to ensure the official voter list 2020 is more accurate and transparent, all citizens who registered to vote from 2016 to 2020 are invited to check their names and relevant data on The first voter list and the list of those who will be removed from the 2020 voter list for everyone.
The meeting was attended by 75 people from the Constitutional Council, the Senate, the National Assembly, the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of Information, 18 political parties, 20 non-governmental organizations and 11 media units.
