(Philippines): ASEAN countries, including Cambodia, participated in the 6th Meeting of the ASEAN Trade Alliance on HIV / AIDS in the Workplace and the 3rd Red Cross Award Ceremony for Factories Enterprise in Good Practice, 2 days from November 25-26, 2020 via video from Manila, Philippines.
According to Leng Tong, Director of the Department of Labor Medicine of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, representing Cambodia, the meeting discussed the challenges of implementing and eliminating HIV / AIDS related to the ASEAN Trade Alliance among other countries. Countries that provide updated information and good practices in the prevention and control of HIV / AIDS programs in the workplace in each country.
The objectives of the 6th ASEAN Business Forum on HIV / AIDS are to focus on four areas:
* First: Update information on HIV / AIDS in the workplace for ASEAN member countries, such as the process of achieving HIV / AIDS prevention, other challenges related to HIV / AIDS in the workplace and In the National Trade Alliance of each ASEAN country
* Second: Share good practices and experiences in establishing an AIDS Commission in the workplace.
* Third: Discussion on the progress of HIV / AIDS prevention in the workplace from the plan for 2020-2022
* Fourth, the ASEAN Trade Alliance on HIV / AIDS will change its chair to coordinate the meeting every two years.
