(Phnom Penh): On November 25, 2020, the traffic police throughout Cambodia inspected and fined a total of 791 vehicles, including 550 motorcycles and 241 cars. This was confirmed by Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and spokesman for the National Police.
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, during the 209 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to November 25, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and A total of 224,318 vehicles were fined, including 165,652 motorcycles and 59,503 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 209 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for November 25, 2020, traffic accidents throughout the country also occurred 9 times, in which 2 people died, 14 people were injured (10 people were seriously injured).
