BERLIN (Reuters) - A car crashed into the entrance of German Chancellor Angela Merkel's office in Berlin on Wednesday morning ahead of a meeting on the renewal of closure measures. This was released by RT on Wednesday, November 25, 2020.
It was not immediately clear why the car hit the fence at the entrance to German Chancellor Angela Merkel's office, and there were no reports of injuries or arrests. However, according to several photos in the German media, the words on the car read: "Stop the politics of globalization and you are the killer of children and the elderly."
The incident took place before Merkel had to attend a video conference from her Berlin office Wednesday morning to discuss measures to combat COVID-19, including Consider renewing the closure measures.
