Secretary of State Em Chanmakara added, "In Cambodia in recent years, society has undergone many positive changes from the promotion of the rights of people with disabilities. "People with disabilities are recognized as important human resources for the development of the nation and are given equal opportunities to participate in various activities in society."
In front of the participants, civil servants of the Office of the Council of Ministers, Mr. Em Chanmakara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs and Secretary General of the Disability Action Council, requested the Disability Action Team of the Office of the Council of Ministers to help mainstream the National Strategic Plan on Disability 2019. -2023 and the Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities into the action plan of the relevant departments.
He added that the Royal Government of Cambodia has a clear vision to ensure that children with disabilities and families have a good quality of life and will participate fully and equally in a society with respect for rights and dignity, as well as an environment for disability. All sectors.
He added, however, that ensuring that people with disabilities could enjoy their rights without discrimination was not easy, despite the protections of the treaty in force. There are many barriers to equal participation in society, so we need to implement the Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities more strongly in accordance with the general principles.
At the same time, Mr. Soy Sokha also thanked the General Secretariat of the Disability Action Council for its good cooperation with the Disability Action Team of the Council of Ministers, which will soon give an important presentation on the progress. The implementation of the Convention to raise awareness, prevent, reduce, eliminate discrimination, protect the rights, freedoms and interests of people with disabilities as a priority goal of the Royal Government's social policy.
