Cambodian traders rush to sell rice in Vietnam through Koh Roka international gate, with authorities and police facilitating free of charge
Vendors and Taikong rice trucks say they are happy with the authorities at the Koh Roka international gate, not only do not charge for the truck, but also facilitate them to bring rice to sell in Vietnam without No obstruction.
They added that in the past, Tai Kong Lan had violated Vietnamese procedures to prevent Kovit 19 by being detained by Vietnam, but was immediately returned to Cambodia by the authorities and the immigration police. .
Moreover, if they bring rice to the border too late in the evening and the Vietnamese side closes the gate, the head of the headquarters and the gate police have arranged a suitable place for them to stay.
Mr. Khieu Soeun, Chief of Koh Roka Commune, commended Mr. Sang Sarum, Chief of Koh Roka International Border Checkpoint, and Mr. Keo, Chief of Koh Roka International Border Police, for leading the coordination work with the Vietnamese side for his local people as well. People in the provinces import rice to sell in Vietnam.
At the same time, Mr. Khieu Soeun also thanked Mr. Sang Sarum and Mr. Keo Chea, who always took care to facilitate the settlement with the Vietnamese side to understand the release of both people and cars immediately after the car was seized. And our Cambodian people who have problems related to mistakes affecting the prevention of Kovid-19.
Mr. Sang Sarum, Head of Koh Roka International Border Crossing Office, said that in relation to this international gate, in case Vietnam was disturbed or blocked from importing goods, he and Mr. Keo Chea immediately intervened to mediate. However, the Vietnamese side to facilitate the agriculture of our people down quickly, and if the Vietnamese side is closed, please inform in advance so that people do not come to block rice.
He said that lately, there are a lot of rice trucks coming and going, so he is very busy in organizing the force to guide them to understand each other in order to avoid congestion, not to stop on the bridge. Do not drive too close to the edge of the road for fear of breaking the road and educate them about hygiene to protect Kovid 19.
