Court sentences woman to 12 years in prison for stabbing 5-year-old girl in the face
Phnom Penh Municipal Court has sentenced a woman to 12 years in prison for brutally stabbing a 5-year-old girl in the face of Chhouk Va 2 in Borey Phop Thmey, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Sen Chey. Torture and cruelty are aggravated. This is according to a court official who told Fresh News on the afternoon of November 25, 2020.
On the morning of November 25, 2020, the President of the Trial Chamber of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court held a hearing to announce the verdict in the case of 43-year-old Liu Bunthoeun, who used a knife to operate on a child. The victim was angry when the boy threw a stone, causing her son to break his head. The Trial Chamber sentenced the woman to 12 years in prison.
It should be noted that Mr. Sok Keo Bandith, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, on July 18, 2020, decided to charge the brutal woman named Liv Bunthoeun, 43 years old, who used a knife to cut the face of a 5-year-old girl for committing the crime. Cruelty and torture are aggravated under Article 211 of the Penal Code.
Article 211 of the Penal Code states that torture and aggravated assault involving a victim is punishable by 10 to 20 years in prison if the offense is committed:
Liu Bunthoeun was arrested by police and taken for questioning on July 16, 2020, and sent to court on the afternoon of July 17, 2020, after being stabbed in the face and other places. Another of a 5-year-old girl named Las Mavilia.
The woman above is located at No. 6, Street 26, Borey Phop Thmey, Chhouk Va 2, in the village of Tek Panho, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Sen Chey. The victim, a 5-year-old girl named Las Mavilia, lives at No. 18, Street 20, Borey Phop Thmey, Chhouk Va 2, Tek Panha Village, Sangkat Samrong Krom.
The cause of the atrocity came after the woman became angry with the victim, injuring her two-year-old son during a quarrel.
