Samdech Techo Hun Sen: The King of Cambodia is a King with a Great Humanitarian Heart (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, on November 25, 2020, said that His Majesty the King The Khmer king is the poorest king in the world, but he is a king with a great humanitarian spirit for the Cambodian people to follow.
This statement was made on the occasion of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's meeting and review of the work of "Samdech Techo Sen Volunteer Lawyer" at the Peace Palace this morning, November 25, 2020.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "The poorest king in the world is the King of Cambodia, but he is also a humane king for the people. "Our civil servants follow the example."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the King is a leader in donating royal property to the Royal Government of Cambodia to fight against the Kovid 19 virus (COVID-19).
Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued that after the King's gift, a number of tycoons joined in, which increased the budget to more than 19 million dollars and spent 11 million dollars, the remaining 8 million dollars are being Order more equipment to fight Kovid-19.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also said that in some countries, the president issued a decree to cut the salaries of civil servants, but for Cambodia, just announced immediately, tens of thousands of Cambodian officials have contributed, while so far a total of about 42 billion riels. Equivalent to more than 10 million dollars.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed that the money received from the donations of all Cambodian civil servants has not been used yet.
Unable to kill Cambodia, Cambodia was able to successfully control the spread of Kovid 19 and was named the No. 1 country in Asia and the No. 3 country in the world for best control and response to Kovid 19. As for the EBA, despite losing 20 percent, Cambodia's exports are still growing well.
According to figures from the General Department of Customs and Excise of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Cambodia's export trade volume in the first nine months of 2020 will be about 14.1 billion US dollars, compared to the first nine months of 2019. 20.07%.
The Prime Minister also stated that Cambodia is not a rich country, but to lead and manage the country is to act like a housewife who has a very clear management system, making it a mechanism for a single commander-in-chief, a single chief of staff, a success of the version. Cambodia's financial system profile.
Please be informed that Cambodia has not yet died of Kovid 19 disease. As of November 25, 2020, a total of 307 cases of 19 Kovid have been found in Cambodia, of which 298 have been cured and nine are being treated in hospitals.
As for the EBA, the European Union decided on August 12, 2020 to remove the Cambodian preferential tariff system under the "Everything But Arms (EBA)" program, with a tariff of about 20 percent on Cambodian goods. It is estimated that the cut in parts of the preferential tariff system is worth more than 100 million US dollars on 40 products.
