Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Cambodia's economy will recover in 2021, so far tax collection has reached 4,500 million dollars (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on 25 This November 2020, he expressed the hope that the Cambodian economy will recover in 2021, while in 2020, the Cambodian economy will decline to negative points due to the Kovid 19 crisis.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that although in 2020, the Cambodian economy will be negative due to the crisis of Kovid 19, but the volume of Cambodia's exports increased by 18 percent.
In the first eight months of this year, Cambodia's exports reached 11.714 billion US dollars, an increase of 18 percent. This is according to the report of the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
Once again, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also asked for the understanding of all types of civil servants of the Armed Forces that in 2021 the Royal Government can not increase salaries, keeping the same rate as in 2020. But in 2021, the Royal Government will maintain a pension increase for veterans and previous retirees so that the pension will be similar to those of new retirees.
Although the Cambodian economy will shrink below zero in 2020, in 2021, the two international institutions forecast that Cambodia's economy will recover, with the World Bank predicting that the Cambodian economy will grow by 4.3 percent and the ADB Cambodia will grow by 5.9 percent. Kampot Provincial Council Continues to Organize Dissemination and Consultation Forum in Angkor Chey and Banteay Meas Districts
(Kampot): Mr. Chheng Phalla, Chairman of Kampot Provincial Council and Mr. Chiao Tai, Provincial Governor, on November 24, 2020, continued to organize outreach and consultation for the third mandate Provincial Council 2020 in Angkor Chey and Banteay Meas districts. With the participation of 270 stakeholders in Angkor Chey and 87 in Banteay Meas.
The forum aims to create a culture of democratic dialogue and accountability through:
