Through these humanitarian gestures, Samdech Techo said, "Cambodia is small but still generous." A muscle sports instructor was abducted by a group of thieves on a motorcycle while teaching students in Ang Snoul district, Kandal province, 8 suspects were arrested
(Kandal): A muscle sports instructor was abducted by a group of thieves on a motorcycle after leaving a gym in Phnom Penh to return to Kampong Speu province. This incident happened on November 24, 2020 at the point of National Road No. 4, Tonleab Khpos Tbong Village, Damnak Ampil Commune, Ang Snoul District, Kandal Province.
According to the report of Kandal Provincial Police, which was received by Fresh News on the afternoon of November 25, 2020, the victim was Isa, 27 years old, a Khmer Muslim, a muscle sports trainer in Trapeang Preah village, Kandol Doum commune. Chbar Morn City, Kampong Speu Province.
Police confirmed that before the incident, the victim was riding a motorcycle from the gym in Phnom Penh to a house in Kampong Speu province, when the scene suddenly a group of 9 suspects riding three motorcycles. Came to hit the victim with a helmet on his head, causing him to fall on the national road.
At that time, the suspects were intimidating the victim to take the motorcycle, suddenly saw the police patrolling, the suspect rode the motorcycle to the east on Route 4, and the police chased and hid each other Detain the group of suspects at once.
According to the confession, the suspect, Heng Rayuth, confessed that he and his accomplices had been waiting for an electric shock on National Road 4, and only then did the victim, who was riding a motorcycle from the east, chase him on a motorcycle. From behind and hit the victim and threatened to take the motorcycle for sure. The suspects are now being trained to build a case to be sent to proceed with the procedure.
