This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen met with "Samdech Techo Sen Volunteer Lawyer"
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on November 25, 2020, met with and inspected the work of "Samdech Techo Sen Volunteer Lawyer". The ceremony will take place at the Peace Palace.
In addition to assisting in the resolution and defense of the "Volunteer Lawyer Samdech Techo Sen", he also does social and humanitarian work. For example, in collaboration with the Siem Reap Provincial Administration, the Apsara Authority, the Court of First Instance, and the Siem Reap and Banteay Meanchey Provincial Prosecutors, planted saplings in the southern part of the Angkor Thom temple complex.
"Samdech Techo Sen Volunteer Lawyer" also provided equipment, food and money to the people affected by the fire, wind, floods, and the elderly widows who have a poor life and collected money from Member to the Royal Government in the campaign to prevent and fight against Kovid 19 virus.
According to the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, during the video meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Nguyen Suon Fuc discussed ways and means to further promote bilateral relations and exchange views on regional and global issues. His concerns and interests include cooperation in the fight against Kovid-19.
The Prime Minister congratulated Vietnam on the successful outcome of the 37th ASEAN Summit and related summits, especially the signing of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP).
The two Prime Ministers expressed their satisfaction with the excellent development of all-round cooperation between Cambodia and Vietnam in recent years and agreed to strengthen and expand the existing cooperation to expand and deepen in The spirit of good neighborliness, traditional friendship, all-round cooperation and long-term stability.
The two leaders reaffirmed joint efforts to strengthen bilateral cooperation in defense and security in order to ensure security and order in the border area.
The two leaders noted with satisfaction that Cambodia and Vietnam had successfully controlled the spread of the virus-19 epidemic.
The Prime Minister thanked the Vietnamese government for providing medical equipment to Cambodia to fight Kovid-19 and facilitating the return of hundreds of Cambodian students to study in Vietnam. The Vietnamese Prime Minister praised the Royal Government of Cambodia for maintaining economic and social stability during the global epidemic.
The two Prime Ministers applauded the ratification of the Supplementary Treaty on the 1985 State Boundary Treaty and the 2005 Supplementary Treaty between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Socialist Republic of Vietnam, as well as the Protocol on Boundary Demarcation and Border Posting. Land between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Socialist Republic of Vietnam in 2019.
The two prime ministers also stressed the importance of exchanging maps of the border between Cambodia and Vietnam. The two sides agreed to expedite the procedure to change the instrument of ratification of the Supplementary Treaty and the 2019 Protocol as soon as possible.
The two leaders also pledged to resolve the remaining 16% of the border in order to turn the Cambodia-Vietnam border into a border of peace, stability, cooperation and development. The two leaders highlighted the importance of the 18th Ministerial Meeting of the Cambodia-Vietnam Joint Commission, which is scheduled to take place on December 22, 2020 in Bavet, Svay Rieng Province, Cambodia.
