The Senior Minister emphasized this at the 26th ASEAN Transport Ministers' Meeting via video on November 24, 2020.
During the meeting, the Senior Minister stated that Cambodia has cooperated systematically and hierarchically, both public and private administrations, to explore all procedures, mechanisms, strategies and measures to prevent and curb the spread of Kovid 19 virus under the guidance of the Health Organization. World and the Ministry of Health of Cambodia.
"As a result, Cambodia has no community outbreaks and no 19 people have died of Kovid, and no country or region has been declared a state of emergency. However, Cambodia still adheres to the preventive measures of the Ministry of Health of Cambodia, as well as the prevention measures of the World Health Organization very strictly. The Senior Minister underlined to the ASEAN Transport Minister.
The senior minister also said that the Kovid 19 crisis did not hinder the construction of transport infrastructure. In fact, the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway, Sihanoukville Deep Sea Port, as well as other road and bridge infrastructure are still under normal construction, but both workers and engineers must adhere to preventive measures.
