General knowledge: The apartheid war or the Civil War in the United States 1860-1865
(USA): Between 1860 and 1865, the United States waged a major civil war between the northern and southern states in an attempt to divide the United States due to differences over the issue. Abolish slavery as this war has been dubbed the "separatist war."
Although the United States is a single federal state, it has geographically contrasting northern and southern regions. In the north, which has 23 states, is an industrial center rich in factories, enterprises, large cities, schools from primary to college, highways, labyrinths, populations, and also rich cultural centers.
The southern state, which has 11 states, is an agricultural area rich in corn and cotton. People live in rural areas, are not rich in big cities, and even lack roads. The plantation owners in the south relied on black slave labor. They are used like animals to work day and night, with almost no rest.
The southern state has a population of only 9.5 million, of which up to 5 million are black. The northern states have a population of 22 million and are more economically developed than the southern states. The conflict between the two states formed a civil war that erupted on April 6, 1860. The war lasted for five years, until 1865, when the southern states agreed to surrender.
Spokesman for the General Commission: On November 24, another 1,103 vehicles were inspected and fined
(Phnom Penh): On November 24, 2020, the traffic police throughout Cambodia inspected and fined a total of 1,103 vehicles, including 802 motorcycles and 301 cars. This was confirmed by Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and spokesman for the National Police.
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, during the 208 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to November 24, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and A total of 223,527 vehicles were fined, including 165,102 motorcycles and 58,425 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun continued that for the past 208 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
It should be noted that for November 24, 2020, there were 9 traffic accidents throughout Cambodia, in which 6 people were killed and 15 people were injured (08 people were seriously injured).
