Cambodian Human Rights Masters: Preparation of Dissemination of UPR Report and Recommendation Round 3 at Local Level Demonstrates the Royal Government of Cambodia's Will to Work on Human Rights
(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Keo Remy, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, stated that the acceptance of the UN UPR Recommendation shows the will of the Royal Government of Cambodia led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen in Protection and promotion of human rights.
"The adoption of the UPR Recommendation demonstrates the Royal Government's commitment to the protection and promotion of human rights, and the Royal Government needs to disseminate the UPR Recommendations at the national and sub-national levels," he said. "National, so that all relevant ministries, departments and institutions implement this recommendation to improve the field of human rights."
The purpose of this workshop is to disseminate the UPR report and the UPR recommendations that Cambodia accepts. In addition, Cambodia passed the UPR report on January 30, 2019, with 73 countries participating and 198 recommendations, with Cambodia accepting 173 recommendations and making 25 remarks.
Mr. Keo Remy, Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, stated that the UPR Report is a report on the human rights situation of the member states of the United Nations, and that each State has an obligation to defend the report. Every four or five years, Cambodia defended its first report in 2009, its second in 2014 and its third in 2019.
Mr. Keo Remy said that under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Royal Government has paid great attention to the protection as well as the promotion of human rights and has improved the human rights situation with recognition and evaluation. High for Cambodia. For example, the adoption of eight out of nine conventions and conventions that Cambodia has adopted and is one of the leading countries in the ASEAN region.
At the same time, Mr. Keo Remy stated that the Royal Government, all relevant ministries and institutions have worked together to respect the rights and improve the human rights situation, in addition, Cambodia will have a fourth round report in 2024. This is to submit to the United Nations as well.
According to Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, the workshop was organized to disseminate information to provincial leaders, municipalities, departments, units around the province, the Armed Forces, judges, representatives of the Prosecution, Prisons, and spokespersons for each unit. Of the National Report on the Global Review of the National Report, especially the Royal Government's efforts to improve the human rights situation in all areas of Cambodia.
It should be noted that in this workshop, three topics were also mentioned, including the first topic: UPR report, the audit report, the second topic: the content of the UPR report and the third topic: The defense of the UPR report at the United Nations and the adoption of the third round of recommendations.
Senior Minister Kun Kim emphasized this during a visit to inspect the re-farming of farmers in Kampong Cham and Kratie provinces on November 24, 2020.
In recent weeks, farmers affected by the recent floods have been busy cultivating their crops.
In order to intervene and meet the needs of farmers on the re-cultivation of rice, Senior Minister Kun Kim, on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's staff, has been inspecting the rice fields since November 20. The Senior Minister visited Battambang, Banteay Meanchey, Pursat, Kampong Thom, Kampong Cham and Kratie provinces.
On November 24, 2020, Senior Minister Kun Kim inspected the re-farming of farmers in Kratie province. During his visit to Kratie province to inspect rice farming, Senior Minister Kun Kim expressed his pleasure to see that farmers are busy cultivating crops again, as Samdech Techo wants to see.
In a conversation with farmers in the rice fields, the Senior Minister told the farmers that the work of farmers to grow crops after the floods recede is the work that the Prime Minister pays the highest attention. Because this replanting helps ensure food security and also helps solve difficulties in people's lives.
The Senior Minister added that due to this careful attention, Samdech has urgently taken action on the re-cultivation work, including the management of rice seeds, the arrangement of irrigation water supply systems and the preparation of transportation systems.
Senior Minister Kun Kim emphasized that "the management of work and the issuance of quick and rigorous regulations as a leader have a clear understanding of Samdech Techo's farming work and make the work of growing crops and farming of our farmers achieved quickly." "
At the same time, Senior Minister Kun Kim also praised all relevant authorities for paying attention and responding quickly to facilitate the cultivation of farmers. However, the senior minister reminded the authorities to continue to pay more attention, especially to the water system, to ensure that the re-cultivation is as expected.
It should be noted that the recent floods have affected tens of thousands of hectares of rice fields. More than 6,000 tons of non-seasonal light rice varieties have been distributed to farmers for replanting.
According to Senior Minister Kun Kim, more than 62% of the cultivable land in Battambang, Banteay Meanchey, Pursat, Kampong Thom, Kampong Cham and Kratie provinces have been plowed and sown.
