Angkor Residents Describe Procedure for New House Construction
(Siem Reap): The construction of houses in the Angkor resort area must be carried out in accordance with the conditions set by the law governed by the APSARA Authority in order to preserve the cultural landscape, Khmer identity, archeology must be protected and avoid any destruction in the World Heritage Site. .
A resident of O Toteung village, Mr. Suong Dany said that he applied for a building permit through the village chief and there was no problem because he attached the required documents. Not only that, APSARA Authority also facilitated the technical design and style of Khmer house for him. There was no payment for the application, and he complied with the request, including the style of the house and the size of the fence.
Mr. Dany also instructed all the people in Angkor Park before building a house to build something must comply with the law, have enough documents and in accordance with the conditions, it is not difficult to apply for construction and avoid arbitrary theft Alone that affects the value of Angkor resort and self-interest.
Mr. Khieu Vichet, Technical Officer of the Department of Land Management and Housing Management in Angkor area, confirmed that if people want to apply for the construction of small houses and other requests can come to the six gates of APSARA Authority. There are staff officers on duty to advise on the documents to be attached, such as legal land title, family book, birth certificate, land title and identity card.
Upon receipt of the permit, the team will inspect the site in person, including monitoring the construction activities for accuracy or deviation from the requested conditions. In the case of citizens who adhere to the principles of applying for the APSARA Authority will have a letter of commendation for them to contribute to raising the value of the Angkor area, and all applications are free of charge.
General Knowledge: The Birth of the State of Singapore and Major Trade Ports in Southeast Asia
The seizure of international seaports and the most important international trade port in Southeast Asia has contributed to the development of this country with a total area of 725.7 square kilometers.
How long has this economic dragon country been born and established an international trade port?
The word Singbora is derived from the Sanskrit word Singha plus Bora. The word lion or lion means lion, but people believe that the lion is more powerful than all the quadrupeds, which in Khmer we call Reachsey, and the word Bora or Borey means city. Therefore, the word Singapore means the city of the lion.
Following the acquisition of the island of Singapore, the United Kingdom became the sole owner of the Strait of Malacca. Until 1830, Singapore became one of the major international trade ports in Southeast Asia.
The reason why Singapore has become such a potential multi-purpose area is because the location has three unique features:
First, a good geographical location, which is a crossroads for maritime links between China, India and Europe.
Second, it is a free international port, unlike the port of Patavia in Indonesia and the Philippines, which is a domestic port and requires additional taxes.
Third, to fully serve the British economy, the first industrial growth in the 19th century.
