(Kampot): The Ministry of Economy and Finance has opened a training course on "State Asset Management Procedures and Non-Tax Revenue Management" for target trainees who are civil servants in charge of work related to state property management and revenue management. Non-tax of departments, specialized units and municipal administrations of Kampot province. The training course was held on November 23, 2020 at Kampot Diamond Hotel.
The purpose of this training is to strengthen the capacity and increase the awareness of civil servants to contribute to the promotion of transparency, accountability, efficiency and effectiveness of the management of state assets and non-tax revenues in accordance with technical principles and in accordance with the law. Public financial system and within the framework of the Royal Government's public financial management reform program.
The opening ceremony was presided over by Mr. Pich Sambath, Representative of Dr. Hean Sahip, Secretary of State and Chairman of the Capacity Building Working Group of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and attended by Mr. Has Sobin, Deputy Governor of Kampot Province. Ministry of Economy and Finance, Department of Economy and Finance, Kampot, Kep, Takeo and Sihanoukville Provinces, trainers and trainees, a total of 70 participants.
