(Kampong Chhnang): A family living in Dangkhao Mao village, Chak commune, Baribo district, Kampong Chhnang province has asked the provincial court to help his family to expedite the settlement of traffic accident cases that the parties did not come to solve by delaying More than eight months ago, while his family has not received any compensation yet.
The mother and brother of the deceased and her children, including the mother and grandmother, raised their hands to the relevant authorities as well as the judiciary, please summon the representative of the above bus company to work with his family. As soon as the daughter and sister died, the family borrowed money to pay for the seven-day funeral, which cost a lot of money.
As a result, he did not have the money to pay them back, hoping to rely on the bus company to guarantee that he would be able to pay off some of his debts, but to this day, company representatives have not come to deal with his family. No. On the other hand, today he has no business.
She said that in the beginning she went to work in a garment factory, but since her sister died, all the burden fell on her to stay at home to take care of her mother-in-law, who was physically ill and could not get out of bed. She also raised some chickens, sold some cricket bulbs to take care of her mother, and settled some of her family's debts, while her husband now works in a factory with them.
Separately, Mr. Chea Saren, clerk of the judge of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court, also said that the case of the traffic accident that caused the death of two people above, the case has reached the judge and has just received. Ministry of Environment spokesman encourages local authorities and citizens to increase tree planting in public places to increase greenery and improve air quality
Mr. Net Pheaktra's encouragement to increase tree planting was held on November 23, 2020 on the occasion of the National Environmental Sanitation Day with the participation of Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, government officials, students, and law enforcement forces. Symbolic trees are planted on the campus of Preah Vihear Provincial Hall.
Secretary of State Net Pheaktra said that forests play an important role in protecting the ecosystem we need to grow in addition to the natural wood that Cambodia has.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that currently Cambodia's forest cover is more than 8.5 million hectares, equivalent to 46.86% of the total land area of Cambodia. The forest area under the protection and conservation by the Ministry of Environment is about 7.3 million hectares, divided into 65 protected areas, including national parks, wildlife sanctuaries, landscape protection areas, multi-use areas and conservation corridors. Biodiversity.
The Secretary of State said that when towns and villages are green, people will play an important role in improving fresh air, maintaining soil and groundwater quality and as part of adaptation to climate change. Climate change.
In addition, Mr. Neth Pheaktra continued to encourage people to manage and store properly generated waste, both waste from daily use and waste in the environment, by properly sorting waste according to techniques and packaging. Store properly.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra emphasized that both increasing greenery in the community by planting trees and cleaning the environment regularly will make our villages, communities and cities have a clean, hygienic environment and provide a comfortable living and Make our community healthy, which is in line with the motto of the celebration of the National Environmental Sanitation Day, November 23, 2020, "Good Environmental Sanitation, Good Community Health".
On the occasion of the National Environmental Sanitation Day, Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, reminded and urged public and private institutions, authorities at all levels, people to participate in cleaning and maintaining the environment in their localities. He also urged local authorities and relevant institutions to educate people about the proper management of garbage and solid waste.
At the same time, Mr. Chuob Baris, Director General of the General Department of Environmental Knowledge and Information, thanked the leaders and civil servants of the Ministry of Environment, especially the authorities and civil servants of Preah Vihear Province, youth, students around the province who always support all environmental movements. .
He hopes that the celebration of this day will be the driving force behind the initiation of environmental friendly action from individuals to be responsible for the storage of waste and not to throw it in public places. Affect the beauty of the whole country and its own dignity.
Mr. Chuob Paris also gave some recommendations to take care of the environment, including: regular personal hygiene, keep garbage in the bin, love to protect and plant trees.
