(Preah Vihear): A suspect was arrested immediately after he acted with a machete on the victim, causing his death on the spot.
This case happened at 1:30 pm on November 23, 2020 at the army farm in Rong Roeung 4 village, Moratok commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province.
This morning, the suspect was identified as Sarath Sarith, a 27-year-old farmer from Poy Ta Sek village, Boeung Pring commune, Thmor Koul district. Battambang Province. The victim is named Ra Beb, male, 24 years old, farmer, his hometown is Trapeang Krasaing village, Sre Noi commune, Varin district, Siem Reap province.
Currently, the suspect and the victim are temporarily staying in the commune where the incident took place.
The district inspector said that before the incident, the suspect and the victim had a verbal conflict with each other in the drinking circle since noon. At night, the conflict continued and the victim kept saying words to the suspect, making the suspect unable to control his anger, so he grabbed a knife and stabbed the victim in the neck and ears, causing his immediate death. At the scene.
Lt. Col. O Seng said that after the operation, the suspect intended to escape, but under the command and guidance of Major General Suos Sok Dara, Preah Vihear Provincial Police Commissioner, the district police force, in cooperation with the 9th Intervention Brigade, detained The suspect was arrested overnight and brought to the district inspector to build a case to be sent to the provincial police commission in accordance with legal procedures.
