Announcing the position of Chief of Staff of the Army, Lt. Gen. Khem Chea Sa Khoeun, replacing General Chea Saran, who has been appointed Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has issued a sub-decree appointing Lt. Gen. Khem Chea Sakhoeun ID 00116 as Deputy Commander and Chief of Staff of the Army Command to replace General Chea Saran. Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense.
The inauguration ceremony took place this morning, November 23, 2020, at the Army Command under the chairmanship of General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
In the welcoming report, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander-in-Chief and Commander-in-Chief of the Army, highlighted the progress in all areas of the Army Command, including ownership, core duties, training, participation in social development, including cooperation. Maintain security, order and peacekeeping, political stability.
During the talk, General Vong Pisen expressed his appreciation and appreciation to the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) for all types of troops who have paid attention to fulfilling their roles and responsibilities in defending the territorial integrity, especially deepening the process of reforming the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces. Overall) and in particular, the Army Command, which has overcome all obstacles and achieved proud results.
General Vong Pisen congratulated and highly appreciated the work of Lt. Gen. Khem Chea Sakhoeun, who has worked hard in the past to serve the country and instructed him to work hard as the Chief of Staff of the Army. Land, capacity building, morality, virtue, sharing knowledge and experience to officers, taking turns and strengthening internal unity.
In addition, the Commander-in-Chief instructed the officers and officers of the Army Command to continue to enforce the law, the general rules and regulations of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, and strictly abide by the 10 provisions of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Speaking on the occasion of celebrating the 20th anniversary of the Army's birthday (January 24, 2019).
At the same time, it is necessary to participate in the protection of peace at all costs, and to pay attention to building human resources for future sources, including proper review, promotion, appropriate positions according to the position, law, statute of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces. And promote good management of state property in the units.
The inauguration ceremony of the Chief of Army Staff ended after Lt. Gen. Khem Chea Sakhoeun made a commitment and the delegation handed over a bouquet of flowers and souvenirs to a former senior officer of the Army Command, who was promoted. Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of National Defense. "Run for charity with Say" raised more than $ 400,000 and helped Angkor Children's Hospital
Angkor Hospital for Children is a hospital that has been on a mission to save the lives of Cambodian children free of charge since 1999. In 2020, due to the outbreak of Kovid 19, the hospital ran short of funds in its operations.
Tep Navy, Executive Director of Angkor Hospital for Children in Siem Reap, said that the hospital's operations depend entirely on foreign and local charitable funds. The Kovid 19 crisis has reduced the hospital's annual budget from $ 6.5 million to just $ 5.9 million for 2020.
Of that amount, about $ 3.3 million has been pledged by philanthropists and foreign fundraisers. The remaining $ 3 million to support the operation requires the hospital to seek donations from local philanthropists.
To raise funds for the Cambodian children's life-saving process, the hospital has set up several charitable programs. At the same time, the hospital also set up another fundraising program called "Run for Charity with Say", hoping to raise additional funds to support the operation of Angkor Hospital for Children.
"Run for Charity with Say" is a project to provide a positive example in the community, initiated by Say, a singer who loves to run. This program is to celebrate the 30th anniversary and to give back to the society by running around the country to raise funds to help children at Angkor Hospital for Children.
The fundraiser is not only about fundraising, but also about the meaning and goals that Say wants to focus on helping children and their future.
Determined to run around Cambodia to raise funds to support Angkor Say Children's Hospital, running for 99 days on the road and running a distance of about 40 kilometers per day. Say started to run away from Phnom Penh on October 6 and is scheduled to end on January 13, 2021.
The owner of the song "Passionate" Mr. Say said that although the run went through many obstacles and difficulties, he was happy to see the generous participation of enthusiasts. According to Mr. Say, the budget received from this philanthropist exceeded the expected plan.
However, Say continues to call on philanthropists to donate as much money as possible to support the operation of Angkor Hospital for Children as well as save Cambodian children from various diseases.
Say's humanitarian run is a good example for young people because young people are an important pillar of society as a whole. It is very important that every citizen in the society participates in sharing problems, whether small or large, to maintain unity for the common good.
This is a small hope and support for the younger generation, especially to ensure that children have the same opportunity to grow up healthy and become good human resources for the development of the nation.
