Cambodia-Singapore vows to continue to expand Cambodia's employment and human resource training
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia-Singapore is strongly committed to expanding Cambodia's employment and training of human resources to better respond to the rapid development of technology in the region and the world.
This sharp commitment was made during the farewell meeting of Mr. Michael Tan (Singapore) Ambassador of Singapore to Cambodia between Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training on the morning of 23 November. 2020 at the office of the Ministry of Labor.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng spoke about the progress of diplomatic relations and various fields, especially the field of employment and vocational training between Cambodia and Singapore during the mission of Mr. Michael Tan, which has contributed significantly to the development of Cambodia.
Minister Ith Sam Heng's next proposal is related to the Technical and Vocational Training (TVET) sector, which is the key to the country's development, especially Cambodia needs qualified human resources, and Singapore has played a significant role in promoting On this work. At the same time, Cambodia also intends to continue cooperation with Singapore and hopes that Singapore will continue to share more experiences with Cambodia.
The Ambassador of Singapore highlighted the efforts of the Government and the Embassy of Singapore in Cambodia in providing technical and vocational training to Cambodian trainees. He mentioned that Cambodian trainees like to study in the workplace, which is a special point in developing their skills to be better.
He added that Singapore ranks second in terms of investment in Cambodia, and he, as an ambassador, always urges companies to continue to take responsibility for their investment in Cambodia. According to the laws and regulations, as well as to participate in the training of labor skills of Cambodian workers so that they get a suitable skill for better livelihood.
The Ambassador also commended the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, where one of the leaders, Mr. Heng Sour, was appointed as a consultant to the Regional Center for the Future of Work for a two-year term from September. 2020 to August 2022 to share experiences and knowledge that are valuable for the development of the labor sector, especially in occupational safety and health.
Mr. Michael Tan confirmed that he accepted the requests of Mr. Ith Sam Heng to inform the Government of Singapore to consider and continue to cooperate better.
