Dr. Steng Sokhom: Education Reform Remains the Core of the Royal Government's Fourth Rectangular Strategy
(Prey Veng): Dr. Steung Sokhom, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the National Task Force for Kamchay Mear District, Prey Veng Province, stated that education reform remains at the core of the fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategy, which defines resource development. People are the first priority.
He added that Cambodia needs human resources with deep knowledge and clear skills to serve the economic structure to promote economic diversification, run through the deep structural changes of the world and make Cambodia more competitive.
Dr. Steng Sokhom said this at the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of a 6-room school building in Chhor Kindergarten in Kranhung commune, Kamchay Mear district, Prey Veng province, which was a precious gift from Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior. And Lok Chumteav on November 21, 2020.
During the ceremony, the Chairman of the National Working Group explained why the Royal Government gives priority to human resource development? Because the development of a society, a nation needs human resources.
He added that the education sector has been expanding from urban to rural areas to provide opportunities for all Cambodians to receive an education. Education for all, with at least nine years of free basic education in accordance with the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The Royal Government is still focused on finding and recruiting children for everyone, no matter where they are or what their circumstances are. In the future, the Royal Government will continue to address the challenges of the education sector, to ensure a balance between strengthening the quality of education and expanding the volume, as well as promoting lifelong learning, because learning is a job. The end.
At the same time, the Chairman of the National Working Group also expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Lok Chumteav for donating their own funds to build many social achievements in Kamchay Mear District and Provide wise ideas to lead work in Prey Veng.
Mr. Seng Sokhom told the people, teachers who participated in the program that the help of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng in the construction of kindergartens as well as primary schools here, Samdech has no desire for anything in return. No, I just want to see the children of the people go to school.
At present, the kindergarten has 7 teachers and 140 students. Mr. Neth Pheaktra: Every year, Cambodia produces about 4 million tons of garbage, 65% of which is organic waste.
