Senior Minister Kun Kim: Help restore the livelihood and cultivation of the people after the flood as a strict order of Samdech Techo (Video inside) (Battambang): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, is the staff of Samdech Techo Hun Sen On the morning of November 21, 2020, on the work of the disaster, they went to inspect the rice cultivation of the people after the flood receded.
Today, the Senior Minister visited the rice farming activities of the people in Battambang and Banteay Meanchey provinces. The two provinces were severely flooded by floods, with many hectares of rice and other crops damaged.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Commander-in-Chief of the Disaster Battlefield, has set out urgent measures to save lives and farm as well as plant crops for the people after the water recedes.
In order to ensure the restoration of people's livelihood and cultivation, Samdech Techo has issued orders to three main ministries, including the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, the Ministry of Water Resources and the Ministry of Development. Distribute rice seeds, crop seeds, repair irrigation systems, canals and roads in rural areas.
As of November 15, about 6,000 tons of rice seeds and nearly 560,000 packages of mixed crops were distributed to farmers to replant after the floods receded. Currently, farmers are busy with their cultivation.
According to the report of the National Committee for Disaster Management, the rehabilitation work in Battambang and Banteay Meanchey provinces has achieved more than 50% of the results. In Battambang province, 5,831 hectares were cultivated on 10,500 hectares of rehabilitated land.
In Banteay Meanchey province, 5,113 hectares were damaged, a total of 11,169 hectares were recoverable.
The relevant authorities have been paying close attention to the people's replanting and have put in place measures to intervene in their cultivation. During the visit to inspect the replanting of farmers, Senior Minister Kun Kim stated that helping the farmers to replant effectively is a strict order of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, which was introduced to the relevant authorities. All.
"Samdech Techo Hun Sen has paid great attention to the replanting of the people. Post-flood cultivation is essential to address food and livelihood issues for affected people. "Rescueing people from the floods is important, but it is even more important to restore people's livelihoods and crops after the flood." This was confirmed by Senior Minister Kun Kim.
As the eyes and nose of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Senior Minister Kun Kim further appealed to the relevant authorities, especially in the flooded provinces, to increase their attention and intervene in the cultivation of farmers.
From the fields that are being replanted, the people expressed their great pleasure for the attention and help to promote the replanting from the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia and relevant officials. They said that the provision of rice seeds and water solutions from Samdech Techo Hun Sen has enabled the resumption of farming.
Notably, in the fields where the water has just receded, farmers have been busy plowing and replanting.
