(Phnom Penh): Cambodian Young Engineers Mr. Neou Dina, President of the Cambodian Young Engineers of the Board of Engineers of Cambodia, has been elected Vice President of the ASEAN Young Engineers Council, a demonstration of the value and confidence in the capabilities of young Cambodian engineers.
The selection was made at the 38th ASEAN Engineering Meeting on November 20, 2020. Mr. Neou Dina led the young Cambodian engineers to participate in this meeting through the video system. The meeting was attended by the chairmen and representatives of young engineers from ASEAN countries as well as the ASEAN Secretariat of Young Engineers.
The meeting also aims to contribute to the improvement of the engineering profession, strengthen the professional capacity of all technical skills and expand human resources in line with current and future social needs, especially Industry 4.0 and ensure the engineering profession. High quality, efficiency, safety, stability and responsibility.
The meeting also aims to strengthen ASEAN-international cooperation and relations, and to recognize the quality of engineering education in the region and to train vocational skills for national and international professional engineers.
As a result, the meeting approved the draft report of the 27th ASEAN Young Engineers Council Meeting to submit to the ASEAN Engineering Council for review and approval and to continue to review the procedures and procedures for competency competition in the field of engineering of young engineers to Review and decide to award medals and certificates to a young engineer every year for each country.
The meeting also agreed to encourage and encourage as well as provide opportunities and resources for young engineers in the region to participate in the ASEAN Young Engineers Meeting and agreed to nominate Mr. Neou Dina, President of the Young Engineers of Cambodia as Vice Chairman of the ASEAN Young Engineers Council.
