Officials find banned chemicals in Siem Reap's Svay Leu market, experts warn distributors
(Siem Reap): CPP Branch Officer of Siem Reap Province, led by Mr. Khieu Panhavath, Branch Manager of CPP In cooperation with the officials of the Provincial Department of Commerce and local authorities, on the morning of November 20, 2020, inspected the quality of food, which is unpackaged and pre-packaged food in Svay Leu market, Svay Leu district, Siem Reap province, including at the booths and depots. Distribute 3 other large packaging goods located in the above district.
Mr. Khieu Panhavath said that the purpose of monitoring food activities, officials focus on finding banned chemicals that can be present in any food by using on-site test kits as well as More non-compliance that does not respond to food safety.
In fact, experts tested 13 different samples and as a result, out of 13 samples, one was found to contain banned chemicals and 152 bottles of non-compliance with food safety. The confiscated goods were recorded and confiscated, including a warning letter to the distributor, and sent to the branch for safekeeping.
Mr. Khieu Panhavad added that Svay Leu district has the highest number of cases of food poisoning in recent months.
