Philippines to import more rice by 2021 as typhoons devastate crops (Video inside) (Manila): A senior Philippine official said on Thursday that the Philippines will import more rice this year The latter to fill the void of damage caused by the typhoon to its agricultural output. This is according to a release by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Thursday afternoon, November 19, 2020.
Statistics show that the Philippines, with a total population of nearly 110 million, will import about 7-14% of its total annual rice needs, in line with the amount of damage caused by the typhoon in 2020. According to the Philippine Ministry of Agriculture, the average Filipino needs nearly 120 kilograms of rice per person for the whole year.
