133 Troops Strengthened in Disaster Relief
(Phnom Penh): About 133 troops from 4 units have successfully completed the Disaster Relief Training after 3 months of training.
The Closing Ceremony of Disaster Relief Training was held on Thursday, November 19, 2020 in Tonle Village, Pean Longvek Village, Kampong Loung Commune, Ponhea Leu District, Kandal Province, chaired by Lt. Gen. Chan Lumphat, Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management. Disaster Represents Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management.
The ceremony was also attended by Lt. Gen. Chap Pheakdey, Deputy Commander of the Army and Commander of the Special Forces Command, as well as Deputy Commanders from other relevant units.
According to the report, the course trains on opening and repairing equipment, as well as other rescue work skills. The training includes both theoretical and practical training, including relief work in the recent floods.
Lt. Gen. Chan Lumphat expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the efforts of the leaders at all levels in the Special Forces Command, who have worked together as a whole to achieve common tasks. And an annual training plan.
The lieutenant general also mentioned that disasters are a global problem that no country can avoid. In addition, countries around the world are very concerned about climate change and the potential for more catastrophic disasters.
Lt. Gen. Chan Lumphat also highlighted the recent floods in Cambodia. Mr. Chan Lumphat said that in this disaster, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia and the Commander-in-Chief of the Disaster Battlefield, as well as Senior Minister Kun Kim as his personal staff, managed and responded quickly to the rescue operation. Disasters are fast and efficient.
The lieutenant general also praised and appreciated the courage of all rescue forces who were bravely committed to the rescue operation to help the victims escape from danger to life.
On the occasion of closing the training course, Lt. Gen. Chan Lumphat encouraged and encouraged the officers and men of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to continue their good work. In particular, be loyal to the motherland and the people by taking all the time, all the traffic regulations, the statutes of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, the legal standards, adhere to the noble tradition, become a real force for the cause of national defense, the motherland and the people.
