Minister of Public Works Leads a Delegation to Attend ASEAN and ASEAN Plus Three Meetings on Public Function in Video
The meeting reviewed the implementation of the work plan from 2016 to 2020, appreciating the efforts of member countries in the development of the framework based on the capacity of officials, institutional capacity building, strengthening leadership, strengthening the role of the research center. ASEAN Member States and Public Sector Reform.
In the past, Cambodia has also led the development of the ASEAN Guidelines on Public Service Delivery, a strategic document for the development of public service delivery mechanisms of ASEAN member countries. The document was also recognized at the 37th ASEAN Summit in Vietnam in November 2020.
Meanwhile, the meeting approved the Action Plan in the framework of ASEAN Cooperation in the field of public functions from 2021 to 2025 and the action plan in the framework of ASEAN cooperation in the field of public functions plus (China, Korea, Japan) from 2011 to 2025.
The ASEAN Heads of Public Works also agreed to continue to strengthen the network of ASEAN Public Administration Training Institutions to promote the capacity development of civil servants of ASEAN Member States.
During the meeting, the heads of ASEAN and ASEAN Plus Three Public Works exchanged views on the fight against the Kovid 19 epidemic.
Mr. Prum Sokha outlined some national strategies and measures in the field of civil service in the fight against Kovid 19, including: Retention of civil servants' salaries, suspension of the recruitment of new civil servants in 2020 to help save the national budget. Procedures of officials to maintain the regularity of the process of providing public services to the people in accordance with the guidelines of the Ministry of Health.
As for the regional framework, the Minister requested that ASEAN should continue to exchange information with ASEAN member countries, China, Korea and Japan regarding the outbreak of Kovid 19 in a timely manner, and ASEAN should continue to assist member countries through humanitarian assistance based on access. In fact, Cambodia has recently provided more than 2 million masks and some medical equipment to Laos as well.
All Member States commended and were proud of the efforts, achievements and progress of cooperation between the ASEAN Member States and ASEAN Plus Three in the field of public functions, despite the situation of the 199 Kovid epidemic.
