General knowledge: The largest political party in the world
(World): The world today has more than 200 countries and a population of more than 7 billion people, all of which are governed by liberal democracy, pluralism or bipartisanship, and also have a one-party regime. The communist regime.
The largest parties are the Indian People's Party in India, the Chinese Communist Party in China, the Democrat Party and the Republican Party in the United States.
The reason why the Communist Party is the second largest party is because China has the world's largest population of about 1.4 billion people, and another big reason is that China's political system is a one-party regime. Therefore, all Chinese people have no progress to join any party other than the Communist Party.
In the United States, the father of democracy, there are only two parties, the Democrat Party, which was founded in 1828 and currently has about 40 million members, and the Republican Party, which was founded in 1854 and currently has about 30 million members.
