General knowledge: In the sea, which animal makes the loudest noise?
In the sea, which animal has more natural sound power than the blue whale?
The sound of the shrimp is the only natural sound that is more powerful than the sound of a blue whale. Their sound can interfere with the submarine's sonar sound frequency, making it impossible for the submarine's hearing aids to hear anything else. The submarine will not hear any sound when it is opened above or below the shrimp.
This loud noise is caused by their brackets colliding simultaneously. The combined sound of shrimp can be heard up to 246 decibels, but because the sound travels in the water is not faster than outside, it can only be heard at 160 decibels.
What's even more interesting is that the meticulously recorded video clearly shows that the sounds came after a 700 microsecratic collision.
Shrimp use these sounds to distract their prey or to signal to each other and to find females. In addition to damaging the submarine's sonar frequency, its sound can also damage the hull's hull. Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia Congratulates Samdech Techo PM on Successful Meditation
(Phnom Penh): The Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary Ambassador of the People's Republic of China to Cambodia, Mr. Wang Vintieng, paid a courtesy call on Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and wished Samdech Techo success in his post.
The Chinese Ambassador paid his respects during a courtesy call and handed over two motorcycles to the Ministry of Health for use in preventing and responding to the Kovid-19 epidemic in Cambodia.
The handover ceremony was presided over by Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, accompanied by Dr. Yuk Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, on the afternoon of November 17, 2020 at the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia.
On that occasion, Minister Mam Bunheng stressed that the new precious humanitarian aid of the Chinese government and people, which is a friend of white steel, confirms the traditional friendship, solidarity and cooperation in the Cambodia-China comprehensive strategic partnership. More and more, it is constantly strengthening and expanding and clarifying the progress towards achieving the building of a common destiny of Cambodia and China.
He added that Cambodia and China have been holding hands shoulder to shoulder in the fight against Kovid-19, but to continue the socio-economic sustainability of both countries and the world.
At the same time, the Minister of Health expressed his deep gratitude to Mr. Wang Wentian, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the People's Republic of China to Cambodia, as well as the Chinese government and people who have always supported Cambodia, especially in the field of health.
Please be informed that on that occasion, the Minister of Health also informed his Chinese counterpart about the situation of Kovid-19 disease management in Cambodia, especially the management of the November 3 event.
Minister of Agriculture: Senior Minister Kun Kim helps farmers to replant on time
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that as of November 15, 2020, more than 6,000 tons of non-seasonal light rice varieties and nearly 560,000 packages of mixed crops have been distributed to farmers. Replanted after the floods receded.
In a letter of thanks sent to Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, received by Fresh News on November 17, 2020, Mr. Veng Sakhon said that light rice seeds were distributed to the people. 64,343 families and seeds were distributed to 93,041 families in 20 capitals and provinces affected by the flood.
In this letter of thanks, Mr. Veng Sakhon highlighted the active intervention and coordination of Senior Minister Kun Kim to make the distribution of rice seeds and other crops to restore farmers' cultivation successfully and timely. .
Mr. Veng Sakhon emphasized that "His Excellency the Senior Minister and Senior Minister have closely cooperated, helped to coordinate and make orientation recommendations to the working group of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries during the study on impact, damage, rehabilitation and management." "Intervene to provide crop seeds to farmers affected by floods in a timely manner in line with the extremely warm growing season."
Mr. Veng Sakhon said that the seed distribution assistance of these crops really contributes greatly to the improvement of agricultural production and reduce the cost of farmers in this difficult time of natural disasters.
It should be noted that for about a month and a half during the period when Cambodia suffered from the floods, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia and the Commander-in-Chief of the Disaster Battlefield, acted responsibly. Highest day and night to save people from floods and supply food, as well as provide rice seeds and other crops to restore people's cultivation after the water recedes.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, on behalf of Samdech Techo's personal staff on the disaster work, strictly and strictly enforced Samdech Techo's orders to carry out operations to resolve the flood battle.
Although one leg of the ankle was inflamed, it was difficult to travel and the doctor forbade him to walk, but as a servant of the people, the Senior Minister operated to all destinations, both sore feet and relying on wood. Stretch without complaining.
The consistent and strict implementation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's orders by Senior Minister Kun Kim, all kinds of armed forces, local authorities and philanthropic forces has made the response to the rescue operation visible. Highly effective and timely both during flooding and rehabilitation after the water recedes.
