ACLEDA makes more than $ 98 million in 9 months of this year
(Phnom Penh): According to the financial report of ACLEDA Bank, in the first nine months of 2020, the bank, which has just entered the stock market, made a profit of more than 98 million dollars, despite the 19 cases of Kovid. .
This profit is more than the same period in 2019, while in 2020, the year of the Cambodian economy suffered by Kovid 19, ACLEDA Bank's profit is expected to reach more than 120 million US dollars. This was confirmed by Ms. Ma Amara, Executive Vice President and Chief Financial Officer, to Fresh News on November 17.
Ms. Ma Amara stated that there are two main reasons why ACLEDA's profit has kept growing despite the difficult circumstances due to Kovid 19, First: The National Bank of Cambodia's Facilitation of Reducing Reserve Rates Obligation (RRR) from 12.5% to 7%, which makes it possible for banks to increase cash flow to lend to customers, and secondly, the bank has reduced some of its operating expenses, which has kept profits growing.
In the first nine months of 2020, the bank earned more than $ 380 million, according to ACLEDA Financial. More than 13 billion riels to be implemented on 3 projects in Kampot province by the end of 2020
(Kampot): Mr. Chiao Tay, Governor of Kampot Province, chaired a meeting of the Provincial Development Planning Committee on the afternoon of November 17, 2020 to discuss, approve and request for compliance with the Ministry of Interior for development.
There are three major development projects with a budget of about 13 billion riels, which were studied and prepared by the working group of technical officers of the Kampot Provincial Administrative Planning Committee to be implemented quickly before the end of 2020.
As a result of this meeting, it was confirmed that this project is a project to build and renovate the infrastructure of the concrete road system, public park, and improve the drainage system in some communes of Kampot city and in Touk Meas commune. Banteay Meas District, Kampot Province.
During the meeting, Mr. Chiao Tai praised and appreciated the efforts of technical officers in the study to achieve the results of the project for the development of infrastructure in the province to further improve to meet the needs of Citizens as well as the general public.
The provincial governor instructed all relevant leaders and officials after the project was approved at this meeting to continue the proper procedure based on the guidelines of the Ministry of Interior to promote the implementation. To expedite the development of these projects to be completed by the end of 2020 to achieve successful results and quality.
Please note that these projects, after being approved by the Provincial Planning Commission, the provincial administration must prepare the project for approval from the Ministry of Interior, and when the Ministry of Interior provides compliance, the provincial administration will reach the implementation of procurement procedures. Provinces in accordance with the procedures of the standard letter and manual on the preparation of capital-provincial projects of the Ministry of Interior.
The project was selected from the province's three-year rolling investment program, and the budget allocated for this project was prepared in the provincial annual budget using the end-of-year supplementary loan budget.
