Chin Malin presents three comparative points on legal aspects and democratic exercise of rights in the United States and Cambodia (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Chin Malin, Spokesman and Vice Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, This November 2020, three comparative points were made about the legal aspects and the exercise of democratic freedoms in the United States and Cambodia.
Aspects of the law and the exercise of democratic rights in the United States and Cambodia include:
First, as a matter of principle, in both the United States and Cambodia, every individual has the right to monitor and observe court proceedings and the conduct of public hearings, but not to engage in any form of interference or pressure on the courts. Which is an independent institution.
Second, in a democratic society, the rule of law in both the United States and Cambodia is a valid factor, but as the number of crimes and crimes increases, the number of cases sent to court increases, which leads to the flow and proceedings. Regular courts, such as the issuance of orders and procedures for prosecution and investigation, etc.
