(Phnom Penh): On November 17, 2020, the traffic police throughout Cambodia inspected and fined a total of 977 vehicles, including 705 motorcycles and 272 cars. This was confirmed by Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and spokesman for the National Police.
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, during the 201 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to November 17, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and A total of 216,828 vehicles were fined, including 160,185 motorcycles and 56,643 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun continued that for the past 201 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
It should be noted that for November 17, 2020, there were 10 traffic accidents throughout Cambodia, in which 6 people were killed and 8 people were injured (4 people were seriously injured).
