Typhoon Vamco is the latest in a series of typhoons to hit Vietnam in the last six weeks, causing floods and landslides, killing at least 159 people and injuring 70 others. Others are still missing.
A preliminary report from the Disaster Management Authority on Sunday said five people were injured as they tried to protect their homes.
In the same 24-hour period, 63 patients were reported dead, bringing the total number of deaths due to COVID-19 to 15,211, according to the Indonesian Ministry of Health. The ministry added that the number of patients had risen to 391,991 after 3,897 had recovered and were allowed to leave the hospital on Sunday.
While daily COVID-19 infections continue to rise to record highs, Indonesia on Friday also announced plans to launch a nationwide large-scale vaccination campaign by the end of 2020.
General Knowledge: The Origins of Democracy
(World): Democratic rule is very popular in many countries around the world, but do you know where this democracy originated and when it appeared? ?
The Greeks believed that in order for their society to be a good society, they had to rely on the rule of law, and that the laws had to be tailored to the lives of the people, in fact, could not be on the orders of the king as before. No. They also believe that a good society must be guided by ethical principles.
In Greek society, it was common for people to gather to discuss policies as well as to jointly draft and amend laws. This is called democracy and only men can be elected to represent the people, lead the people and the nation.
As time went on for thousands of years, the meaning of the word democracy has gradually changed and it has become a form of government in many countries around the world as the United States is now recognized as a republic. The best democracy, or in other words, the "father of democracy." Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone is preparing documents to enter the Cambodian Stock Exchange
(Phnom Penh): Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone is preparing relevant documents to be listed on the stock exchange with the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia to attract more international investment to build this special economic zone to grow. This is according to Mr. CHEN JIANGANG, Chairman of Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone.
The statement of the Chairman of Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone was made during a courtesy call with Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong at the Office of the Council of Ministers on the morning of November 16, 2020.
"The Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone is preparing a listing on the Cambodian Stock Exchange to increase the attractiveness of international investment, especially in Europe and the United States, in order to mobilize international resources for further development," said Chhin Jiang Kang.
The President of the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone also asked Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong to support the listing on the Cambodian Stock Exchange to promote the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone to become Samdech Techo Hun Sen's International Park.
Mr. Chin said that after the listing on the Cambodia Stock Exchange, the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone will continue to list on the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region of the People's Republic of China.
In response to the above request, Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong expressed his immediate support for the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, which is preparing to enter the Cambodian Stock Exchange.
The Deputy Prime Minister expressed confidence that the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone will be more developed in the future after entering the Cambodian Securities Exchange and Hong Kong.
Meanwhile, Mr. Chhin Jiang Kang said that the coal-fired power plant of Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone is scheduled to be completed soon and he even invited Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong to attend the inauguration ceremony. This too.
With pleasure, Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong replied that he would attend the inauguration of a coal-fired power plant in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone so as not to obstruct the operation of the plant due to power outages.
Please be informed that currently in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, there are a total of 165 investment companies that have created job opportunities for about 30,000 workers. The company has also built six dormitories for about 3,000 workers.
From January to October in 2020, the export and import value of Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone amounted to US $ 1.3 billion, an increase of 31% compared to the same period in 2019. . 536 officers and soldiers receive the 29th generation of parachute training and the 8th generation of scuba diving training
