Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong encourages Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone to expand into a major production base in ASEAN (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong has expressed his willingness to encourage Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone to expand. To become a major production base in the ASEAN community of more than 600 million people to export a wide range of products to the ASEAN community as well as other countries.
Mr. Hor Namhong's encouragement was made while allowing Mr. CHEN JIANGANG, President of Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, at the Office of the Council of Ministers on the morning of November 16, 2020 to report on Developed in Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone.
On that occasion, Mr. Chhin Jiang Kang informed Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong that at present, there are a total of 165 investment companies in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, which has created job opportunities for about 30,000 workers. The company has also built six dormitories for about 3,000 workers.
From January to October 2020, the export and import value of Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone amounted to US $ 1.3 billion, an increase of 31%. Compared to the same period in 2019.
