Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, has decided to provide a total of 2,100,000 masks and equipment for the fight against Kovid 19, a total of 12 items, to the Royal Government to participate in the fight against Kovid 19 in Laos. These masks and equipment were handed over by the Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh to the Lao government on the morning of November 16, 2020.
Mr. Thongloun Sisoulit and other senior Lao government officials came out to receive the masks and equipment directly at the airport in Vientiane, Laos.
Speaking at the reception, the Prime Minister of Laos thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, as well as the people of Cambodia for providing mass donations and equipment for the fight against Kovid 19. He considered this gift a precious gift for the government and people of Laos.
Mr. Thongloun Sisoulit stated, "I would like to express my deep gratitude to the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia. In particular, Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, who has always been concerned and has provided precious humanitarian gifts to the Royal Government as well as the people of Laos on this occasion.
"I would like to commend this very meaningful gift, even though Cambodia itself has been affected by the spread of Kovid 19," he said. "But the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia have always been generous in sharing this most precious gift in a timely manner to the government and people of Laos."
The Lao head of government also considered these gifts as a clear reflection of the friendly relations, solidarity and close cooperation between Cambodia and Laos.
On that occasion, Mr. Thongloun Sisoulit also highlighted that as a village country, Cambodia and Laos have a good relationship and have always supported each other for a long time. Especially since the national liberation struggle from the colonies, having stood shoulder to shoulder and supported each other inseparably to fight an enemy.
The Prime Minister of Laos also reminded the support of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia when it encounters the disaster of the dam collapse in 2018.
The Prime Minister of Laos has vowed in front of Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh that he will use all these masks and equipment for the benefit of the Lao people. The Prime Minister also wished Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Royal Government of Cambodia success in the fight against Kovid 19.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh emphasized that these gifts are a gesture of brotherhood and solidarity of the Cambodian people with the Lao people in a situation where the whole world is facing unprecedented challenges. Safety of health and security of humanity.
