Minister of Health answers questions about the importance of hand washing to protect yourself and your loved ones from Kovid 19 and other diseases
(Phnom Penh): Why is it important to wash your hands thoroughly to protect yourself and your loved ones from Kovid 19? This question was explained in detail by Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, to the public about the importance of hand washing.
The minister said that washing hands with soap and clean water or washing hands with alcohol or gel will help kill germs from hands. Washing hands with alcohol or gel should be done with a solution containing at least 60% alcohol. Hand washing should be done properly and last at least 20 to 30 seconds.
1: People often touch their eyes, nose and mouth without realizing it. The virus can enter the body through the eyes, nose and mouth and make us sick.
He said that disinfection through proper hand washing not only helps prevent the spread of Kovid 19, but also prevents the spread of other respiratory and other diseases such as tuberculosis. Diarrhea, eye and skin diseases. This is one of the measures to prevent infectious diseases, especially COVID-19, which the public should understand and implement frequently and correctly.
