(Phnom Penh): Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, General Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, attended the ASEAN-New Zealand Summit held on November 14, 2020.
According to a press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, obtained by Fresh News, the main results of this meeting are as follows:
The meeting was held to commemorate the 45th anniversary of the ASEAN-New Zealand Dialogue Partnership. ASEAN leaders congratulate Jesinda Adin on her landslide victory in the New Zealand general election in November 2020.
The meeting noted the adoption of the ASEAN-New Zealand Action Plan (2021-2025), which focuses on four new partnership programs: people, prosperity, peace and the planet. The meeting also adopted the Joint Statement of the ASEAN-New Zealand Leaders' Vision on the 45th Anniversary of the ASEAN-New Zealand Dialogue Partnership: A Legacy of a Partnership and a Common Future.
ASEAN leaders thanked New Zealand for its $ 1 million support to the ASEAN Fund for Response to the Kovid-19 Epidemic.
The meeting agreed to work together to promote people-to-people exchanges and cooperation in human resource development, education, innovation and technology. The meeting also focused on trade and business coordination, strengthening small and medium enterprises (MSME), tourism, public health, food security and connectivity.
