* History of customs
* Current habits
Of course, most of the custom of wearing rings applies to affirmations and marriages. But today, wearing your ring does not necessarily mean that you want to express your desire to have a partner. For some couples, not sure to wear it on her left finger, sometimes they wear it on any finger.
In fact, in some countries, such as Austria, Denmark, Norway, Poland, Germany, and Latvia, it is customary for couples to wear a ring on their left finger. But for Spain, they wear a ring on their right finger.
However, due to the evolution of one era, some countries adhere to the Roman way and others do not. In general, the choice of wearing a ring on either finger is your choice, because wanting to express your desire to be single or have a partner is not just confirmed by the ring, it is confirmed by the heart. In this sense, many Europeans lived together and had children until death, they never got married or married.
In Cambodia, we also see people wearing rings, especially holding her left finger. Wearing this ring is a ceremony to be heard by the elders on both sides, not like the Westerners wear the ring to each other according to the decision of both parties without the family knowing in advance.
