(Phnom Penh): On behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, attended the 8th ASEAN-US Summit held this morning. November 14, 2020.
A press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation states that the main results of the summit are as follows:
This year marks the 43rd anniversary of the ASEAN-US Dialogue Partnership and the 5th anniversary of the Strategic Partnership. ASEAN leaders congratulated the United States on its successful general election in November 2020 and expressed their desire to further deepen their strategic partnership with the United States.
The meeting noted the progress of ASEAN-US relations, including through the full implementation of the ASEAN-US Strategic Partnership Action Plan (2016-2020) and the adoption of a new Work Plan (2021-2025). .
ASEAN leaders commended the United States' continued support for the ASEAN Middle East and its efforts to build the ASEAN Community and Multilateralism, as well as cooperation within the ASEAN Indo-Pacific Perspective.
In economic affairs, the leaders commended the work of the ASEAN-US Business Council (USABC) in promoting stronger ties between the business communities of the two sides. Leaders agree on the importance of cooperation for economic recovery in the aftermath of the Kovid-19 pandemic.
In development cooperation, ASEAN leaders welcomed the United States' support for building a people-centered and people-centered ASEAN community through education, capacity building and development programs. In this spirit, the Meeting adopted the ASEAN-US Joint Declaration on Human Resource Development.
During the meeting, Cambodia expressed its commitment to strengthening the partnership and called for more cooperation from the United States in building the capacity of young entrepreneurs so that they can grow and prosper in this era. The digital economy will focus on collaboration between science, technology, engineering and mathematics (STEM) and digital education programs.
Cambodia stressed that both sides need to further increase bilateral trade and investment flows through the implementation of the "ASEAN-US Investment and Trade Framework Agreement 2020-2021". Cambodia has encouraged the American business community to expand their investment in ASEAN.
