Authorities demolished houses in Sitbo commune, Takhmao city under the pretext of building on state land
(Kandal): On November 13, 2020, Takhmao City Authority, under the coordination of the Prosecutor's Office, deployed forces to dismantle the houses of some people built on state land and lakes in Sangkat Sitbo, Takhmao City, Kandal Province.
However, during the demolition, it was observed that some residents were dissatisfied with the Takhmao municipal authorities who used force to demolish their houses, considering them to be slums built on state land.
The people are dissatisfied and ask the authorities to suspend the demolition of their buildings because they stated that in the past, the governor of Kandal province has been considering their request for legal ownership. .
The villagers claim that their land has been occupied since 1985 and that they have been enjoying farming, livestock and fishing, but that the authorities claim that they have not been given a title deed. It is said that this land is a lake, state land and it is forbidden to resell it to others.
According to the people, in the past, they also made a letter of request to the Governor of Kandal Province to make a letter of possession of unregistered real estate, and at the meeting of the State Land Management Committee on September 29, 2020 The province considered the request of these people, but in the end, Takhmao city authorities sent forces to dismantle the house.
In connection with this case, the news agency Fresh News has not been able to ask for an explanation regarding the demolition of the residents' homes. Residents have urged the governor of Kandal province to intervene to help them enjoy and rebuild their homes for asylum.
