Welcoming and supporting China, the 23rd ASEAN-China Summit on "Review of ASEAN-China Cooperation and Future Directions" was held on the afternoon of November 12. 2020.
Under the theme "Review of ASEAN-China Cooperation and Future Directions", the 23rd ASEAN-China Summit focused on challenges including public health issues and social status. Economy caused by the Kovid-19 crisis in both regions.
The meeting stressed the need to increase cooperation between ASEAN and China in strengthening solidarity and cooperation in response to epidemics and in restoring stability and recovery of the post-crisis socio-economic situation. This is accomplished through existing mechanisms, including the "Implementation Plan 2016-2020" and the "ASEAN-China Free Trade Agreement (ACFTA)", as well as seeking new cooperation mechanisms.
The leaders of ASEAN welcomed and appreciated China's contribution to strengthening and enhancing ASEAN-China relations, as well as promoting the "ASEAN-China Partnership on the Blue Economy" Initiative and the Vision for Sustainability. "ASEAN-China Strategic Partnership 2030."
The ASEAN-China leaders pledged to continue to uphold the principles of multilateralism and called for increased regional cooperation on building trust and maintaining future socio-economic resilience and openness. Free trade, regional supply chain connectivity, and digital economy practices.
At the same time, the leaders of the ASEAN countries expressed their satisfaction and support for the commitment of the Prime Minister of the People's Republic of China Li Kequiang to enhance cooperation, assistance to the ASEAN region and Resolve other issues through peaceful mechanisms based on the spirit of unity and prosperity for all the people of the two regions.
