Discover NASA key technologies to be used in manned missions to Mars
(Foreign): Mars is one of the most important targets of scientific research on Earth. In addition to sending robots there, the development of advanced technology to allow the first manned mission to Mars during the 2030s has already begun, by the US space agency. NASA. This is according to the release by Science Daily on Thursday evening, November 12, 2020.
Many technological capabilities will be demonstrated in NASA's Artemis mission, first aimed at the moon, but there are other technologies being developed specifically for humans to explore even further. Like Mars itself. The following are the main technologies that NASA is working to develop to make the dream of sending humans to Mars come true:
* Far more powerful engine system to get us here and back soon
Advances in spacecraft technology are the key to getting us to our destination quickly and safely in space. It is not clear at this time what technology scientists will use to send astronauts to Mars, but NASA is focusing on some nuclear power technologies.
* Heat shield for astronaut landing
In contrast to sending robots to land on Mars, sending humans will require a huge spacecraft. As a result, new technologies are needed to allow spacecraft, which is heavier and larger than ever, to land safely on Mars. NASA is developing a heat shield.
* Space suit for astronauts on Mars
To reduce the amount of material to be sent to the surface of Mars, NASA decided to focus on combining accommodation and vehicles to travel into a single object. NASA is focusing on vehicle technology for maneuvering on Mars' surface and allowing the spacecraft to act as a living room or lab with normal ventilation, similar to the RVs on Earth.
* Uninterruptible power supply
* Communication technology using lasers to transmit more data
