Despite 19 Kovids, the trade volume of Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone continues to grow, reaching more than 1 billion USD in the first 10 months of this year, an increase of 31%
(Phnom Penh): Despite the hardships caused by the Kovid 19 crisis, trade in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone (SSEZ) is still gaining momentum. According to the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, in the first 10 months of 2020, the trade volume of exports and imports into the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone reached 1.273 million US dollars.
The report of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia also shows that in the first 10 months of 2020, the number of containers entering and leaving the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone was 36,206 containers.
The Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, invested by a Chinese company, highlighted in its press release that the scale of trade demonstrates the sustainable development potential of the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone during the crisis. Kovid's disease 19.
Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, invested by a Chinese company, is an internationally open international investment forum that has established close economic and trade ties with countries around the world. From the beginning until now, Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone has considered providing services to factories, enterprises and improving the business environment as the most important task.
In addition, efforts have been made to accelerate the development of Phase II by accelerating the construction and improvement of infrastructure for production and livelihoods in the region, providing strong guarantees for manufacturing plants.
Today, the 50MW High Voltage Substation, located in the Special Economic Zone, operates and supplies power normally and will greatly improve the capacity and stability of the power supply in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone.
According to statistics, from January to October 2020, the total electricity consumption of enterprises in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone amounted to about 7,727,000 kilowatt hours, an increase of 50.46% compared to Will be the same period last year.
The second phase of the coal-fired power plant and wastewater treatment plant has been accelerated. It is estimated that the project will be completed by mid-2020. Accommodation for the six Cambodian staff has been completed and officially put into use. These meet the needs of workers who have homes far from the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone.
Although the spread of Kovi 19 has brought serious challenges to the enterprise and caused some companies to decline their production capacity, depending on the role and strength of the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, the enterprise The region remains committed to resolving its challenges and gradually restoring its production capacity.
Some enterprises have turned risk into business opportunities and achieved double-digit productivity compared to last year.
On the other hand, some companies that have just come to invest in their area have tried to overcome obstacles to produce as soon as possible. From the beginning of the year until now, eight new companies have been in the process of production and have become remarkably new growth points.
AIDC trading Co. Ltd is a grain processing company with a parent company in Laos. The company invested in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone in February 2020. After investing in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, the company overcame all obstacles caused by the effects of Kovi 19 in international relations and resumed production in September 2020.
Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone claims that as the "engine" of economic development in Sihanoukville, Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone is promoting the development of local industries with practical activities with the development of Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone. Stage 2.
Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone expressed its belief that through the efforts and strength of the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, more and more international companies will be able to achieve the development forward and be a part of the economic development. The society of Sihanoukville as well as Cambodia. Minister Chea Vandeth defended two draft laws during the 6th Senate session of the 4th legislature
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of November 12, 2020, at the Senate Palace, Mr. Chea Vandeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, and Mr. Panh Sosak, Minister of Commerce, led a delegation to attend the 6th Senate Session of the 4th Legislature under the chairmanship of Samdech Vibol. Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, to defend two draft laws.
The two draft laws are: 1. Draft Law on the Approval of the First Protocol Amending the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement between the Member States of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations and Japan; and 2: Draft Law on Approve the protocol for the implementation of the 10th pledge under the ASEAN Framework Agreement on Services.
The Minister stressed the benefits of the "Draft Law on the Approval of the First Protocol Amending the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement between the Member States of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations and Japan" to boost ASEAN-Japan trade. Improved responsiveness to global economic developments and ASEAN-Japan economic connectivity through liberalization of trade, services, physical displacement and investment.
The minister said that Cambodia will have more opportunities to benefit from the amended agreement because Japan is a large capital market in the region and has advanced technology. After the entry into force of this protocol, it will attract more Japanese investors and business people to invest in Cambodia and the flow of technology and technology will be better.
Minister Chea Vandeth thanked Samdech, President of the Senate, for allowing him and his colleagues to participate in the defense of the two draft laws.
The Minister strongly hopes that these two laws will bring significant benefits to the whole society and promote the economic growth of Cambodia for the better.
It should be noted that these two draft laws were approved by the Council of Ministers in the plenary session of the Council of Ministers on September 4, 2020 and approved by the National Assembly on November 2, 2020 in the session. For the fifth time, the 6th legislature received 116 votes in favor and was approved by the Senate today with 52 votes out of the total number of senators.
