Spokesman for the General Commission: On November 12, another 531 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, during the 196 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to November 12, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and A total of 212,232 vehicles were fined, including 156,820 motorcycles and 55,412 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kimkhoeun continued that for the past 196 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
It should be noted that for November 12, 2020, there were 9 traffic accidents throughout Cambodia, in which 4 people were killed and 12 people were injured (9 people were seriously injured).
(Kampong Speu): Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu Province and Honorary President of Kampong Speu Provincial Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross on November 12, 2020, distributed humanitarian donations of the Red Cross to the flood victims in the past. In Trapeang Kong commune, Samrong Tong district, Kampong Speu province, there are 119 families.
On that occasion, Mr. Vy Samnang paid a courtesy call on the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, to the flood victims. Rain with nostalgia and sympathy at last.
The governor continued that although this gift can not help you become rich, but all these materials can help solve the problem for a short time to give you the opportunity to earn a living.
Mr. Vy Samnang instructed all people to participate in protecting themselves from Kovid-19 disease, not to have this virus in the community or village where you live, and to be clean after the flood. You try to grow mixed crops to improve your livelihood. In particular, we must help reduce traffic accidents that the Royal Government is concerned about and must make sure that the villages and communes are safe.
Banteay Meanchey Provincial Authority Continues to Distribute Masses and Disseminate Kovid-19 Prevention Measures to Local People
(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Koeung Vannak, Deputy Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, on November 12, 2020, the representative of Mr. Oum Rath, Provincial Governor, led a working group to distribute masks and disseminate information on measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 to the people in Banteay Meanchey. Locally in Thmar Puok district.
During the mass distribution and dissemination of health measures, Mr. Koeng Vannak said that prevention of Kovid-19 virus infection is very important because the disease can be transmitted in all forms and conditions. They are required to be kept indoors for 14 days, wash their hands with water, soap, alcohol and gel, and meet to raise their hands or raise their hands to avoid shaking hands because of anxiety. Copy the virus as well.
"Kovid-19 is a deadly disease that continues to plague the world, killing millions of people and infecting millions of people worldwide," he said. There is medicine that can cure this disease, so we must all participate in the prevention of Kovid disease by local officials to teach people to know how to use alcohol, wash hands and use masks for everyone.
(Stung Treng): In order to contribute to the education and awareness of children and girls in remote rural areas to be more aware and equal in decision making, Plan International Cambodia in collaboration with Stung Treng Provincial Department of Education, Youth and Sports Roundtable discusses the impact of the Kovid-19 pandemic and the safety of girls on the Internet.
The forum was held in the presence of Ms. Ty Thida, Deputy Director of the Provincial Department of Education, Youth and Sports and Mr. Phen Bunthoeun, Executive Director of Stung Treng of Plan International Cambodia, and was attended by 60 students, local authorities and stakeholders. This took place at the meeting hall of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Stung Treng Province.
According to Mr. Phen Bunthoeun, this forum was held to celebrate the International Girls' Day on October 11 and to learn about the effects of Kovid-19 disease on rural communities and the problems faced by students, especially children. Girls in rural communities to study online or online.
He said that in the context of Kovid-19, Plan International Cambodia has partnered with KE to study rural communities, especially girls, about the difficulties of learning about violent decision-making and girls' dropouts, as well as discuss And cooperate with relevant authorities to find a better solution for them.
Ms. Ty Thida said that during the Kovid-19 outbreak, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports closed schools prematurely, but the ministry also paid attention and cooperated with the Ministry of Information and stakeholders to organize Teaching on TV, on the Internet, on Facebook or online to avoid gatherings to avoid the spread of Kovid-19 disease.
At the same time, she acknowledged that in the context of Kovid-19, some students, children and girls in rural communities still find it difficult to study due to the remoteness of the community.
Ms. Ty Thida added that in the second phase of the education system during Kovid-19, we have a full study in Stung Treng, but in the other 5 districts of Stung Treng province, arranged to study in order with 3 days and 2 days. By alternating teaching, it means that the children in the school, but not more than 20, if more students are divided into two or three groups and still keep the distance to participate in preventing infection.
She also encouraged and appealed to parents, guardians of students to send children of all ages to school and encourage students to continue their education until they finish without dropping out and to eliminate the abandonment of children and girls. .
Ministry of Interior Inspected the Implementation of Roles, Duties and Functions of Municipal-District-Khan Administration in Banteay Meanchey Province
