According to the Philippine Meteorological Agency, the force of the storm was between 130-200 km per hour and is now moving towards the South China Sea. 37th ASEAN Summit Focuses on 19 Kovid Impacts and Post-Crisis Rehabilitation Targets
(Phnom Penh): The 37th ASEAN Summit and related summits started this morning, November 12, 2020 via video.
The summit is organized under the theme "Coherence and Response of ASEAN" and will take place from 12 to 15 November 2020.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, led a Cambodian delegation to the 37th ASEAN Summit via video at the Ministry of Economy and Finance. Stuff.
According to a statement from the Ministry of Economy, obtained by Fresh News today, the summit is aimed at discussing the impact on the country's public health and socio-economic sectors. Areas affected by the Kovid-19 outbreak, setting the next direction for restoring and maintaining the socio-economic stability of member countries and regions as the crisis ends.
The summit is also an important forum for ASEAN leaders and all stakeholders to exchange views and provide input on addressing key regional and global issues, as well as to further strengthen and expand cooperation on For new and existing initiatives in order to strengthen the spirit of multilateralism and the maintenance of ASEAN neutrality.
On behalf of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth participated in the intervention, emphasizing Cambodia's strong commitment and commitment to the common vision of ASEAN in achieving strong collective integration. And prosperity through cooperation, solidarity and adherence to trade liberalization and multilateral mechanisms.
The 37th ASEAN Summit also approved the launch of the Mid-Term Review of the 2025 ASEAN Community Detailed Plan, the ASEAN Comprehensive Rehabilitation Framework and the ASEAN Regional Medical Reserve.
If recurrence of the disease occurs more frequently among those who are vaccinated than with placebo, the effectiveness figure may decline. Therefore, we do not yet know how this figure reflects the protective ability of the vaccine, which means that we have to go to the final stage of testing.
* If you are not sure, why announce the provisional results now?
The only way to determine if resume is the right choice is to allow an independent data and security team to evaluate some or all of the results. At a time when the whole world is plagued by COVID-19, time is of the essence, and further efforts are being made to integrate provisional analysis data into studies in a way that can provide answers. Be confident in a timely manner as much as possible.
Therefore, a review of the provisional data has been planned since the start of the vaccine trial. It is a positive sign that the test needs to continue, although the actual data from the analysis raises a lot of questions.
However, according to the actual data, mRNA-based vaccines are new to all of us, we need more time to find out if the initial response starts to weaken. In addition, we need to find out if this vaccine and other vaccine candidates can boost the immune system, which can provide protection for many years.
Another important thing to know is whether vaccines can completely prevent people from contracting any virus, or it makes people more effective in fighting the virus if they fail to prevent infection. This will determine whether the vaccine can only prevent disease or prevent viral transmission, and what we do know now is that it has reduced the symptoms by more than 90 percent (Pfizer vaccine).
Although the vaccine is not yet fully pictured, the US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has stated that it will consider the vaccine's approval immediately before full approval once the trial has collected data on the safety period. 2 months on half participants. Pfizer expects to release all of this data in the third week of November.
Trials will continue for several months to reach a reliable level, and there will be further monitoring to check the safety of the vaccine and the immune response, especially protection against volunteers. Other. This is why it is important to provide more information and transparency about vaccine safety to the public.
