Mr. Apil Khan continued, "Giving a mask to the poor people in the past as well as now is to pay attention to the well-being of the people, especially the poor people from Samdech Techo Hun Sen on prevention. To infect 19 Cambodians with Kovid virus. ”
Taking the opportunity to distribute the mask, Mr. Cheng Monira also advised all people to know how to clean their hands, wash their hands with soap or alcohol or gel often, wear a protective mask regularly and reduce all Gatherings or crowds in public places.
Please be reminded that on the afternoon of November 11, 2020, the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, announced the release of 2 million masks to be distributed to the people in Phnom Penh.
Cambodian leader Samdech Techo Hun Sen has ordered the Ministry of Health and Phnom Penh Capital Hall to do this immediately by releasing a mask from the Royal Government's strategic warehouse so that people living in poor communities can wear it. The mask will be used to prevent Kovid-19 infection.
Secretary of State Em Chanmakara: Campaign for the promotion of the rights of persons with disabilities is being actively promoted at both the national and sub-national levels.
Secretary of State for the Ministry of Social Affairs Em Chanmakara called on people with disabilities to maintain good sanitation in accordance with the Ministry of Health's rules to avoid the spread of Kovid-19 in the community. At the same time, Secretary of State for the Ministry of Interior, Mr. Yun Chhuny, reminded to maintain social gaps in all meetings and communication.
