The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior also stated that under the wise leadership of Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia has set out a national development policy by continuing its commitment to maintaining peace, political stability, national security and growth. Economy based on independence, sovereignty, territorial integrity, democracy and respect for human rights, thank you for peace.
(Prey Veng): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, this morning, November 12, 2020, presided over a visit to distribute rice seeds and other gifts to people in need. 3,500 families from 7 districts in Prey Veng province were affected by the floods.
This method was organized in Chheu Karch village, Chheu Karch commune, Ba Phnom district, Prey Veng province, with the participation of Mr. Suon Somalin, acting governor of Prey Veng province, as well as government officials and thousands of people.
Mr. Suon Somalin reported to Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng that Prey Veng province has experienced floods since the beginning of October 2020, which damaged more than 77,000 meters of roads built by the commune fund. 150 meters of canals, 65 drainage systems and affected rice fields in 7 districts.
Speaking at the ceremony, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng emphasized that the presence of Samdech who came to meet and distribute gifts to the people on this occasion is in a campaign of the Royal Government to enable you to start cultivating again.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng continued that the work of providing special assistance to rice seeds and vegetables to the people now is the next step after the Royal Government led the work to save people from the flood disaster, which coincided with the rescue in the past. By then, the people really know that the Royal Government and the authorities have provided emergency assistance to the people during that difficult time.
Samdech Krala Hom emphasized that Prey Veng is currently the number one province in Battambang province with a lot of rice cultivation. He added that the increase in rice production is due to the fact that farmers have the opportunity to farm two to three times a year, depending on the irrigation system and modern farming methods combined with a good market.
Samdech Krala Hom stated that nowadays, although the number of farmers is increasing, the demand for farmers is less due to the shift from traditional agriculture to modern farming, such as switching from Cattle plowing is the use of tractors or bulldozers, or switching from sowing to sowing and reaping with machine tools.
Taking that opportunity, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also informed the people that the working system of the Cambodian People's Party and the Royal Government of Cambodia, which you always vote for, has a tradition of dividing officials down to the grassroots to monitor. Needs, concerns and suggestions of you and cooperate from the bottom to the top to have measures to resolve as soon as possible and have a habit of mourning with the people.
At the same time, Samdech Krala Hom also informed the people about the situation of Kovid-19 in Cambodia and in the world, expressing hope that the local administration and the people will continue to increase vigilance and implement measures as instructed. Of the Ministry of Health, such as reducing the collection of masks and hand washing.
The Deputy Prime Minister also went on to talk about the drug problem, with Prince Kralahom emphasizing that the drug problem will not end as easily as the Kovid-19 problem. Therefore, the prince called on the people to continue to educate their children and family members to stay away from drugs. At the same time, the authorities must take strict legal action and people must report drug cases to the authorities.
In addition to reporting or complaining about drug problems or other problems to the authorities, or in case the authorities do not pay attention to any issues, Prince Sar Kheng also encouraged people to report those problems to the media or through Social media means such as Facebook to get those issues exposed and addressed.
Before concluding, on behalf of the Royal Government and on behalf of the Chairman of the National Working Group for Prey Veng Province, Samdech Krala Hom expressed his deep gratitude to the leaders of the working group and the authorities at all levels for their cooperation in rescuing the people in a timely manner. He called on the people to work hard to build a better family life in order to contribute to the economic, social and national development.
Please note that the gifts that Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, gave to the people on this occasion include 100 kg of rice seeds, 4 kinds of vegetable seeds, 2 kinds of cabbage, eggplant and squash, and a kit with materials and food. Including some budget.
After the visit and distribution of gifts to the people here, Samdech continued to visit and distribute the same gifts to the people organized at Prey Veng Provincial Hall. Deputy PM Yim Chhay Ly Distributes Relief to Flood Victims and 300 Veterans in Kampong Cham
On that occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly also met with the people and brought greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who both always think about the well-being and suffering of the people. Citizens.
At the same time, the Deputy Prime Minister called on the people to be more vigilant in preventing and preventing Kovid-19 disease in accordance with the guidelines of the Ministry of Health to prevent the disease from spreading in the family and in Community as well.
It should also be noted that the families who suffered and suffered from the recent floods and the families of the veterans who came to receive the gifts showed their happy faces and supported the authorities who brought Samdech Techo's gifts. Hun Sen came to the rescue with materials and food and money, making their lives easier for a while during this difficult time.
