(Siem Reap): Nowadays, the western part of Angkor Wat has been transformed into a beautiful face decorated with flowers, green grass and many trees. As for the hospitality area, APSARA Authority is busy constructing information buildings, first aid buildings and other buildings to facilitate national and international tourists to international standards, which is scheduled to be completely renovated in mid-2021.
Ms. Ho Sela, a gardener, said that in less than a year, the face of Angkor has become beautiful with forests, flowers and lush green grass, and refreshed and exhausted from work.
Similarly, Ms. Chuon Srey Mom described that tourists who visit Angkor last time will praise the beautiful beauty and good order in Angkor. She also thanked the leadership of APSARA Authority for their attention and efforts to improve the perimeter of Angkor Wat.
As gardeners in front of the Angkor Wat temples, Ms. Ho Seila and Ms. Chuon Srey Mom called on tourists visiting Angkor to maintain a clean environment and always throw garbage in the trash, because without the participation of the public. Nor can the environment remain beautiful.
Mr. Pov Sinith, Technical Officer of the Department of Forest Management, Landscape, Culture and Environment of the APSARA Authority, who is in charge of arranging the garden in front of the Angkor Wat temple complex, said that at the entrance in front of the Angkor Wat temple complex, there are plants such as flowers, black chicken bones, red leaves and flowers. Duck-foot grass, a thick, durable foot grass, is suitable for planting here where people walk around.
In addition, the team also cut down the branches, removed the trees at risk to keep the tourists safe and planted trees in turn, such as thnong, peacock, Neang Nuon, Beng, Koki and so on.
* The main results of the three meetings are as follows:
The meeting reviewed the progress of the implementation of the ASEAN Political-Security Community Master Plan, one of the three pillars of the ASEAN Community Vision 2025. Despite the challenges posed by Kovid-19 since the beginning of the year, the meeting praised the momentum of cooperation under the pillars of the ASEAN Political-Security Community.
The ASEAN Foreign Ministers acknowledged the importance of regional action to address security and transnational issues as contributing to the promotion of peace and stability in the ASEAN region. The Ministers accepted the report of the mid-term review of the 2025 ASEAN Political-Security Community Master Plan.
The meeting also agreed on the need to continue to carry out activities that can enhance trust and confidence in maritime cooperation, such as in the form of seminars on maritime loans and recent workshops on the promotion of maritime loans. Cooperation in ensuring the accuracy and humanity of fishermen in the South China Sea.
28th ASEAN Coordinating Council Meeting:
The meeting was organized in preparation for the 37th ASEAN Summit and related summits. The ASEAN Foreign Ministers also exchanged views on ASEAN community-building efforts, including the review of the implementation of the ASEAN Charter, the mid-term review of the ASEAN Community 2025 Detailed Plan and the development of the post-2025 ASEAN Community Vision. ASEAN Response Initiative for Kovi-19.
The ASEAN Foreign Ministers also agreed on the importance of raising awareness and understanding of ASEAN through the display of ASEAN flags and anthems at ASEAN member governments and ASEAN events.
The ASEAN Foreign Ministers welcomed the accession to the Treaty of Amity and Cooperation in the Southeast Asia (TAC) of the Republic of Cuba, the Republic of South Africa and the Republic of Colombia, and the video signing ceremony of the Supplementary Documentation. And TAC accession documents were also made at the meeting.
This participation reflects the growing interest of countries outside the region to join ASEAN on the basis of respect and adherence to the goals and principles of the TAC. Royal Government Mass Distributed to Vendors and Residents at Chbar Ampov Market, Vegetable Market and Boeung Kang Kang Market for Kovid 19 Prevention
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of November 12, 2020, three market presidents, including Boeung Keng Kang Market President, Mr. Ek Nimol, Mr. San Bunna, President of Chbar Ampov Vegetable Market and Mr. Kouch Chamnan, President of Chbar Ampov Market, and his team met with relatives. Vendors and customers have distributed masks to their hands to use to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
According to the directors of the three markets, these masks will be given to people who can not afford to buy and use, as well as those who enter and leave the market who do not wear masks, by offering two pieces of masks that can be washed several times. .
Phnom Penh Governor Khuon Sreng said that tens of thousands of masks were distributed to 14 districts and markets, which was a precious gift from the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, to the Phnom Penh administration for distribution. Communities in Phnom Penh are one of the many measures taken by Samdech Techo as well as local authorities to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
In the response to the 19-year-old Kovid infection, the market management has taken a number of steps by educating traders to be aware of the 19-KVID infection and has set temperature targets for visitors, including alcohol spraying. Through many entrances and exits.
The Senate issued a press release on the results of the 6th session of the 4th legislature (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The General Secretariat of the Senate issued a press release on the results of the 6th session of the 4th legislature. Held this morning, November 12, 2020, under the presidency of Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate of Cambodia, with 52 senators present.
1. Draft Law on the Approval of the Protocol on the Boundary and Post of Land Boundary between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Socialist Republic of Vietnam.
2. Draft law on the ratification of the Treaty on the Prohibition of Nuclear Weapons.
3. Draft Law on the Approval of the First Protocol Amending the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement between the Member States of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations and Japan.
4. Draft Law on the Approval of the Protocol Implementing the 10th Pledge under the ASEAN Framework Agreement on Services.
5. Draft Law on the Approval of the Investment Agreement under the Framework Agreement on Comprehensive Economic Cooperation between the Association of Southeast Asian Nations and the Republic of India.
6. Draft Law on the Approval of Investment Agreement between the Member States of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations and the Government of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region of the People's Republic of China.
