(Phnom Penh): Ms. Youk Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, would like to announce the complete rejection of the information that more than half of the more than 900 Kovid cases among more than 900 test takers involved in the "November 3" event.
The dismissal came after a man shared on social media that more than half of the more than 900 people tested for Kovid 19 were positive.
Through Fresh News on the morning of November 12, Ms. Youk Sambath expressed regret for the crooks who fabricated all this unfortunate information and considered these inspirations as a poisonous intent to commit. To cause social unrest.
Ms. Youk Sambath pointed out that in connection with the "November 3" event from November 4-11, 2020, there were 2,497 test takers. Of these, 1,680 took the first test and 817 took the second test. She claimed that out of a total of 2,497 test takers, only four were positive. Other than that, all the negative results.
While rejecting this information, Ms. Youk Sambath asked the relevant authorities to increase the action to deal with these crooks to prevent unrest from their fabrication.
It should be noted that in recent days, criminals have tried to share a lot of fabricated information related to the 19 cases of Kovid. In addition to fabricating news to scare the 19 cases of Kovid, they also fabricated information related to the closure of countries, the closure of capitals and provinces.
