In the first nine months of this year, Cambodia's exports to the United States reached nearly $ 5 billion, up nearly 22 percent.
(Phnom Penh): The report of the Office of Trade Statistics of the US Department of Commerce confirmed that in the first nine months of 2020, the volume of Cambodia's exports to the United States amounted to 4,828.7 million US dollars, an increase of nearly 22% compared to the same period in 2019, which was 3,958.7 million dollars.
Cambodia's imports from the United States in the first nine months of this year amounted to $ 232 million, down 42 percent from $ 400 million in the same period last year.
According to figures from the General Department of Customs and Excise of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the volume of trade in the first nine months of 2020 will be about 13.6 billion US dollars, compared to the same period last year. 2019 decreased by 8.70%.
