The opening of the third mandate consultation forum was chaired by Mr. Khlot Phorn, Chairman of Kampong Cham Provincial Council, Mr. Un Chanda, Provincial Governor of Kampong Cham, as well as members of the Provincial Council, Deputy Governors and civil society, with a total of more than 100 participants. This morning, November 11, 2020.
On that occasion, Mr. Khlot Phorn stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Hun Sen, has decided and committed to deep and long-term administrative reform at the sub-national level, both administratively and politically, through the establishment of the Council. Commune / Sangkat, which is the direct representative of the people.
Mr. Khlot Phorn stated that the introduction of the policy of decentralization and deconcentration reform is in line with the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia, which was adopted in 1993, with the main purpose of improving the governance system in various administrations to promote Local democracy, promoting local economic and social development, contributing to poverty reduction throughout Cambodia.
Mr. Khlot Phorn emphasized that the organization of outreach and consultation forums is an important tool for promoting accountability, transparency and the participation of both men and women in the governance process of the Council of Sub-National Administration.
It should also be noted that in the consultation forum, there were 12 points raised by the people, some of which were resolved immediately, while some issues were raised by the Kampong Cham Provincial Board of Governors to be addressed first. Next time.
