Jeep crashes into Ratanakkiri Provincial Referral Hospital, killing one patient and injuring four
(Tbong Khmum): A traffic accident occurred when a jeep (direction from Tbong Khmum to Kratie province) collided with an ambulance of Ratanakkiri Provincial Referral Hospital (direction from Ratanakkiri to Tbong Khmum province) in the opposite direction, causing one death. And injured 4 people.
The accident happened at 8:40 pm on November 10, 2020 at the 35-36 km marker in Svay Kambit village, Seda commune, Tambor district, Tbong Khmum province. Caused by speed and lack of caution.
One person was killed and four others were injured in the accident, which involved five people in an ambulance, one in Taikung (minor injuries), a female doctor (severe fracture of one thigh) and two attendants. (Seriously injured) and the patient died after being involved in a car accident.
The driver of the truck (unidentified) escaped after the incident. The four victims were taken to hospital. The bodies were taken to the family for a traditional ceremony, while the two vehicles were measured to deal with legal procedures.
