Chea Chanto Attends Central Bank Governor's Summit with IMF Director to Discuss Policy Implementation in Support of Economic and Social Activities
The conference will be held on November 10, 2020 on "Ensuring Growth and Resilience in ASEAN: Post-Crisis Politics - 19".
The purpose of the conference was to exchange ideas and experiences between policymakers from countries in the region and international financial institutions, including finance ministers, governors, central banks and the IMF's managing director, discussing key policy practices. To support economic and social activities, as well as the main challenges after the Kovid-19 crisis.
The Kovid-19 pandemic is a crisis unlike any other, with no country escaping the effects of this serious health and economic crisis, and uncertainty about the spread of the disease. Still threatening.
ASEAN member states have introduced a series of measures, including fiscal and monetary policies, diversification and macro-prudent policies aimed at stabilizing the lives of the poor and vulnerable and supporting economic and social activities. In order to be highly effective, these measures should be focused on specific goals and implemented at appropriate stages and times to avoid moral hazards and unexpected results.
In addition, the experience of some countries in the region has also shown an increase in household debt levels caused by job losses and incomes, which has also posed a major challenge in the economic and financial sectors.
However, the Kovid-19 crisis also provided a number of opportunities, including the promotion of green investment, the development of a digital economy and the strengthening of regional cooperation to find new sources for economic growth, as well as strengthening economic resilience and resilience. Local Finance Meetings in Phnom Penh and Kandal Provides Two-Week Suspension to Prevent Kovid 19
