A report by the Ministry of Economy shows that in the first eight months of this year, Cambodia's exports reached 11.714 billion US dollars, an increase of 18 percent. High-growth goods such as rice accounted for 23.1 percent, bicycles for 17 percent, electricity for 22.3 percent and other agricultural products, and gold rose sharply to 716 percent. 8 percent. As of August 2020, gold exports totaled $ 2220 million.
In the first eight months of this year, imports totaled 11,853 million US dollars, down 11.6 percent.
According to the Ministry of Economy, in the first eight months of 2020, a total of 3,350 construction applications increased, 455 projects worth 5081 million US dollars, down 15 percent from the same period last year. The increase in the number of construction projects is mostly residential.
In the first eight months of this year, Cambodia received a total of 113 private investment projects, down 22 projects with a total investment of 2,329 million US dollars, down 57 percent. Despite the overall decline in investment projects, industrial investment projects increased by eight projects compared to the same period last year.
