General Knowledge: Where are the giant meteor craters that fell to kill dinosaurs?
(Earth): Scientists have discovered that dinosaurs became extinct 65 million years ago, their deaths, as well as many large asteroids fell to Earth and meteor craters. Those also see clear scars to this day.
Where are the meteorite craters located and what do they look like?
Scientists have discovered traces of 162 giant meteorite craters around the Earth that fell to Earth hundreds of millions of years ago and massacred dinosaurs.
Scientists have revealed that the oldest asteroid crater is about 200 million years old, that is, it fell to Earth before the extinction of the dinosaurs, but now traces of it. Gone.
Research has shown that our planet has been hit by five asteroids. Each collision kills terrestrial life and pollutes the earth's atmosphere.
