(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on November 10, 2020, issued a reminder once again to the owners of factories, especially textiles, footwear and travel products and bags. Cambodia to continue to properly implement the guidelines of the Ministry to continue to increase attention and strengthen the implementation of measures to prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
According to the announcement of the Ministry of Labor, which was received by Fresh News, in order to continue to increase attention and strengthen the implementation of measures to prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid 19 according to the guidelines of the Ministry of Health, factories and enterprises. All must be done as follows:
2. Manage, monitor, record and maintain on a daily basis the implementation of measures to prevent and control Kovid-19 to provide the competent authorities if necessary.
3. Arrange for alcohol or hand gel or hand soap at the entrance of the building for workers to wash their hands before entering the factory.
5. Prepare enough masks for the workers to be prescribed by the doctor, depending on the health condition and general condition of each worker.
6: Remind workers when coughing or sneezing, cover mouth and nose with a towel, scarf or elbow, then wash hands with soap or alcohol.
