(Siem Reap): Six male twins from two families in Siem Reap province received gifts from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross.
Mr. Seng Teang, Personal Assistant of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, accompanied by Mr. Kuch Lina, Member of Siem Reap Provincial Council, this morning, November 10, 2020, paid a courtesy call and distributed Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit gifts to the people. The three twins, both families, settled in Kralanh and Srey Snom districts of Siem Reap province.
Three male twins in the first family were born on August 27, 2020 at 3:30 pm at Kantha Bopha Hospital, Siem Reap Province. The first family has a father named Lan Kim Leang, 30 years old, and a mother named Tay Rany, 29 years old, born in Kampong Thkov 1 village, Kampong Thkov commune, Kralanh district, Siem Reap province, and have two children before their son.
Three male twin grandchildren in the second family were born on August 8, 2020 at 4 pm at Kantha Bopha Hospital, Siem Reap Province. The second family has a father named Tek Toun, 35 years old and a mother named Ros Mach, 30 years old, born in Sleng Spean village, Sleng Spean commune, Srey Snom district, Siem Reap province.
Donation from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, which were given to the three twin families. Each family received 50 kg of rice, 2 large boxes of milk, 05 kg of sugar, 2 scarves and 2 sarongs. And a budget of 5 million riels.
In front of the families of the twins, Mr. Seng Teang brought a message of deepest greetings from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, both of whom always send greetings to people everywhere. All places in Cambodia.
According to the personal assistant, from 1999 to the present, 369 families have given birth to three or four twins, and have received generous donations from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to help. Support for hardships in daily life, especially raising three twin children, who are the grandchildren of the two princes after giving birth.
Mr. Seng Teang continued that the number of families of three twin babies is even higher, which Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit supported through MPs and working groups to help people in villages, communes, districts, capitals and provinces last year. 1999.
Mr. Seng Teang added that all these donations were not donations from the Royal Government, donations from the Cambodian Red Cross or donations from political parties. On the contrary, all these gifts are the gifts born of the sincere and high-mindedness of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, who have realized the real difficulties for people who have given birth to triplets. Real people.
Mr. Seng Teang reminded all people to take care of hygiene, live clean, wash their hands with algae soap or hand wash to prevent the spread of the deadly Kovid disease that has been spreading around the world.
Representatives of the twin families expressed their deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit for always helping the people in all circumstances. Especially for people in distress, there is always the presence of both Samdech to intervene at all times. Spokesman for the General Commission: On November 10, another 765 vehicles were inspected and fined
