Today marks the 44th anniversary of the death of the eldest son of Samdech Techo Hun Sen due to the negligence of the Khmer Rouge midwives
(Phnom Penh): On November 10, 2020, it has been 44 years since the eldest son of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen passed away just minutes after his departure. Because of the negligence of midwives during the Khmer Rouge regime.
November 10, 1976 was the saddest event in the lives of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit and was an event that both Samdechs will never forget. Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit named their eldest son "Hun Komsat".
Every year, on November 10, Samdech Techo always remembers this bitter memory, and it is also a time when tears always roll down. For the year 2020, on November 2, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also commemorated this bitter history.
The following is the full text of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's post on Facebook on November 2, 2020, commemorating the tragic memories of the loss of his beloved son for the first time.
I feel that something bad is going to happen to me, because since I was growing up, I seem to have a caregiver who can tell me in advance what will happen in the future, both good and bad, through dreams or Through crying animals or other omens, etc. That night I missed Rany so much and thought Rani could give birth tonight. I did not sleep at all, and after 12 o'clock at night, the animals not only cried in the trees, but also in the trees outside the fort, they cried in horror.
