The spokesman for the Ministry of Environment said that the level of wild elephant hunting had been marked by a sharp decline in almost 20 years due to the authorities' ability to enforce the law. Well, more than 30 years ago, poaching killed many wild elephants.
At the same time, Mr. Net Pheaktra said: "In Cambodia today, there are about 400 to 600 Asian elephants, most of which live in the Cardamom Mountains, the northern plateau, the Tonle Sap and the highlands. The eastern part of Mondulkiri province, which is rich in biodiversity, ecosystems and slopes, favorable for the life of elephants and other wildlife. The number of domestic elephants is estimated at 71.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that as a result of the recent installation of automatic cameras in the South Cardamom Mountains National Park, out of seven elephants, four had traps attached to their legs and had children. A wild elephant also died from a trap.
According to estimates, the 10-year action plan for the conservation of Asian wild elephants requires $ 40.5 million, which is expected to come from a combination of government, NGO and partner budgets. Developments.
Farmers rush to harvest red corn after being affected by floods in Malai district, Banteay Meanchey province
(Banteay Meanchey): Farmers living along the Cambodian-Thai border rush to harvest red corn and cassava on their fields in Banteay Meanchey province's Mat Bai district after being affected by floods.
Meeting with Fresh News Agency in Banteay Meanchey province on November 9, 2020, farmers said that at the end of this year, they face difficulties, natural disasters, unfavorable, making his family life in chaos every day. Not selling because the sky is raining every day in a row, causing water in the fields, rotting tubers, damaging their cassava crops, not even a little bit left.
The farmer continued that this year he really lost a lot because he spent money to buy cassava to plant on 10 hectares of land and to buy corn seeds to plant on 1 hectare, hoping that when the harvest can be Sell some money to pay off debts and the rest to support daily life. But due to the natural disaster, the heavy rain made him very desperate and could not seem to find the money to pay off his debts.
Farmers say that in this corn field, the yield is only 10 percent because of the heavy rain, some corn sprouts in the fruit and some fall down the water, some damage.
The cost of harvesting corn is 7,000 riel per bag, and they can harvest more than 10 bags of corn per day. According to the farmers, the red corn crop in 2020 will not be as productive as last year, because when the corn is flowering and pruning, it rains too much every day, making the sugarcane, but when the corn is ripe, the sky is still raining. Causes corn kernels to sprout in the fruit.
Some places are forced to harvest immature potato tubers and it is difficult to transport them, while 1 kg of red corn traders buy 4.5 baht (Thai currency) and 1 kg of cassava traders buy 1.5 baht. The bottom is slightly lower than last year.
