67th Anniversary of Independence! Mr. Hun Many reveals the three depths of the word independence
He asserted that independence was not just a matter of words and deeds, but also of meaning:
* First: a turning point that Cambodia can successfully recapture the right to decide the fate of the nation by the Khmers themselves. This decision refers to independence, sovereignty, not allowing any country to direct the implementation of foreign policy, especially domestic politics in any form.
The people of this country do not condone the interference in the internal affairs of Cambodia and uphold the right to a proportional response, including the right to self-defense as a sovereign country.
* Second: It is proud that Cambodia itself has been able to achieve the development of the country from scratch to this day under a thorough and clear leadership with responsibility, dedication and upholding national interests and The population is large.
Cambodia has achieved a lot for the nation and its people in the last 40 years, especially 20 years after the win-win policy, but there is still much work to be done for the future of Cambodia as stated in 3C. Have a vision in 2050 that the people of Cambodia will receive a high income.
This miserable country went through a long war, internal divisions, the main causes of which were due to geopolitical factors in the region, especially during the Cold War, in which the people should not forget the 1970 coup d'état by Lon Nol. The deaths of millions of innocent Cambodians during the Khmer Rouge genocide and, most recently, the economic siege of the 1980s.
From these factors, the leaders took life as their capital, tried hard to stand up, and through all the sacrifices and sacrifices, the leaders liberated the nation, united the nation and promoted development to this day, which is what Cambodia Proud and the basis of believing that "Khmer can do", so people should be proud of the peace achieved for this difficult country and people.
Please be informed that on November 9, 1953, Cambodia gained full independence from the French Republic after this European power colonized Cambodia for almost a century, that is, since 1863.
