Nigerian Arrested After Taking Counterfeit Dollars to Pay Traffic Police at Chamkar Dong Steel Bridge in Dangkor District
(Phnom Penh): A traffic police force stationed at the former Chamkar Dong steel bridge traffic stop arrested a Nigerian man and handed him over to the Dangkor District Police Inspectorate after the foreigner took a counterfeit dollar bill and paid a traffic law fine on his own. Driving without respecting traffic lights. This incident happened at 10:40 AM on November 9, 2020.
During the payment of the fine, the foreigner handed over a $ 100 bill, but the police had no cash, so they exchanged it at two exchange offices, but it was confirmed that the money was counterfeit and the authorities handed it over to the person. The Nigerian was suddenly pulled out and torn in front of the police without paying a fine, so the police arrested him and handed him over to the Dangkor District Police Inspectorate for questioning.
Dangkor police confirmed that around this case, specialized forces were temporarily detained at the district police inspectorate to build a case to be sent to court to deal with the legal process related to the use of counterfeit money. General knowledge: Why British people put red poppy flowers on Shirt in November?
It seems strange that this superpower uses opium poppies as a kind of drug. It is even more noticeable for English football fans as all clubs also make shirts with poppy seeds for sports to wear for this November game.
Putting red poppy flowers on the shirt is a sign to commemorate the soldiers who lost their lives during World War I and to the people who were killed by terrorists. During the 11th of November, you will see millions of red poppies (now resinous) being sold across the country by thousands of volunteers (some to raise money for humanitarian work).
Please note that during the 11th of November, there are also many philanthropists donating money for humanitarian work. The money from the donations was used to help those who survived the war and whose lives were changed because of the war. The money also helps veterans who are looking for a new job or who need help.
For English football players or non-British residents, if you do not want to wear a shirt with poppy flowers, it is not forced. Not only poppy flowers on the shirts, institutions, sports clubs and many other places put poppy flowers to commemorate this day of remembrance.
