The following is the announcement of the Ministry of Labor: Spokesman of the General Commission: On November 08, 627 more vehicles were inspected and fined
(Phnom Penh): On November 08, 2020, the traffic police throughout Cambodia inspected and fined a total of 627 vehicles, including 479 motorcycles and 148 vehicles. This was confirmed by Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and spokesman for the National Police.
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, during the 192 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to November 8, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and A total of 209,386 vehicles were fined, including 1548,3030 motorcycles and 54,556 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorbikes are mostly without helmets, offenses, without license plates, drunkenness and using mobile phones. In particular, the offenses for cars are mostly speeding, overtaking, drunkenness, no driver's license, no seat belt and using a mobile phone.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 192 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
It should be noted that for November 08, 2020, there were 6 traffic accidents throughout Cambodia, in which 3 people were killed and 6 people were injured (3 people were seriously injured).
