Kampong Cham Provincial Authority Pumps Reserved Water for Dry Farming in Kang Meas District
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, on November 08, 2020, led a team of relevant officials to inspect the geography of Boeung Kak Dam and pump water for dry farming people in Kang Tanung Ty village. 8 Kang Tanung Commune, Kang Meas District, Kampong Cham Province.
According to residents in the area, every year, two communes, Kang Tanong and Sdao, in Kang Meas district, rely on the Boeung Kak Dam to pump water into their dry fields, but in 2020 This is due to the low level of flooding of the Mekong River, making it impossible for water to flow into the reservoir, and flooding in the fields, making it impossible for them to grow dry season rice.
Residents said that when the provincial authorities pump water from the rice fields, they will be able to grow dry rice. As for the stored water, they can use it to irrigate their rice fields when needed.
According to the Director of the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Um Vibol said that at the Boeung Kak Dam, his professional officers used two 65-horsepower engines to pump water until it stopped.
Mr. Um Vibol also confirmed that the two machines can pump about 130,000 cubic meters in the past 144 hours.
