Lt. Gen. You Serey Vuth explains to the active military students that Samdech Techo Hun Sen is the greatest and most powerful political and military leader in Cambodian history.
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. You Serey Vuth explained to active military students that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, is one of the greatest and most powerful political and military leaders in Cambodian history.
He explained this during a lecture on winning politics and peacekeeping to the students of the Active Military Academy on the afternoon of November 6, 2020.
For 22 years, under the umbrella of complete peace throughout the country under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who came to power through democratic elections, the Cambodian people have lived in peace and prosperity, and the nation has Grow and develop in all areas that have made Cambodia's reputation equal on the international stage, both regionally and globally.
The presence of the Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces on this occasion confirms that the Head of the Royal Government, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has taken care to solve all difficulties and support for the Armed Forces. Weapons of all kinds, especially every season, are the rainy season providing raincoats and the winter providing winter coats.
General Ith Sarath expressed his appreciation and appreciation to all officers and soldiers who have worked hard to fulfill the mission of national defense and defense of the territory according to their duties and achievements and achieve success.
At the same time, General Ith Sarath also conveyed greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Samdech Kittipritthbandit, Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to the officers and soldiers. When all the leaders are always concerned about the well-being of all the troops, no matter what the circumstances.
General Ith Sarath reminded the Armed Forces to continue to raise the patriotic conscience of the Royal Government, join forces to protect peace, prevent and crack down on unscrupulous people who have a plan to destroy the peace and continue to maintain all achievements. Born from the win-win policy of the lone peace leader Samdech Techo Hun Sen to bring more progress and prosperity for the people and society.
In addition, the General thanked all the forces involved in rescuing people from the disaster caused by the recent floods, according to the order of the Head of Government, Ministry of National Defense and Commander-in-Chief.
At the same time, General Ith Sarath also instructed all forces to continue to pay attention to help people in the work of transplanting and harvesting.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Bun Sambo, Secretary of State of the Office of the Council of Ministers and his family were invited to meet with the people living in Sangkat Boeung Thom, Khan Kampoul, Phnom Penh and give charitable gifts to the people affected by Kovid-19 and Flooding of 344 families this morning, November 7, 2020.
