General Vong Pisen Brings Food to Support Families Affected by Fire in Kampong Popil Market, Pearang District, Prey Veng Province
(Prey Veng): On the morning of November 7, 2020, General Vong Pisen, Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group visited Prey Veng province's Pearang district, and held a get-together and donated food to support vendors at Kampong Papil Market. Affected by the fire on November 4, 2020.
A social gathering and food distribution ceremony was held at Kampong Popil pagoda, Pearang district, with the participation of Mr. Sbong Sarath, Chairman of Prey Veng Provincial Council, together with many other officials of the Pearang District Field Team.
According to the report from Mr. Hi Thuok, Governor of Pearang District, the fire broke out at Kampong Popil Market in Pearang District at 9:00 pm on November 4, 2020, with a power outage and completely extinguished at 12 o'clock. : 30 minutes a night using a total of 21 water trucks. About 70 percent of the damage was done, with 75 stalls burning out of a total of 96 stalls, valued at about $ 1,080,000.
During the meeting, General Vong Pisen expressed his condolences to the business people who lost their property due to the fire and thanked all the people who participated in the firefighting on time without causing any harm to any people. No life.
General Vong Pisen requested the local authorities and market traders to meet and discuss in order to reach an agreement to reorganize the Kampong Popil market with a clean and safe environment to ensure safety in line with the development of the current society.
During the meeting, General Vong Pisen supported 99 families, each of whom received rice, noodles, fish sauce, soy sauce, orange juice, sarong and a total budget of more than 24 million riels.
On behalf of the business community, the Governor of Pearang District expressed his deep gratitude to General Vong Pisen, the leader of the provincial authorities, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit, who have always taken care of their lives and well-being. Condolences to the people in all circumstances.
