* First name: Panh Sopheak, 20 years old, Occupation: Worker, living in Village 2, Sangkat Kampong Svay, Serey Sophorn City * The two suspects, after being questioned, confessed that they had indeed stolen drugs.
After receiving the confession and the evidence, the two suspects were sent by the provincial drug crime office to the provincial court for further action.
Mr. Chea Chanto: Nothing is more valuable than peace
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Chanto, Permanent Member of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the National Task Force for Stong District, Kampong Thom Province, said that there is nothing more valuable than peace, so let's work together to protect peace, because if we protect Peace, we can preserve, have wealth and all the achievements we have survived.
Mr. Chea Chanto's remarks were made on November 5, 2020 on the occasion of his and his colleagues visiting monks and residents of Pov Wei commune, a commune in the middle of Tonle Sap Lake, Stong district, Kampong Thom province.
Mr. Chea Chanto said, "There is nothing more precious than peace, so if we can keep the peace, we can keep our wealth and all the achievements we have made and give us more ability and opportunity to continue to build and develop." More recent achievements.
He added that including the field of Buddhism, as well as the new temple, Wat Pov Wei, which is floating on the surface of the Tonle Sap Lake is a testament to this. Did we ever imagine that this remote area was as prosperous as it is today? There are things like today.
On that occasion, he also called on the monks and people living in Pov Wei commune in Stong district to continue to maintain good peace to protect the achievements of the ancient heritage and all the achievements built after the day of liberation to survive. Descendants have known and lived in peace.
Therefore, great care must be taken, including the effects of recent floods and other diseases.
