BEIJING, Nov. 6 (Xinhua) - Chinese President Xi Jinping on November 6, 2020, presented the "Friendship Medal of the People's Republic of China" to Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Queen Mother of Cambodia. Highly responds to his actions in contributing to the improvement of relations between Cambodia and China.
With the awarding ceremony, the Chinese President also expressed his efforts to promote and enhance better Cambodia-China relations. The President stressed that Cambodia and China must continue to push for a comprehensive strategic partnership to a new level.
During the meeting, the Chinese President praised the deepest friendship with His Majesty the King and Queen Mother and thanked them for sending messages of condolence and generous donations after the spread of COVID. -19 in China by both of them.
Xi Jinping said that the awarding of the "Friendship Medal of the People's Republic of China" to the Queen was not only a great appreciation for the special and important contribution made by the Queen. There is only good relations between China and Cambodia. But also to promote the deepest friendship between the people of China and Cambodia.
The Queen Mother of Cambodia also expressed her willingness to work for the betterment of Cambodia-China relations. "I will continue my efforts to strengthen Cambodia-China relations," she said.
It should be noted that the "Friendship of the People's Republic of China" award, presented by the Chinese government to the Cambodian Queen Mother, is the highest level award for outstanding foreign dignitaries who have actively contributed to the modernization of Chinese socialism. Exchanging cooperation between China and foreign countries and safeguarding world peace.
As the wife of the head of state of a country, she warmly served and contributed with the King Father in welcoming a high-level Chinese delegation to Cambodia. Especially after the political situation in Cambodia changed dramatically in the aftermath of the March 8 coup, both of them had to flee to Beijing.
During his life in exile in Beijing, he served as the personal secretary of His Majesty the King, assisting in the preparation of correspondence, documents, and the publication of information related to the press. Situation of Cambodia will fulfill its role as President of the Cambodian Red Cross under the framework of the Royal Government of National Unity of Cambodia.
The Queen Mother of Cambodia continued that since the coup d'etat, she has been forced to engage in important political activities by trying to understand international affairs and especially the circumstances around Cambodia.
Through many years of relations since President Mao Zedong, Her Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia has been considered by Chinese leaders as an important witness for this historic friendship, and Chinese leaders of all generations have always welcomed the royal welcome. Greatest condolences to him, especially every time he was in the People's Republic of China.
