A woman was seriously injured after a thief robbed her of jewelry in the middle of a rice field in Ang Snoul district, the suspect was finally arrested!
(Phnom Penh): A woman was seriously injured after being robbed by some suspects with an ax while she was visiting a field. After the robbery, the suspect escaped, but the suspect was apprehended by several villagers and beaten, injuring 18 stitches in the head, scratching the skin on the right neck and swelling on the right cheek.
The robbery happened on November 6, 2020 at a rice field in Rokar Thom village, Bek Chan commune, Ang Snoul district, Kandal province.
After the arrest, the suspects were confiscated: an ax, a wooden pole, a 2.50-meter-long ox, a gray backpack, a sharp metal case, two plastic handles, two door keys, and a red cable. A Cambodian named Leng Chantha, two metal triggers and a piece of paper, a platinum necklace (belonging to the victim).
At 08:20, the suspects were found by the public, and the suspects fought and injured, so the Phnom Penh police arrived and arrested them and handed them over to the Ang Snoul district authorities. The suspect was taken to Ang Snoul District Referral Hospital for treatment.
Currently, the criminal force of the Ang Snoul District Inspectorate is building a case to send the suspect to court for legal action. The King Congratulates the Queen Mother on Receiving the "Friendship of the People's Republic of China" Medal
