(Phnom Penh): On November 6, 2020, the traffic police throughout Cambodia inspected and fined a total of 1,174 vehicles, including 895 motorcycles and 279 cars. This was confirmed by Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and spokesman for the National Police.
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, during the 190 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to November 6, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and A total of 207,841 vehicles were fined, including 153,748 motorcycles and 54,093 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 190 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for November 6, 2020, traffic accidents across Cambodia also occurred 10 times, in which 12 people died and 15 people were injured (06 seriously injured).
