Boundary Committee and Senate Committee Meet to Pass the Draft Law on the Approval of the Boundary Protocol and the Cambodia-Vietnam Land Border Post
(Phnom Penh): The Joint Committee on Border Affairs of Cambodia this morning (November 6, 2020) held a meeting with the Senate Expert Committee to pass a draft law on the approval of the border demarcation and land border posts between Cambodia and Cambodia. Vietnam before being included in the upcoming plenary session for review and approval.
Ms. Koy Pisey, Deputy Director of the Permanent Secretariat of the National Authority for Border Affairs, confirmed to Fresh News that in this meeting, the Joint Committee on Border Affairs led by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense and Mr. Var Kimhong, Senior Minister in charge of Border Affairs, while the Senate is headed by Mr. Sok Isan, Chairman of the Fourth Commission and representatives of nine other commissions.
She added that the border demarcation and land border demarcation between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Socialist Republic of Vietnam was signed on October 5, 2019 during Samdech Techo Hun Sen's two-day official visit to Vietnam. .
The Draft Law on the Approval of the Protocol for the Demarcation of Khan Boundary and Land Boundary between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Socialist Republic of Vietnam was approved by the Council of Ministers on October 9, 2020 and was fully approved by the National Assembly. On November 2, 2020, with 116 out of 116 votes.
