(Phnom Penh): The Royal Academy of Cambodia on November 6, 2020, published a book entitled The Right Way for Cambodia to Maintain Peace and Towards Development 2008-2018.
This book is compiled by a group of nine scholars to reflect the historical truth in Cambodian society and is a record of the significant achievements of the Cambodian government over the past 10 years, held at the Khmer Art Heritage Hall of the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
A book featuring the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, entitled "The Right Way for Cambodia to Maintain Peace and Towards Development 2008-2018" was officially released on November 6. This book is compiled by a team of nine doctors led by Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
The book "The Right Way for Cambodia to Maintain Peace and Towards Development 2008-2018" is a research achievement under the direct supervision of Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia and Permanent Vice President of the Council of Professors. Has spent three years researching and highlighting the path to peace in Cambodia and the development of the country in the past, especially from 2008 to 2018.
In addition to highlighting the progress and achievements of the Royal Government in the past mandate, the book "The Right Way for Cambodia to Maintain Peace and Towards Development 2008-2018" also analyzes the current situation, challenges and makes recommendations to It is also an input for the continuous development of the nation.
Researchers at the Royal Academy of Cambodia hope that this book will be useful to politicians, researchers, any aspect that can be cited as an experience, a lesson or a strategy for people in the future.
