According to the Cambodian Movement for Health's interviews with cigarette dealers, the duty-free cigarettes were distributed by cigarette companies and bought directly from wholesalers. The cigarette seller said that the agent of the cigarette company always distributes cigarettes to them, and when there is no company agent, he goes to buy directly at the wholesale depot.
On this issue, Dr. Yil Daravuth, Technical Officer for Tobacco Product Control of the World Health Organization, expressed the opinion that cigarettes without tax stamps are illegal. Illegal smoking is a major obstacle to tobacco control in Cambodia, as it not only reduces the state's tax revenue, but also puts people at greater risk of diseases caused by smoking. Tobacco increased.
Tobacco use poses a serious risk to the health of the population and causes enormous economic losses. Each year, about 15,000 Cambodians die from diseases caused by tobacco use and lose about $ 656 million.
