General knowledge: Which metal conducts electricity the best?
In addition to being used as jewelry, a large amount of silver is now used in the photographic industry, as well as in durable batteries and as solar panels.
Silver has the unique property of disinfecting water with a minimum amount of only 1 / 100,000,000,000. This amazing fact has been known since 500 BC, when Herodotus recorded that the emperor Cyrus of Persia always drank boiled water and put it in a silver jar.
On the other hand, the ancient Romans and Greeks also observed that food and drink in silver vessels were not perishable.
