Please be informed that immediately after receiving the news that the Hungarian Minister of Foreign Affairs is infected with Kovid 19, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on the night of November 4, 2020 issued an urgent press release on measures for educational institutions with staff or students. Involved in the official visit of the Hungarian delegation to Cambodia.
Due to recent developments related to Kovid-19 disease, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports calls on schools, parents and students to implement the following measures:
* Institutions with staff participating and communicating directly with the Hungarian delegation must suspend their studies for 14 days from the date of this announcement and resume teaching and learning online.
Employees and stakeholders must be self-employed for 14 days. Professors, educators, students and students involved in the Hungarian delegation must report to the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports at 012 335 999 by November 05, 2020
* School management, educators, students, parents and guardians of the above institutions must raise the highest level of vigilance and continue to monitor personal health. In case of doubt, contact the hotline of the Ministry of Health.
