Ministry of Economy Holds a Course on Strategic Planning, Budgeting and Budgeting for the Anti-Corruption Unit
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance this morning, November 05, 2020, opened a training course on "Strategic Planning, Budgeting and Program Budget Monitoring" for the target trainees who are civil servants of the opposition unit. Corruption.
The opening ceremony was presided over by Dr. Hean Sahip, Secretary of State and Chairman of the Capacity Building Working Group of the Ministry of Economy and Finance; Objects, leaders of the Anti-Corruption Unit, trainers and trainees, a total of about 100 people.
Speaking at the ceremony, Dr. Hean Sahip, Secretary of State, emphasized that the reform of public financial management is one of the key reform programs of the Royal Government in order to change the Cambodian budget system from the budget. Inputs and decentralization towards the budget based on achievements and decentralization to contribute to national socio-economic development.
He said that building and developing professional capacity is a necessary requirement for leaders and civil servants of all ministries and institutions to participate in understanding and strengthening the capacity to carry out work more effectively. In this regard, the Ministry of Economy and Finance has considered and paid close attention to the development of professional capacity, which supports and contributes to the implementation of public financial management reform.
He highlighted a number of key aspects of the 2018-2025 Budget System Reform Strategy, which aims to transform the Cambodian budget system into an efficient, accountable and transparent system in line with international best practices. Socio-economic development of the nation.
The program budget is an important core of the budget management system based on performance and decentralization, and the budget must be based on a clear program to achieve the objectives of policies, ministries, institutions in line with policies in each sector.
He emphasized that the strategic budget plan is a mechanism of the annual budgeting process in which each ministry plans to implement a budget for the implementation of priority programs or strategies in line with the policies of the ministries and institutions. The implementation of the annual budget needs to be monitored to direct activities towards the planned results in the year.
Budget units or ministries use three main tools to ensure effectiveness, namely: regular or periodic review of program implementation, second: reporting on budget implementation, and third: Evaluate and compare the results of the implementation of the program with the planned target indicators.
Spokesman for the General Commission: On November 5, another 1,022 vehicles were inspected and fined
(Phnom Penh): On November 5, 2020, the traffic police throughout Cambodia inspected and fined a total of 1,022 vehicles, including 742 motorcycles and 280 cars. This was confirmed by Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and spokesman for the National Police.
