On November 4, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen had already tested 19 for Kovid virus, with a negative result. Through Samdech's Facebook, Samdech claims to be in good health and strictly follows the instructions of the Ministry of Health to wait for the next 19 Kovid virus tests.
From the time of taking the sample at 12 noon on November 4, I have been doing cataracts for more than 30 hours. There is nothing strange in the body at all. What is different is that my wife and I share a room and do not dare to touch each other like when we were young.
Servants must wear masks, socks, and gloves as directed by their physician. In this case, my wife and I have to take the test up to 4 times. The first will be held on November 4, the second will be held on November 9, the third will be held on November 14 and the fourth will be held on November 18, 2020.
If the next three tests are not positive, Kovid 19, my wife and I, as well as 18 other people, I will leave on a separate day on November 19 or 20, when I ask my children to bring me grandchildren. Come and take my mother's hand back to my father's room.
