BEIJING (Reuters) - A Chinese military spokesman recently voiced strong opposition to the US plan to sell drones to Taiwan. This is according to a quote from the Xinhua news agency on Thursday evening, November 5, 2020.
China has therefore urged the United States to immediately cancel all arms sales to Taiwan and other military agreements with the island to avoid damaging bilateral ties, including peace and stability in the region.
China's reaction comes after the US State Department on Tuesday announced plans to sell four of its advanced MQ-9 Reaper drones to Taiwan. The United States has also planned to sell billions of dollars worth of other weapons, such as missiles and missile launchers, to Taiwan.
