Mr. Hun Many announced the launch of the Clean Phnom Penh Campaign 2020 with the key slogan "Clean as a new habit"
The ceremony took place on November 4, 2020 at the main hall of the new National Sports Training Center under the presidency of Mr. HUN Many, Member of the National Assembly and co-founder of Clean Project.
This campaign aims to raise awareness of the current state of "clean words" in the context of Kovid 19 for the running of the Clean Phnom Penh 2020 campaign.
Since the global epidemic of Kovid-19 invaded nations around the world during the turn of the new decade, "cleanliness" has become a global trend and a new habit that humanity needs and adheres to.
As a contribution to the World Health Organization and the Ministry of Health, this year's Clean Phnom Penh Campaign under the new direction will encourage modern people to implement the principles of cleanliness and safety measures from 19 Kovid infections, including wearing Massage consistently when necessary, wash hands frequently with soap, alcohol or gel, keep a social distance, avoid contact with animals or patients, cough and fever.
In addition, "Clean as a New Habit" has been truly associated with proper waste management and management, which has been the main mission of the Clean Phnom Penh Campaign since its first appearance in 2017.
The Executive Team of the Clean Phnom Penh Campaign also organized a "Clean Environment School" concept project competition to provide opportunities for students in public and private high schools, as well as students at a number of universities in Phnom Penh to share their experiences and insights in the field. Environment.
In that, based on the spirit of innovation, progress as well as innovation in the context of the Industrial Revolution 4.0 to achieve "cleanliness" "environmental friendliness" as well as the proper storage and management of waste with self-ownership in Fulfilling obligations as a model citizen.
In addition to the "Clean Environment School" action plan, the Clean Phnom Penh Campaign has brought innovative ideas to promote its outreach.
The "Clean Phnom Penh Campaign" was created by six co-founders, including Hun Many, Tep Kolap, Chi Sela, Chea Sophalla, Hay Phirum and Heng Thida, who initiated the project.
In 2020, the Clean Phnom Penh Campaign of Clean Project has received the cooperation and support as well as the full support of the Ministry of Environment and Administration, Phnom Penh Capital Hall, as well as the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, which has cooperated and supported in "Clean Environment School" concept project.
The "Clean Phnom Penh Campaign" also received cooperation from relevant ministries, government institutions, private companies, associations, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions from secondary to higher education, both public and private, as well as from the public. Check out the main gallery of international events on November 4, 2020! (Photo inside)
