He added that the Koh Kong Vocational Training Center, which is far from the school, has a suitable place to stay, so those who have lost their education and wish to learn more, please come and register to continue learning. National Assembly Expert Committee and Representatives of the Royal Government Discuss Two Draft Laws
(Phnom Penh): Before reaching the agenda for the upcoming plenary session of the National Assembly, the National Assembly Expert Committee and representatives of the Royal Government met to review the draft law on state securities and the draft law on the preparation and Behavior of non-bank financial services authorities.
The meeting was held on the morning of November 4, 2020 at the National Assembly building, chaired by Dr. Rath Cheam Yeap, Chairman of the Second Committee of the National Assembly, and a representative of the Royal Government, chaired by Dr. Aid Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance. With the participation of various expert committees.
Dr. continued that the draft law on securities has 5 chapters and 16 articles. This law contains important principles and important tools for mobilizing both domestic and foreign financing for social development. Amendments to the Securities and Exchange Act are a fair and practical tool of the law, as well as relevant regulations in force that allow the government to use the financing for additional financing.
Dr. said that this law also has a negative effect on the management of trading and management of state securities issued on behalf of the Royal Government. The new draft law on securities has been amended in almost every article of the Law on Securities of 2007, and the Royal Government has added content to suit the real situation of Cambodia in the region and the world.
At the same time, Dr. Rath also mentioned about the organization and functioning of the Non-Banking Financial Services Authority in 5 chapters, 8 sections and 25 articles. The draft law was made in response to the rise of the non-banking financial sector.
He said that the draft law was made to integrate the mechanisms of management and control of the non-banking financial sector, including the insurance and private pension sector, securities sector, social security sector, administration sector, accounting sector and so on. Auditing and real estate, collateral and granting in order to strengthen and ensure the effectiveness of management, control and development of the non-banking financial sector.
Please be informed that the draft law on state securities and the draft law on the organization and functioning of the Non-Banking Financial Services Authority were approved by the Council of Ministers on September 4, 2020.
