Small and Medium Enterprise Bank of Cambodia will launch a public pilot business from November 5 onwards
Under the smart vision of the Royal Government of Cambodia to promote the development of small and medium enterprises for growth and sustainable growth, which is the basis for diversification and economic growth in the SME sector in Cambodia. Was initiated.
The main mission of the SME Bank of Cambodia is to provide effective and efficient financing and banking services to support small and medium enterprises, promote economic diversification and expand export volume in line with the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia. Small and Medium Enterprise Bank of Cambodia offers four main additional benefits to the community, including:
1: Provide affordable financing and simplify financing procedures, 2: Provide technical assistance to small and medium enterprises to increase productivity and product efficiency, 3: Provide business consulting support and 4: Promote expansion Local market.
As a policy and commercial financial institution, the SME Bank of Cambodia has the role of implementing the strategic goals of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025 by providing financing in Affordable and convenient for small and medium enterprises to access financing, focusing on five priority areas:
1: Manufacture and processing of food, 2: Manufacturing of local consumer goods, processing of waste and production of goods for tourism 3: Manufacturing of finished products or parts or components to supply other industries 4: Research and Development of information technology, including the provision of innovative information technology management services.
In addition to the products and credit services provided to small and medium enterprises, the SME Bank of Cambodia will provide safe and profitable savings services to the public, such as savings accounts, children's accounts, retirement accounts, current accounts and Fixed deposit and so on. Please wear a helmet when driving a motorcycle! 3 killed and 10 injured in traffic accidents nationwide on November 4 yesterday
