(Phnom Penh): On November 4, 2020, the traffic police throughout Cambodia inspected and fined a total of 1,167 vehicles, including 897 motorcycles and 270 cars. This was confirmed by Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and spokesman for the National Police.
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, during the 188 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to November 4, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and A total of 205,645 vehicles were fined, including 152,111 motorcycles and 53,534 vehicles of all types.
