Tensions between China and Taiwan are at an all-time high?
For decades, Taiwan has learned to live with the Chinese leader's warning that they will always be ready to seize territory that China considers part of it. But now tensions between Taiwan and China seem to have reached a tipping point through the deepening of Chinese military aircraft moves closer to Taiwan, as well as the release of video of Chinese troops depicting the invasion of Taiwan and attacks on Taiwan. US base in Guam.
Failing to win the heart of Taiwan, it is likely that Chinese President Xi Jinping has taken the most hostile stance toward Taiwan since Mao Zedong. Xi did not hide anything about his goal. The Chinese president considered taking control of Taiwan as an inevitable necessity for the future of all Chinese people.
During a visit to a Chinese military base last October, Xi told the army to prepare for war. Former U.S. Navy intelligence chief for the Pacific, James Fanell, has said that in the next 10 years, China may take action in some form against Taiwan.
According to Fanell, the reason why China's policy design on Taiwan is so dangerous now compared to past tensions is that China may now have enough military power to conquer Taiwan. Any aggression will cause China to sacrifice a small amount of value.
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of November 4, 2020, General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, brought a winter coat, a gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen. Distributed to the Gendarmerie. The distribution of winter coats took place at the Royal Gendarmerie Institute (KPOL), accompanied by the leadership, commanders, and deputy commanders of the General Command.
