At the same time, General Vong Pisen mentioned that the value of peace that is happening in Cambodia today is difficult to find and very important for the nation and people. In this regard, the General called on all forces to work together to maintain peace, no matter what the cost.
The Commander-in-Chief, on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, thanked all the forces for their conscientious and responsible efforts to protect the legitimate Royal Government and timely suppress all acts of treason. The unscrupulous maintain peace, stability, social order and peace of the people.
In addition, the General thanked all the forces that have participated in the rescue of people from the disaster by the recent floods, according to the order of the Head of Government, Ministry of National Defense and Commander-in-Chief. The general further instructed the forces to continue to pay attention to assisting the people in transplanting and harvesting.
