The Singaporean Ambassador's support for the use of the riel was made on the occasion that Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, allowed him to pay a courtesy call and bid farewell before his end. Mandate on December 31, 2020 after completing a four-year mission in Cambodia.
The Ambassador joined in congratulating and expressing his support for the Royal Government of Cambodia's and the National Bank of Cambodia's policy on promoting the use of the riel, which has been consistently successful and improving the effectiveness of monetary policy in Cambodia. .
The Ambassador thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia as well as the National Bank of Cambodia for strengthening bilateral cooperation and facilitating trade and investment between the two countries. In the banking and financial sector, Singapore has significantly increased its investment, with Singapore-based stakeholders including Phillip Bank Plc. And Cambodia Post Bank contributing to the growth of the banking sector.
In terms of bilateral relations between the two central banks, the National Bank of Cambodia has good relations with the Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS) through information exchange, human resource training and cooperation in various fields.
Please be informed that in 2019, the National Bank of Cambodia and the Monetary Authority of Singapore signed a Memorandum of Understanding on Bilateral Cooperation in the Field of Financial Innovation, which aims to establish a framework for cooperation between the two central banks to promote innovation. Finance in the markets of the countries.
Through this Memorandum, the two central banks can share information on trends and developments in emerging financial technology markets, as well as regulations related to innovations in financial services.
The Governor also thanked the Government of Singapore as well as the Monetary Authority of Singapore for supporting Cambodia as well as the National Bank of Cambodia in developing the capacity building of NBC staff through scholarships and training, sharing experiences in The banking sector has also contributed to boosting financial innovation in Cambodia.
Mr. Chea Chanto praised the Ambassador's contribution to strengthening bilateral cooperation between the two countries as well as the two central banks during his mission in Cambodia.
