Top US security official: "No foreigner has interfered in the US presidential election"
WASHINGTON, Nov. 3 (Xinhua) - Acting Secretary of Homeland Security Chad Wolf as the new presidential election is being held across the United States on Tuesday, November 3, 2020. ) Claimed that there was no evidence that there was any interference in the presidential election by foreigners. According to a release by CNA.
The remarks by a senior US security official come as Americans continue to run for re-election amid fears of possible election interference by attackers. Foreigners, as some American politicians have warned in the past.
"We have not received any sign that any foreigner has succeeded in interfering in the election," Wolf told a news conference. This statement is seen as encouraging people to calm down and go to the polls. More than 240 million Americans are eligible to vote this term, while more than 90 million have already cast their ballots early.
