Discover: The US Presidential Election Process Held on November 3, 2020
This problem is due to the "representative election system". If so, which will be Mr. Tram or Mr. Biden who will win? Before knowing the answer, we should first understand how the US electoral system works.
1: Who do Americans vote for?
On November 3, 2020, Americans will vote by mail or go to the polls to drop their ballots. As of Thursday, more than 40 million Americans had cast their ballots early, either directly or by mail, according to the BBC.
2: How many representative voters are there?
3: How does the representative voter system work?
According to Article 2 of Article 2 of the Constitution of the United States, the President and Vice President shall be elected by the electorate. The US Constitution does not specify the election of representatives, but each state in the United States has its own electoral system.
It should be noted that the above is just a description of the normal conduct of the presidential election process. That is, in the event of a dispute or no winner can be found, the electoral procedure may change with the intervention of the Supreme Court or both houses of the United States Congress, depending on the circumstances.
5: What methods should be used to resolve post-election controversy?
