General knowledge: Discover ASEAN
The five founding countries, with the exception of Thailand, were all newly occupied territories from the yoke of colonization at that time. Combined with the onset of the Cold War, the five countries are working together to establish this association with the common goal of promoting peace, stability, economic growth, as well as social and cultural development in the whole of Southeast Asia.
Since 1984, five other countries in the region, including Brunei, Vietnam, Laos, Myanmar and Cambodia, have been the youngest members of the association.
2: The purpose of establishing ASEAN
4. ASEAN Secretariat and Meeting * ASEAN Secretariat The ASEAN Administrative Center is the ASEAN Secretariat based in Jakarta, Indonesia, with the Secretary-General in charge of coordinating and implementing ASEAN activities. The Secretary-General shall be appointed by the ASEAN Summit for a term of five years, alternately in the alphabetical order of the English names of the Member States.
The ASEAN Charter stipulates that the selection of the Secretary-General shall be based on conditions such as integrity, work experience, competence and gender equality. The Secretariat is responsible for coordinating the implementation of ASEAN projects and activities.
* ASEAN Meetings All major decisions related to the destiny of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) are to be made by the ASEAN Summit, which takes place annually in the ASEAN Chairmanship. In addition to the summit, there are other meetings, such as ministerial meetings by sector.
The major decisions related to the fate of ASEAN are based on consensus (unanimous decision) as outlined in the existing principles. Since its inception, ASEAN has best implemented this governance principle, despite sometimes regional challenges.
* ASEAN Chairmanship Article 31 of the ASEAN Charter states that "The ASEAN Chairmanship shall be rotated annually in the alphabetical order of the Member States' English names" and the Member States holding the ASEAN Chairmanship shall chair the Summit. ASEAN and other meetings. In the past, Cambodia has chaired ASEAN twice, the first time in 2002 and the second time in 2012.
The 27th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting in Bangkok, July 22-23, 1994, issued a statement reaffirming the direction of AFTA, including: * Encourage the inflow of foreign investment * Agree to trade with other parts of the world.
