(Preah Vihear): Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, told the people not to encroach on state land and set up posts on new state land, which is illegal and is strictly prohibited.
The relevant competent authorities and the armed forces must comply with the laws, regulations and laws in force as well as the regulations of the Royal Government effectively and with a high sense of responsibility to maintain the country's natural resources for future generations.
During the ceremony of handing over real estate ownership certificates to 583 families equal to 831 plots of land in Chhep Keut village, Chhep Muy commune, Chhep district, Preah Vihear province, this morning, November 3, 2020, Mr. Prak Sovann stated that To be distributed to the people today as a result of the implementation of the Land Administration Subcommittee on Systematic Land Registration.
In the campaign to implement the old policy, new activities in the field of land for Preah Vihear province, a new step of deep land reform to solve the situation of land tenure to be safe, strong, farmers have agricultural land to do business to improve livelihoods Which is the policy of the Royal Government to reduce poverty and promote national economic growth.
The provincial governor also said that no individual could be deprived of his land if it was not in the public interest. Withdrawals shall be made in accordance with laws and regulations after proper and fair compensation has been provided in advance. In this sense, he said that from now on, our people have the security of occupying their land, the land abuse that has been experienced in the past has been completely ended.
At the same time, the Governor of Preah Vihear Province advised all relevant authorities to coordinate as much as possible, both in the mechanism and outside the mechanism, before sending to the provincial administration when there is a land dispute in the local area. Any anarchic logging or land claims that do not actually occupy the land for any other reason cannot be resolved.
In the second phase, the Royal Government will continue to provide social land concessions on a regular basis, accelerating the pace for the families of veterans, disabled veterans, and families and the poor who are in dire need of land. Therefore, in the case of encroachment on state land, setting up posts on new state land is strictly prohibited. And for the issuance of certificates, possession and use of non-communal land is strictly prohibited.
Mr. Prak Sovann commended the Governor of Chhep District and the Director of the Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs, as well as the Village, Commune and Special Authorities, all technical officers of the Provincial Land Management Department for their hard work. Success and thanks to all the people who have actively participated in the role of landowners, border guards and witnesses in this systematic land registration.
