(Banteay Meanchey): As of this morning, November 3, 2020, the police have identified the victim of a woman who was brutally murdered, who was found dead on November 2, 2020 at the injection site. Garbage near Reak Achm Bridge in Makak Village, Sangkat Makak, Serey Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
There, she had a romantic relationship and lived like a couple with a widower who was a laborer, but the couple who took the couple did not get along. Authorities say that before and after the murder, the man is still missing.
Please be reminded that at 7:30 AM on November 2, 2020, the body of a woman was found in the water of a rice field south of Phnom Top Bridge, called Reak Achm Bridge, 150 meters east of National Road 56. A about 10 meters north of the road is in Kbal Spean village, Sangkat Makak, Serey Sophorn city, Banteay Meanchey province.
Authorities said that prior to the incident, a 65-year-old man named Ang Sour from Kbal Spean village, Makak commune, Serey Sophorn city, Banteay Meanchey province, went to see the rice fields at the above point. At that time, he saw a branch holding a rice plant and grabbed it. Suddenly, he saw the victim's hand emerge and ran to report to the police at the administrative post to check.
Later, Brigadier General Sithi Loh, Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner, led the Serious Crime Police Force, the Technical Police Scientific Force and the Serei Sophorn City Police Force to conduct a thorough examination and forensic examination. On the body, there was a stab wound with a hard object, a sharp point of suffocation, a wound on the right side of the neck and several scratches on the surface.
Brigadier General Sithi Loh confirmed that the body was wearing a red T-shirt, long sleeves, sports pants. Police at the scene found a pair of glasses and a sharp knife.
