Spokesman for the General Commission: On November 3, another 1,074 vehicles were inspected and fined
(Phnom Penh): On November 3, 2020, the traffic police throughout Cambodia inspected and fined a total of 1,074 vehicles, including 821 motorcycles and 253 cars. This was confirmed by Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and spokesman for the National Police.
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, during the 187 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to November 2, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and A total of 204,478 vehicles were fined, including 151,214 motorcycles and 53,264 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorbikes are mostly without helmets, offenses, without license plates, drunkenness and using mobile phones. The offenses for cars are mostly speeding, overtaking, drunkenness, no driver's license, no seat belt and using a mobile phone.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kimkhoeun continued that for the past 187 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
It should be noted that for November 3, 2020, there were 10 traffic accidents throughout Cambodia, in which 7 people were killed and 12 injured (8 seriously injured).
Mr. Sous Yara: Despite the spread of 19 communicable diseases, the disease has not disrupted the friendly relations, solidarity and good cooperation between Cambodia and Hungary.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sous Yara, Deputy Chairman of the Committee on Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation, Propaganda and Information of the National Assembly and Member of Parliament for Preah Vihear Province, said that despite the spread of 19 communicable diseases, the disease has not Do not disturb the friendly relations, solidarity and good cooperation between the two countries, Cambodia - Hungary.
During the meeting, Sous Yara praised the visit of Peter Sichato and his delegation to Cambodia at a time when the world was plagued by the 19 cases of Kovid.
"Despite the spread of 19 communicable diseases, the disease has not disrupted the friendly relations, solidarity and good cooperation between Cambodia and Hungary," he said. In particular, the close relationship between Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister and leaders of Hungary.
During the cordial meeting between Mr. Sous Yara and Mr. Peter Sichato, they also exchanged views on the important points of strengthening the cooperation between the legislatures of the two countries, Cambodia-Hungary and the exchange of experiences on tourism in During the outbreak of Kovid 19 and so on.
