Ministry of Commerce Holds a Workshop to Promote and Deliver Potential Cambodian Products for Domestic and Overseas Markets to Banteay Meanchey Traders
(Banteay Meanchey): The Ministry of Commerce has organized a workshop on promoting and sending potential Cambodian products for domestic and foreign markets to traders in Banteay Meanchey province, co-organized by the Marketing Development Department, General Department of Trade Promotion of the Ministry. Commerce Department of Commerce.
The workshop was chaired by Mr. Ly Sary, Deputy Governor and represented by Mr. Ou Rathrey, Governor of Banteay Meanchey, Mr. Ouch Savin, Director of Marketing Development Department, General Department of Trade Promotion of the Ministry of Commerce, with the participation of the Department of Commerce. Relevant organizations, businesses and enterprises in the province participated in the opening ceremony of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Hall on November 3, 2020.
The workshop also featured tips as well as experiences from speakers from companies and enterprises, as well as questions from business people in the participating provinces.
CRC Donations Continue to Distribute to 100 Flood Families in Sangkat Choam Chao III, Khan Por Sen Chey
(Phnom Penh): An additional 100 poor families affected by the floods in Sangkat Choam Chao III, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, received a humanitarian donation from the Cambodian Red Cross by Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen.
The distribution ceremony took place on the afternoon of November 3, 2020 at Wat Champouvorn in Sangkat Choam Chao III, Khan Por Senchey, with the participation of Mr. Hem Darith, District Governor, Mrs. Chhun Sunny, Deputy District Governor, Mrs. Im Thavy Chairman of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch Committee, Mr. Yin Kea, Director of Khan Administration, Mr. Va Savoeun, Chief of Sangkat Choam Chao II 3, as well as Khan, Sangkat, Village and other officials.
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Hem Darith sent a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit to all the people, who always take care of the well-being of the people at all times.
He said that the prince always instructed the members of each district to visit the local level to know the well-being, challenges and practical needs, take appropriate and urgent measures. Gifts distributed to 100 families on this occasion, each family received 25 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 1 stick of fish sauce, 1 stick of soy sauce and 50,000 Riels.
641 Property Ownership Certificates Distributed to People in Koul Lap Commune, Chit Borei District
(Kratie): Mr. Hoeur Siyem, Chairman of Kratie Provincial Council, on November 3, 2020, presided over the handing over ceremony of 641 real estate ownership certificates and 405 families were distributed to landowners in Kampor village. In Koulab commune, Chit Borei district, with the participation of you from the departments of the three types of armed forces and the district and commune authorities.
Mr. Yin Botum, Deputy Director of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs of Kratie Province, also said that the project has distributed cards to people in Kambor village in Koulab commune, Chit Borei district, a total of 405 families, equivalent to 641 cards.
The deputy director of the department added that the old land tenure certificate issued by the Cadastral Administration has expired from today. In fact, the issuance of land titles at this time is done after systematic measurement, registration and posting of land judgments.
On that occasion, Mr. Hoeur Siyem said that the systematic land registration took place throughout the province, whether public or private, with the cooperation of property owners and the identification documents recognized by the relevant authorities at each stage. For the benefit of the landowners, they have full rights to occupy and manage in accordance with the law.
The Chairman of the Provincial Council also informed about the legal rights of the people that the Royal Government of Cambodia has given to the management of the land, the enjoyment of the right to use the land and the right to manage its land.
Providing ownership to the people now is the policy of the Royal Government to contribute to encourage and encourage people to strive to increase productivity as well as investment in agriculture to increase even more.
In addition, the issuance of title deeds to the people now also contributes to resolving land disputes between people and people between companies, which in the past has always occurred, affecting people's lives, causing great complications. To the competent authority.
He added that the clarification of the land tenure of the people clearly shows the win-win policy of the Royal Government on the land sector to provide economic concessions to investment companies to encourage the sector. The private sector has contributed to local development more effectively and truly benefits the people living there.
