Senior official of the Ministry of Rural Development: Kovid 19 pushed Cambodia's economy down, but expects growth again next year
(Prey Veng): Due to the spread of 19 smallpox worldwide, including in Cambodia, we have also pushed the economy down sharply, but expect to recover next year. This was stated by Mr. Van Sam Oeun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Rural Development, on November 3, 2020 at the Knowledge Sharing Workshop on the concept of community development in Prey Veng province.
He said that the meeting was attended by professional officials from the Ministry of Rural Development in the provinces and aims to include:
* Share knowledge to the officers in charge of community development of the Department of Rural Development of the Capital, Provinces, relevant departments and partner organizations that are implementing community development activities and capacity building of CEC
* Define input on community development concepts for updating community development strategic plans and for national rural development policies.
* Find out the strengths, weaknesses and challenges related to community development work and capacity building of CEC and determine the community development action plan for the officers in charge of community development work of the Department of Rural Development of the Capital and Provinces.
Minister Veng Sakhon Highlights Cambodia's Agricultural Potential to Hungarian Foreign Minister to Encourage Investors to Come to Cambodia
For this important meeting, he informed that Cambodia has three main sectors for Hungary to invest in the future: first: dairy production and meat processing, second: aquaculture, third: cultivation. And food safety; and fourth, water use and management. In particular, providing loans for agricultural development and short-term and long-term human resource training is also a priority in this visit.
In this regard, he informed that Hungary has provided scholarships to 15 Cambodian students to continue their studies every year, and the Hungarian government is considering increasing the number of scholarships next year, especially in the field of agriculture.
Welcoming remarks, Minister Veng Sakhon expressed his deep gratitude to Mr. Peter Szijjarto and his colleagues for their official visit to Cambodia and especially to the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries for bilateral talks. The friendship, solidarity and agricultural cooperation between the two countries will be further strengthened and deepened.
Taking this opportunity, the Minister informed the delegation about the potential of the Cambodian agricultural sector for development and policies of the Royal Government, agricultural development policies and plans of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries 2019-2023 and the investment climate. The current agricultural sector.
Mr. Veng Sakhon highlighted to the guests about the investment potential in the production of crops for export, such as rice, mango, cassava, cashew, tobacco and aquaculture production. In fact, in 2020, Cambodia exported 1,839 tons of Angkor to Hungary and 118 tons of tobacco.
Regarding the scholarship, Minister Veng Sakhon stated that this is a good opportunity for Cambodian students to continue their studies in Hungary to increase their capacity and experience in agriculture, which must bring the latest technology acquired from Hungary to the producers. Directly to participate in the development of Cambodia's agricultural sector in the future.
Please be informed that at 4:00 pm on November 3, at the Peace Palace, the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding between the Republic of Hungary and the Kingdom of Cambodia will be presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister.
For the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, there is a Memorandum of Understanding to be signed by Minister Veng Sakhon.
