This afternoon, Samdech Techo Hun Sen met with the Hungarian Foreign Minister and chaired the signing of three important agreements and memoranda.
(Phnom Penh): Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen will pay a courtesy call on Hungarian Minister of Foreign Affairs and Trade Peter Ziyato on the afternoon of November 3, 2020.
After paying a courtesy call and meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will also preside over the signing ceremony of three agreements and memoranda of understanding between Cambodia and Hungary. The agreement and memorandum to be signed include:
Although Cambodia and Hungary were old friends when Cambodia was in a difficult situation and had a long relationship, Cambodia and Hungary did not set up an embassy to represent their country.
In June 2019, during his visit to Hungary, Samdech Techo Hun Sen initiated talks to enhance relations and expand cooperation, as well as to establish embassies in each country.
Following Samdech Techo's visit, Haiti led to the visit of Hungarian President Janos Ader to Cambodia at the end of 2019 and the opening of the Hungarian Embassy in Cambodia on November 3, 2020.
Hungary became a member of NATO in 1999 and the European Union in 2004, as well as a member of the United Nations and the World Bank.
