(Battambang): A woman requested the intervention of the Ministry of Justice to help review and expedite the proceedings in the Battambang Provincial Court on the case of fraud between her ex-husband in a land dispute that has been unresolved for more than 5 years She suspected that it could be a match because the land at that time had a high odds.
She said that this was persuaded by her ex-husband to ask for her land to be mortgaged without interest to build a house. Because she was illiterate and did not understand the law, she followed him and got a mortgage, as well as relevant officials, lawyers followed her ex-husband, and later broke up with the provincial court. Entered a series of answers, but the other side refused to come to solve.
The woman recalled that while working as a waitress in a shop in Battambang City, a 68-year-old man named Khan, living in Lok Ta Sak 5 village, Sangkat Chrang Chamres, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh, came to ask for love and lived with her. They even had a daughter as a bond, while she did not know that her husband already had a wife.
She said that after a shortage of money to continue the construction of the house, she took her land title deed to HKL for a loan of $ 17,000, but later due to the high price of this land, the former Her husband tricked her into believing that she knew people in Phnom Penh for free and could borrow up to $ 100,000.
She finally found out that her plot of land with plot number 02030304-0383 had been mortgaged by her husband to Vin for $ 100,000, but in fact Vin did not give her what she said. That. She quickly found a lawyer and filed a lawsuit to prevent a conspiracy to sell her land.
