(Netherlands): A train in the Netherlands was rescued from a disaster on Monday when it hit a safety barrier but did not fall into the water due to a huge whale tail statue. This is according to the release by CNA on Tuesday morning, November 3, 2020.
The statue was built about 20 years ago in a park under the tracks. It had two large whale tails protruding from the water, and one of them saved the train.
The driver was arrested for questioning and the cause of the crash is under investigation. Experts, including sculptors, arrived at the scene to find a way to safely remove the train, but the main problem was that there was water around, so the crane could not get in and now the wind was blowing. Strong winds that have become an additional problem.
