Minister of Health: In the first 9 months of this year, Cambodia had a total of 7,668 cases of malaria, no deaths
(Kampong Speu): The Minister of Health, Professor Mam Bunheng, said that in the first nine months of 2020, there were a total of 7,668 cases of malaria nationwide and no deaths.
This statement was made by Professor Mam Bunheng on the occasion of the inauguration of the last phase of the eradication of malaria in the last phase of 2020-2023 in Cambodia, which took place at Kampong Speu Provincial Hall on November 3, 2020.
"According to the report of the National Center for Malaria Control of the National Center for Malaria Control, Parasitology and Bacteriology in the first nine months of 2020, the total number of malaria cases in the country in 2020 will be 7, 668 cases of illness and no death. "The number of cases in 2020 has continued to decrease by 70% compared to the same period in 2019, which was 25,499."
In order to achieve the complete eradication of malaria (or falciparum), it is necessary to implement the "Elimination of Malaria in the final stages of 2020-2023" in Cambodia, as organized. Now, starting the first operation in Kampong Speu and will expand to other provinces after evaluating the operation in the next three months.
General Chhum Socheat added that Cambodia ranks second behind Indonesia in the 10 ASEAN countries in terms of women's participation in UN peacekeeping operations.
"Since 2006, Cambodia has sent 7,123 peacekeepers, including 419 women, to participate in UN peacekeeping operations," said General Chhum Socheat. "In nine countries, especially in Africa, they are torn apart by war."
Currently, the Cambodian Blue Hat Force is carrying out UN peacekeeping missions in four countries: Lebanon, the Republic of South Sudan, Mali and Central Africa, with a total of 779 troops. Of those, 75 were women.
It should be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, stated that Cambodia will not withdraw its peacekeeping forces from the affected countries and Cambodia will maintain its position to send more. Samdech also highlighted that Cambodia is a poor country in ASEAN, but Cambodia has actively participated in international humanitarian activities through the Blue Hat Army.
