Woman found dead in rice field suspected of premeditated murder
(Banteay Meanchey): At 7:30 am on November 2, 2020, the body of a woman was found in the water of a rice field south of Phnom Top Bridge, called Reak Achm Bridge, 150 meters east of National Road No. 56A, about 10 meters north of the road in Kbal Spean village, Sangkat Makak, Serey Sophorn city, Banteay Meanchey province.
Later, Brigadier General Sithi Loh, Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner, led the Serious Crime Police Force, the Technical, Scientific Police Force and the Serei Sophorn City Police Force to conduct a thorough examination and forensic examination. On the body, there was a stab wound with a hard object, a sharp point of suffocation, a wound on the right side of the neck and several scratches on the surface.
Brigadier General Sithi Loh confirmed that the body was not identified, only that the woman was over 30 years old, wearing a red T-shirt, long sleeves, sports pants. Police at the scene found a pair of glasses and a sharp knife.
According to experts, it is a case of premeditated murder, but it is not yet known whether it is a case of robbery or a love triangle. At this time, the authorities are investigating the murderer who killed this woman brutally and bring her to justice according to the law.
At the same time, the police appealed to the missing family members or relatives who knew the victim, please provide information to the authorities as well.
Four Chinese arrested in connection with the explosion and violence at Borey Kuch Asia, Sihanoukville
(Preah Sihanouk): Four Chinese nationals were arrested by the Sihanoukville Provincial Police in connection with a case of armed explosion and intentional violence on October 29, 2020 at Borey Kuch Asia in Village 1, Sangkat 3 Sihanoukville. This is according to Major General Chuon Narin, Provincial Police Commissioner, told Fresh News on November 2, 2020.
After conducting detailed inquiries about the incident, the Criminal Police Planning Task Force conducted a thorough search to identify the suspects, with the direct coordination of Mr. Penh Piseth, Deputy Prosecutor of the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Prosecutor's Office. Sihanouk and with the cooperation of the Sihanoukville Police Inspectorate and the four administrative checkpoints, the police arrested a total of four suspects in a row.
This case happened because on the day of the incident, the victim went to demand money from the suspect and there was an argument that led to the use of violence. While fighting, the suspect, LI XIN, armed with a handgun, threatened to retaliate, and the victim returned to the scene, firing an assault rifle. The force is currently building a case to proceed with the proceedings.
