Spokesman for the General Commission: On November 2, another 523 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 186 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to November 92, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected And fined a total of 203,404 vehicles, including 150,393 motorcycles and 53,011 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 186 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
