Ms. Koy Pisey: Three out of nine provinces bordering Cambodia-Vietnam have completed the border demarcation
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Koy Pisey, Deputy Director of the Permanent Secretariat of the National Authority for Border Affairs, confirmed to Fresh News that so far, three Cambodian provinces have been completely demarcated. Among the nine provinces bordering Cambodia-Vietnam.
This confirmation was made at the same time as the National Assembly fully approved the draft law on the approval of the Khan Seima Protocol and the demarcation of the land border between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Socialist Republic of Vietnam in its plenary session on the morning of the 2nd. This November 2020.
Ms. Koy Pisey added that of the three provinces that completed the border demarcation, Kratie, Tbong Khmum and Prey Veng, while the remaining six provinces, the two governments are committed to complete in the future. .
Cambodia and Vietnam share a 1,270-kilometer land border, and so far the two governments have set up 84 percent of the border posts.
The border demarcation and land border protocol between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Socialist Republic of Vietnam was signed by the two governments on October 5, 2019 during Samdech Techo Hun Sen's two-day official visit to Vietnam. .
