In contrast to Trump, Joe Biden is seen as having more ways and opportunities to be elected president of the United States. The latest CNN poll shows that Biden will pre-book 203 voters from traditional or general states voting for the Democrats.
For almost a century, no Republican presidential candidate was elected president of the United States without a victory in Florida. So for Trump, too, he needs to win in Florida (with 29 delegates) to get 237 delegates.
According to opinion polls, Biden is ahead of Trump in North Carolina and Pennsylvania, while Trump is in Iowa. However, in 2016, Mr. Tram had already won once in all three states, especially Pennsylvania.
The presidential candidate must collect 26 or more votes. Of the 50 states in the United States, the Republican Party currently has the most delegates in 26 states, while the Democrats have the most delegates in 23 states. However, these are only predictions and what one might know for sure is the results on election day.
