(Banteay Meanchey): Caritas of Switzerland has donated food and some supplies to 1,800 flood-affected families from four communes in Mongkul Borei district, Banteay Meanchey province to share the hardships of the Royal Government and Help solve the difficulties in the lives of the victims.
Each family received 50 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 1 stick of fish sauce, 1 stick of soy sauce and canned fish. The distribution ceremony was presided over by Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, and was attended by Banteay Meanchey Provincial Governor Ou Rath, relevant officials and representatives of Caritas Switzerland.
On that occasion, Mr. Kham Si Nguon, Representative of Caritas Switzerland in Cambodia, praised and appreciated the Royal Government of Cambodia for its hard work to intervene to help people from the floods. Mr. Kham Si Nguon said that the donation was to share the hardships of the victims and to share the hardships of the Royal Government.
The representative of the Swiss organization Caritas said that in addition to the emergency relief, Ritas Swiss, through its partner CIDO, will continue to work with the authorities to improve agriculture after the floods, planting and raising livestock. In addition to the emergency assistance now, the organization will continue to help restore the agricultural sector and people's livelihood, and the organization not only operates in Banteay Meanchey, but in some other provinces.
Senior Minister Kun Kim praised and praised Caritas, which has always been involved with the Royal Government in supporting and helping Cambodian society to solve the difficulties of the people.
"Caritas Switzerland is very good," he said. "Work on the basis of humanitarian needs and respond to the needs of communities in need by coordinating with the National Committee for Disaster Management to identify areas for distribution and better cooperation."
On behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as well as the Royal Government of Cambodia, Senior Minister Kun Kim thanked Caritas for its humanitarian activities and called on the organization to continue such activities to help the victims.
During the distribution, Senior Minister Kun Kim also brought the visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to the people affected by the floods in Banteay Meanchey province and expressed their condolences. For the effects of flooding.
The Senior Minister also highlighted some of the interventions of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to help the affected people both during the flood and after the flood. The senior minister claimed that when the flood hit, Samdech Techo's necessary intervention was to rescue from the floods, find a safe place and provide food assistance.
When the water recedes, Samdech Techo's special intervention is to help restore the livelihood of the people by promoting rice farming, vegetable cultivation and animal husbandry. In Samdech Techo, both rice and other crop varieties were released to the people.
In addition to reminding Samdech Techo of the measures taken, Senior Minister Kun Kim also reminded the authorities in the provinces and localities affected by the flood to intervene and coordinate to help the people to grow crops again. Citizens are highly efficient. What does the "Blue Moon" phenomenon on the night of October 31 mean for the West?
