Cambodian Ministry of Health reacts to rumors that six Chinese have 19 cases of Kovid on their way out of Cambodia
A senior Cambodian health ministry official's reaction came after reports on social media and some media outlets that six Chinese nationals had been diagnosed with Kovid 19 after leaving Cambodia.
According to Ms. Yuk Sambath, the Chinese nationals have been thoroughly screened by the Ministry of Health to test for 19 cases of Kovid 19 on the bodies of the six Chinese nationals twice, the last time on October 24, 2020, with no positive Kovid 19 virus results.
She said that after receiving this information, the Ministry of Health of Cambodia also took the old samples of the six Chinese people to test again and the results are still negative. At the same time, the Ministry of Health of Cambodia also contacted the focal group of the Ministry of Health of China to help research and check again clearly.
She added that not only Chinese nationals, all passengers leaving Cambodia must be tested and have a negative result from the PCR laboratory. When the test is negative, a health certificate is issued, and all Chinese who go out are required to have the same health certificate.
