(Banteay Meanchey): Hundreds of Buddhists in Serei Sophorn and Poipet City have unanimously agreed to hold a solidarity march to collect suffixes for monks who have been waiting for a quarter of the rainy season and to build the Kiri Chum Chamkar pagoda. Knor is located in O'Ambel Village, Sangkat O'Ambel, Serey Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province on the evening of October 31, 2020 for the benefit of Buddhism.
Rev. Dr. Nop Men, Preah Chao Athikar, further stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia considers Buddhism as the state religion as stated in Article 43 of the Constitution, and that Cambodia has many Buddhist festivals, such as: Meak Bochea, Pisak Bochea Asal Worship and enter the rainy season, leave the rainy season, this charity festival and so on.
This Kathina Festival is a very important festival in the field of Buddhism. When Buddhists perform this Kathina Festival, they will become beautiful and wealthy, and become scholars and officials.
This Khmer Kathina Festival is held to meet the practical needs of the monks who remember the rainy season throughout the quarter at the pagodas, as well as to contribute to the construction of seats and achievements in the pagoda, as well as to enhance the observance of Buddhism. Which is the religion of the state to be glorious as well.
This Kathina festival is a festival in Buddhism, a special festival that has a definite time limit and can not be done at any time.
This training is to strengthen the capacity to provide health services to the base in Ratanakkiri and Mondulkiri 3 sessions for 3 days per session from 20 to 28 October 2020.
In addition, the project implementation team of Good Neighbors Cambodia (PMC) trained trainers of provincial and district health departments by inviting professors from the National Center for Maternal and Child Health from Phnom Penh, and all the faculty developed the curriculum. 5 days of training of trainers for local health service activities.
In particular, in order to prevent the shortage of medical staff in health centers, a variety of trainees from Mondulkiri Provincial Health Center staff received training in Ratanakkiri and Ratanakkiri Health Center staff to receive training in Mondulkiri.
Local health services are services that health center staff visit directly to the village, focusing on vaccinating children. Because the village is far from the health center, it is not possible to go to the health center to get vaccinated against children.
For the provision of health services to the local area, two health center staff were assigned to visit the designated villages every two months, but the health center staff could not provide adequate health services to the local area due to insufficient budget and staff shortage. Doctor.
In particular, Ratanakkiri and Mondulkiri provinces are geographically mountainous and there are many villages that cannot reach the health centers due to the floods and can not access the necessary medical services.
Therefore, from 2019 to 2023, KOICA will provide $ 7 million in grants from the Government of Korea to improve essential medical services, especially for pregnant women and children, for the people of Ratanakkiri and Mondulkiri, the most remote geographical area in the northeastern region of Cambodia.
In order to improve the provision of basic health services to people in disadvantaged areas, capacity building of health center staff is the most important part, so PMC has organized three training courses for health center staff.
During the training, Kong Kompheak, a trainee from Krang Teh Health Center in Mondulkiri province, said that for the first time since she started working at the health center, she had received training on providing basic health services.
Ratanakkiri Nhang Health Center official Chum Rathmony also said that this is the first time that the training was conducted jointly by the two provinces and it was a good opportunity to get education from the province. Ratanakkiri to Mondulkiri province. "Therefore, we can discuss between the staff of the provincial health center and prepare a joint action plan to prepare a new environment for the provision of health services to the local in Mondulkiri and Ratanakkiri."
