(Banteay Meanchey): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, highlighted the heroism of the leadership of Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen to flood victims in Banteay Meanchey province. The Senior Minister emphasized that as a habit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's leadership for more than 40 years, Samdech never ran away from the people in times of distress.
The presentation of the heroic example of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's leadership was made when Senior Minister Kun Kim handed over the gifts of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to 1,500 flood victims from Srah Chik commune, Ponley commune and Poi Char commune, Phnom Srok district, Banteay Meanchey province, on the afternoon of October 30, 2020.
The distribution ceremony was also attended by Mr. Ou Rathrey, Governor of Banteay Meanchey. On behalf of the affected people, the Provincial Governor expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who has always considered the well-being of the people affected by the floods by providing relief food and Visit the people in person.
In front of the victims, Senior Minister Kun Kim brought the greetings of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to the people affected by the floods in Banteay Meanchey province and expressed their condolences. Affected houses and crops.
The Senior Minister also highlighted the heroism of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's leadership. The Senior Minister stated that Samdech Techo Hun Sen is a leader who always puts the happiness and sorrow of the people first and always cares about the difficulties of the people.
Senior Minister Kun Kim stressed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen is a leader who is not accustomed to fleeing the people when they are suffering. He pointed out that, in fact, when the people suffered from the flood, Samdech Techo Hun Sen visited and provided food directly.
In addition, Samdech Techo also set out a number of urgent measures to restore people's livelihood after the flood.
The Senior Minister said that in order to restore the livelihood of the people, Samdech Techo released the budget to buy up to 2,000 tons of rice seeds and other crops to distribute to the people. Farmers receive about 100 kilograms of rice seeds per family, and growers receive six varieties of rice. Not only that, the Ministry of Agriculture has ordered agricultural machinery ready to help the people.
(Banteay Meanchey): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen has appointed Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Deputy Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, and Mr. Lim Kien Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, for urgent work to rehabilitate the “Ang Dam”. Ta Meng ”is located in Kork Kathin village, Kork Kathin commune, Thmor Puok district, Banteay Meanchey province, which was also affected by the floods.
This measure is to keep the water in "Ang Ta Meng" for farming and growing crops after the flood recedes. Minister Lim Kien Hor has appointed Chan Sinath, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, to lead the rehabilitation of the dam.
Residents of Kork Kathin commune said that "Ta Ta Meng" has been very beneficial for the people of Kork Kathin commune, not only as a source of water for farming and irrigating other crops. This "Ang Ta Meng" also provides a source of fish for people to find food. In addition, the back of the dam also provides a transportation system for people to travel.
The "Ang Ta Meng" dam has suffered some damage due to recent floods. After the water receded, many officials and machinery of the Ministry of Water Resources put in place to repair the back of the dam to facilitate the movement of people and hold water for irrigation.
The people of Kork Kathin commune expressed their happiness and gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, for setting out urgent measures to repair the dam to hold water and for their travel.
The people in Kork Kathin commune also thanked Senior Minister Kun Kim, who, as the staff of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, paid close attention to the well-being of the people and has been steadily since the floods began in Kork Kathin commune.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim emphasized to the people that the difficulties of the people are the difficulties of Samdech Techo. Because of this, Samdech Techo has issued strict orders to solve the difficulties of the people in this flood incident.
The Senior Minister continued that Samdech Techo's order has been consistently implemented by professional officials and is working diligently to respond to the requests and needs of the people.
On behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's staff on disaster management during the inspection of the dam, Senior Minister Kun Kim praised and thanked the Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology for taking urgent action to repair the dam. Ta Meng "as well as other dams damaged by floods.
Death news! Colonel Chhun Bunthy, Police Teacher at the Police Academy of Cambodia, Dies
(Phnom Penh): Colonel Chhun Bunthy, who worked at the National Police Academy of Cambodia for the Development Council of the National Police of Cambodia and a Exercise Teacher, passed away at 7:30 pm on October 30, 2020. Diseases.
Colonel Chhun Bunthy is a police instructor who is loved by many police students in recent years. Due to severe diabetes, in 2018, Colonel Chhun Bunthy amputated his right leg.
According to Colonel Chhun Bunthy's student, he was admitted to the hospital a few months ago when he needed regular blood transfusions or dialysis to prolong his condition, but unfortunately his condition worsened. He passed away on the night of October 30, 2020.
The disappearance of Colonel Chhun Bunthy is the loss of a pious father-in-law. The body of Colonel Chhun Bunthy is lost, but honor, merit, dignity, and heroism remain in the hearts of his sons, daughters, grandsons, granddaughters, and all his close relatives forever.
Monks, Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province, and Buddhists Start a Solidarity Charity Ceremony at Wat Thom Rattanasophea to Collect More Than 50 Million Riels
(Kampong Chhnang): Solidarity Kathina, initiated by the monks of Rolea Bier district, together with the people of the pagoda and the Buddhists near and far, marched to pay homage to the monks waiting for the end of the quarter in the Buddha Seima Wat Thom Rattanasophea in the commune. Sre Thmey, Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province, collected more than 50 million Riels.
Preah Serey Thom Vongsa Sengda, the chief abbot of Wat Thom Ratanasophea, said that the Kathin ceremony is a major festival in Buddhism. Because Cambodia is a Buddhist country, Cambodians everywhere celebrate this festival every year.
Preah Serey Thom Vongsa Sengda continued that in this ceremony, the monks, monks, monks of Rolea Bier district and the Buddhists at the foot of the pagoda always celebrate the Kathin ceremony at the temple near or far from the house. To give to the monks who have been waiting for the rain for a quarter.
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The United States will lift tariffs on certain Thai goods under the Generalized System of Preferences (GSP) on Friday, President Donald Trump announced Friday (Washington time). On December 30. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Saturday morning, October 31, 2020.
Donald Trump wrote in a letter to the US Congress, stating, "I see that Thailand does not guarantee the United States in bringing American goods into the Thai market in a reasonable and just manner." "Therefore, I think it is appropriate to suspend the preferential treatment under the GSP system on certain goods from Thailand in accordance with the provisions."
