Senior Minister Kun Kim: Water conservation efforts are important for post-flood cultivation
(Banteay Meanchey): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, said that efforts to hold water as well as conserve water are an important task to help people rehabilitate after the floods. The flood receded.
The senior minister said this during a visit to inspect the repair and rehabilitation of the "Ang Ta Meng" dam in Kork Kathin village, Kork Kathin commune, Thmor Puok district, Banteay Meanchey province, which was also affected by floods.
"Atameng" Dam is a large reservoir in Kork Kathin commune to supply rice and other crops. The dam has suffered some damage due to recent floods.
Pursuant to the order of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Minister of Water Resources, Mr. Lim Kien Hor, assigned Mr. Chan Sinath, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology to lead the rehabilitation of this dam to save water for the people.
On behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's staff on disaster management during the inspection of the dam, Senior Minister Kun Kim praised and thanked the Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology for taking urgent action to repair the dam. Ta Meng ”as well as other dams damaged by floods.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has put in place a special plan to restore farmers' livelihoods by helping to increase planting after the floods. To promote the cultivation of both rice and other crops, water conservation is essential. Because of this, the Prime Minister urged the Minister of Water Resources to respond urgently to repair dams and canals damaged by the floods.
The report of the National Committee for Disaster Management shows that the floods affected and damaged more than 700 kilometers of dams, main canals and secondary canals. Now, after the water recedes, the leaders and officials of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology have been working hard to repair the damaged dams and canals.
During the visit to Ang Ta Meng Dam, Senior Minister Kun Kim emphasized that maintaining water in canals is the most important task for farmers to rehabilitate after the water recedes. Back.
In this regard, Senior Minister Kun Kim called on the authorities and people of all provinces affected by the flood to take measures to conserve water at all water sources, whether dams, canals, ponds or ponds. All possibilities to store a lot of water.
The senior minister also asked local and provincial authorities to inspect water sources and find ways to store water for people to grow after the water recedes. Especially for their farming.
