(Pursat): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on October 30, 2020, met and brought 29.2 tons of rice seeds and some food items to 309 farmers in the district. Bakan, Pursat province affected by floods.
According to the director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, the effects of the floods have affected the production of rice, horticulture and agro-industrial crops in four localities, 34 communes, 295 villages and 18,758 families affected.
As of October 28, a total of 36,069 hectares of paddy fields were affected, including light paddy, early season rice, middle paddy, upland rice and heavy paddy, of which 20,412 hectares were damaged. . For mixed crops, the total affected area is 10,107 hectares, of which 2,514 hectares are damaged.
Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province, expressed his condolences and condolences for the loss of livestock and crops with the affected farmers throughout the province and especially in Bakan district. He will work hard to help restore food production, vital physical infrastructure to the people as soon as the water recedes.
On behalf of the local authorities, the provincial governor expressed his deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo Samdech Kittipritbandit and Minister Veng Sakhon for bringing rice seeds as a gift from Samdech Techo through the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Food. Eat and distribute directly to the people of Bakan district.
Receiving the order of Samdech Techo, the Minister and the Provincial Governor brought Samdech Techo's donation of rice seeds, catfish and some other food items to distribute to farmers to alleviate livelihood problems and restore food production. Not only that, the Minister brought the intervention team to plow, harrow and sow rice to help restore rice to farmers.
In connection with rice sowing machines, the Minister expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Techo for supporting 150 more rice sowing machines and 130 previous ones to help agricultural communities in the three target provinces: Banteay Meanchey, Battambang and Pursat provinces.
The plan for the future after the low tide, the Minister encouraged, supported and encouraged farmers to start rehabilitating crops in all forms, especially rice, as much as possible, and the Ministry will wait to intervene at any time as seeds, machinery, technology and Some other important agricultural inputs.
The Minister expressed his deep gratitude to the Cambodian Livestock Breeders Association for donating food worth $ 22,620. Charitable gestures are kind, help to share the well-being and spirit of good solidarity, and cooperate to support each other in all situations in difficult times.
Out of 309 families, 271 families received 100 kg of rice seeds per family and 38 families received 50 kg per family (depending on land size). In addition to the 309 rice varieties, each family received 25 kg of Angkor, 1 kg of sausage, 1 noodle, 1 can of soy sauce and 1 can of fish sauce.
On the same day, Mr. Veng Sakhon and his team also came to meet and bring catfish and some other farming materials to 55 families. Bakan, too.
