(Banteay Meanchey): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, on Friday, October 30, 2020, will continue to bring gifts from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to the people. Flooded 1,500 families in Phnom Srok district, Banteay Meanchey province.
The food distributed to the affected people to share the hardships of life during the flood included: rice, noodles, pure water, fish sauce, soy sauce, canned fish, mosquito nets, blankets, scarves and about 50,000 riels per family.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim conveyed the message of visit, remembrance and sharing of difficulties from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to all the victims. The Senior Minister said that Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit always remember and monitor the impact and suffering of people everywhere in this flood event.
The Senior Minister highlighted the highly responsible intervention of the victims by Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit.
He pointed out that during the floods caused by the rain, Samdech Techo, as the Commander-in-Chief of the flood battlefield, issued orders to the three types of armed forces, relevant authorities at the national, provincial and local levels. Urgent action must be taken to rescue the people, ensuring that "no one should die from drowning because they did not help or did not know."
The senior minister added that in addition to rescuing from the floods, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also took immediate action to address the lack of food and drinking water. Not only to distribute gifts directly in Phnom Penh and in Banteay Meanchey province, Samdech Techo managed to release pure food and water from the warehouse, along with donations from philanthropists to distribute to the people immediately without leaving any hungry people.
The Senior Minister emphasized to the victims that this is a highly responsible measure of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who is highly responsible for the fate of the nation and the people. Especially as the habit of Samdech Techo, every time the country and the people suffer, Samdech always shows up and is present to solve the problem, not the habit of running away from the problem.
The First Vice-Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's staff on disaster relief, said that the water level had begun to recede and that care should be taken to restore livelihoods. Re-cultivated by re-cultivating both rice and other mixed crops.
In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also ordered four ministers, including the Minister of Public Works and Transport, the Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, the Minister of Rural Development and the Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to work together to Rehabilitation of national roads, trails, dams, canals that have been damaged, find ways to store water for use, etc., while the Ministry of Agriculture has to distribute rice seeds and crops to the affected people.
In addition to reminding Samdech Techo of the measures taken, Senior Minister Kun Kim also reminded the authorities in the provinces and localities affected by the flood to intervene and coordinate to help the people to grow crops again. Citizens get high efficiency.
