(Kampong Chhnang): 20 May Reservoir, a large reservoir located in Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province, and this reservoir is also a bond of the Royal Government provided to farmers to bring water to irrigate the dry season rice production area. 2 who need to take water from this pool to irrigate the fields as necessary.
This reservoir is capable of irrigating both dry and wet rice up to thousands of hectares to farmers in two districts, Boribo and Rolea Bier. Not only that, the May 20 Reservoir is now also a beautiful natural tourist area where local and foreign tourists come to bathe here every weekend, especially on national holidays with tourists. From near and far come to visit here a lot too.
Communities that have used the 20 May water, along with farmers who are cultivating more than 1,000 hectares of dry rice on the 20 May dam, are worried about the subsequent loss of land from the 20 May dam. Seen some crooks were throwing water poles into the surface of the reservoir on May 20 to take possession of the land without seeing the ban from the relevant authorities yet.
The reservoir covers four communes: Melom commune in Baribo district, Svay Chrum commune, Banteay Preal commune and Prasnup commune in Rolea Bier district. Today, this reservoir, in addition to providing significant potential to the people's rice crops of more than 1,000 hectares in the dry season and more than 2,000 hectares in the rainy season, it also provides important fish for the people in Boribo district. Rolea Bier and Kampong Chhnang city as well.
More importantly, the May 20 Reservoir also has attractive tourism potential, as it has a large lake overlooking the area, a flooded forest for spawning fish, and a swimming pool every Saturday and Sunday. Sunday for local and foreign tourists to visit the scenery here is never broken.
They said that today, some crooks have come to set up posts to take the land in the pool without any action from the relevant authorities, especially the community using water on May 20 and farmers as community members of nearly 200 families. Is very concerned about this.
In this case, only the authorities can prevent the encroachment on the land of the reservoir on May 20, because the role of the authorities can summon all of them to make a contract, in case of violation, the authorities can build documents to send Court to take legal action. As for the land area of the pool on May 20, there is sub-decree No. 98, so those who claim to have a chicken wing license can not take it officially.
He added that on January 25, 2012, Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, on the occasion of inspecting the work of the 20 May Reservoir Dam, the Minister announced the construction of 20 May Reservoir Dam. Techo Sen II dry rice production area. The reservoir dam is capable of irrigating 2,292 hectares of wet paddy and 1,874 hectares of dry paddy.
