Speaking on the occasion of rice seed distribution, Mr. Mao Thunin said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit have been constantly monitoring the impact of the people due to the recent floods and warned the relevant ministries. In particular, the Provincial Disaster Management Committee brought rice seeds and distributed them immediately to the people for further cultivation.
He said that the water has destroyed our crops and infrastructure of our brothers, so we need to pay back the water by jointly conserving water in the main canals, sub-canals, ponds or rice fields to be able to rehabilitate for We use it in daily life and crop production in the coming dry season.
At the same time, he also empowered the people as well as the businessmen to use the land to the fullest to rehabilitate the natural waterways "lakes, canals, canals or rivers" to use the land or water for agriculture and livelihood. Live daily, avoid congestion or buy outside land to use.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's precious gift to 386 families for further cultivation, each family received 200 kg of fragrant rice seeds, 1 box of Aruna water, along with 1 sarong.
The people who received rice seeds would like to express their deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister and Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, who has always considered their well-being and assigned relevant officials to help solve everything. Their difficulties all the time. Spokesperson: The NEC must protect its professionalism and carry out its work in accordance with the Constitution
